ge space meaning they could have more data stored on their device without needing to buy new storage or server</p><p>2 - faster transfer speeds it means that a person who is going to transfer files from point a to point b would have a faster transfer speeds benefitting people who are working remotely and boosting productivity</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly identified two distinct reasons why an organisation would use compression software.</li><li>For each reason, you effectively explained the practical benefit to the organisation, linking the compression action to real-world advantages like saving money on storage.</li><li>Your explanations for faster transfer speeds also clearly showed the benefit to productivity, especially for remote work.</li><li>Your response is well-structured and directly answers the question, demonstrating a good understanding of the topic.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>You could enhance your explanations by briefly mentioning specific examples, such as reducing the size of email attachments or speeding up network backups, to show an even broader understanding of practical applications.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Organisations use compression software for two main reasons. Firstly, it reduces file sizes significantly, which saves valuable storage space on their servers and devices. This allows them to store more data without needing to purchase additional, potentially expensive, storage hardware, leading to cost savings. Secondly, compression facilitates faster data transfer speeds. Smaller files take less time to upload, download, or transmit across networks, improving efficiency for tasks like sharing files with remote workers or completing network backups more quickly, thereby boosting overall productivity.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-05 14:51:28',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1777991931846_yiolzia0g',7,'2026-05-05 14:51:20','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-05 14:51:28',NULL),(1903,159,1109,1,34,'<p>A full backup will backup everything saved on whatever you are backing up. This is good because it ensures that everything you have is backed up. An incremental backup only backs up everything since the last full backup. which is quicker and means that you aren\'t going to accidentally back up things that have already been backed up.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-05 14:52:58',202,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe the difference between a <strong>full backup</strong> and an <strong>incremental backup</strong>, and give one advantage of each.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>A full backup will backup everything saved on whatever you are backing up. This is good because it ensures that everything you have is backed up. An incremental backup only backs up everything since the last full backup. which is quicker and means that you aren\'t going to accidentally back up things that have already been backed up.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by correctly identifying that a full backup copies everything.</li><li>For a full backup, consider highlighting that its main advantage is how simple and fast it makes the restoration process.</li><li>Your description of an incremental backup could be more precise; it backs up changes since *any* last backup (full or incremental), not just the last full one.</li><li>You correctly noted that incremental backups are quicker, and they also significantly reduce the amount of storage space needed.</li><li>To make your answer even stronger, think about the impact of incremental backups on the complexity of restoring data.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>When describing incremental backups, be sure to mention that they copy data changed since *any* previous backup (full or incremental), and explain that restoring data from them requires the last full backup plus all subsequent incrementals.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A full backup copies every single file on the system, regardless of whether it has changed since the previous backup. An advantage of a full backup is that restoration is very simple and fast because all data is available in one complete backup set. An incremental backup only copies the data that has changed since the last backup, whether that was a full or another incremental backup. An advantage of incremental backups is that they are much faster to perform and require significantly less storage space. However, restoring from incremental backups is more complex as it requires the last full backup plus all subsequent incremental backups to be applied in the correct order.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-05 14:53:06',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1777992048452_9qkbbjkoa',1,'2026-05-05 14:52:58','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-05 14:53:06',NULL),(1904,159,1111,1,34,'<p>Cloud storage is good because it can be accessed remotely, which allows employees to work from home. Also, cloud storage is good because you can back it up easily, meaning that your data is at less of a risk of being lost.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-05 14:57:19',218,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain <strong>two</strong> benefits of using <strong>cloud storage</strong> rather than local storage for an organisation\'s data.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Cloud storage is good because it can be accessed remotely, which allows employees to work from home. Also, cloud storage is good because you can back it up easily, meaning that your data is at less of a risk of being lost.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that cloud storage enables remote access, which is a great point for organisations with staff working from home.</li><li>Your second point about data safety is good, but try to explain *how* cloud storage inherently reduces the risk of data loss.</li><li>Consider specific benefits like cloud providers offering redundancy across multiple locations or built-in disaster recovery features.</li><li>Remember to clearly explain each benefit in an organisational context to show its full impact.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>For your second benefit, explain more precisely *how* cloud storage protects data, perhaps by mentioning redundancy across multiple servers or robust disaster recovery.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Cloud storage offers two key benefits over local storage. Firstly, it provides enhanced accessibility, allowing employees to access data from any device with an internet connection, regardless of their physical location. This is crucial for staff working remotely or across multiple sites, improving flexibility and collaboration. Secondly, cloud storage significantly improves disaster recovery. Reputable cloud providers store data across multiple geographically separate servers, meaning if local hardware is destroyed or stolen, the organisation\'s critical data remains unaffected and readily available.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-05 14:57:27',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1777992048452_9qkbbjkoa',2,'2026-05-05 14:57:19','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-05 14:57:27',NULL),(1905,156,1137,1,34,'<p>reusing old equipment - they wont be in the landfill as it takes up space and costs fuel to go there</p><p>installing solar panels - it means that they get electricity to power the pc on the organisation which means sustainable energy which reduces environmental impact</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-05 14:59:11',172,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Give <strong>two</strong> examples of how an organisation can reduce the environmental impact of its use of information technology.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>reusing old equipment - they wont be in the landfill as it takes up space and costs fuel to go there</p><p>installing solar panels - it means that they get electricity to power the pc on the organisation which means sustainable energy which reduces environmental impact</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully identified two distinct ways an organisation can reduce its environmental impact.</li><li>Your explanation for reusing old equipment clearly links to reducing landfill waste and associated fuel consumption.</li><li>The idea of installing solar panels is a great example of using sustainable energy to power IT.</li><li>You clearly explained how both examples lead to a reduction in environmental impact.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>When giving examples, ensure you explicitly link them directly to the \"use of information technology\" to show how IT practices themselves can be made more environmentally friendly.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An organisation can reduce its environmental impact by implementing power management settings on all IT equipment, such as computers and monitors, to automatically sleep or shut down when not in use. This significantly reduces unnecessary electricity consumption. Secondly, they can establish a certified e-waste recycling program for old or broken IT hardware. This prevents hazardous materials from polluting landfills and allows valuable components to be recovered and reused.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-05 14:59:19',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1777992970760_twigofzpn',1,'2026-05-05 14:59:11','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-05 14:59:19',NULL),(1906,159,1139,1,34,'<p>Latency is the time it takes for an action to happen. Low latency is good because it means that your actions take very little time to happen. For example, sending an email with low latency will arrive quicker than if you sent it with high latency.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-05 15:01:34',132,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain what is meant by <strong>latency</strong> in computer networking and give one context in which low latency is particularly important.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Latency is the time it takes for an action to happen. Low latency is good because it means that your actions take very little time to happen. For example, sending an email with low latency will arrive quicker than if you sent it with high latency.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified latency as a time delay. To make your definition more precise for computer networking, specify that it\'s the delay in data transmission between network points.</li><li>You clearly stated that low latency is good. For a stronger answer, explain the specific negative consequences of high latency within your chosen context.</li><li>While low latency is beneficial for email, the mark scheme looks for a context where it\'s *particularly important*. Consider applications where even very small delays cause significant problems or failures, not just a slower experience.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly define latency as the time delay for data to travel from one point to another in a network.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Latency in computer networking is the time delay between sending a piece of data from one point in a network and it being received at its destination, typically measured in milliseconds. Low latency is particularly important in online gaming, as even small delays between a player\'s action and the game server\'s response can lead to a poor user experience, desynchronization, and a competitive disadvantage.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-05 15:01:42',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1777993154345_a8al4n9rw',1,'2026-05-05 15:01:34','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-05 15:01:42',NULL),(1907,156,1132,1,34,'<p>i think an organisation should use backup software because if there is a power outage they can regain data saved before the power outage</p><p>another reason for backup software is because if hackers are stealing your data and then destroy the entire network you have backups recovered which could be used to restore data before the hackers stole the data</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-05 15:06:49',204,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain <strong>two</strong> reasons why an organisation should use backup software.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>i think an organisation should use backup software because if there is a power outage they can regain data saved before the power outage</p><p>another reason for backup software is because if hackers are stealing your data and then destroy the entire network you have backups recovered which could be used to restore data before the hackers stole the data</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully identified that backup software is crucial for recovering data after a cyberattack, showing a good understanding of that risk.</li><li>For your first reason, clarify how a power outage directly causes data loss that backup software addresses, focusing on saved file corruption rather than unsaved work.</li><li>Great job explaining how backups specifically mitigate the threat of hackers destroying a network by allowing restoration from an earlier, clean state.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>When giving a reason, clearly explain the specific type of data loss or corruption that can occur and how backup software directly solves that particular problem.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An organisation should use backup software for two main reasons. Firstly, it protects against hardware failure, such as a hard drive crashing unexpectedly. Regular backups ensure that if a drive fails, a recent copy of all data can be restored, preventing permanent loss. Secondly, backup software is essential for recovery from cyberattacks like ransomware. If data is encrypted or deleted, a clean backup allows the organisation to restore its systems and data without paying a ransom, significantly reducing downtime and financial impact.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-05 15:06:58',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1777993368931_d3xidvf5f',1,'2026-05-05 15:06:49','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-05 15:06:58',NULL),(1908,159,1068,1,34,'<p>RAM is used for the processes the computer is currently doing. The RAM is volatile (all data stored is lost when the device loses power) which means that it is good for holding the data on what you are currently doing. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-05 15:06:54',151,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe the function of <strong>RAM (Random Access Memory)</strong> in a computer system.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>RAM is used for the processes the computer is currently doing. The RAM is volatile (all data stored is lost when the device loses power) which means that it is good for holding the data on what you are currently doing. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that RAM stores data for current processes and is volatile, meaning data is lost when power is removed. That\'s a great start!</li><li>To improve, explain that programs and files are loaded into RAM *from secondary storage* when they are opened for active use.</li><li>Consider adding why RAM is preferred for active data, specifically mentioning its speed compared to secondary storage.</li><li>Think about how the amount of RAM installed influences the computer\'s overall performance and its ability to multitask.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Explain that RAM is used because it is much faster than secondary storage for the CPU to access the data it\'s actively processing.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>RAM is a type of volatile (temporary) memory that holds the data and instructions the CPU is currently processing. When a program or file is opened, it is loaded from slower secondary storage into RAM, allowing the CPU to access it quickly. All contents of RAM are lost when the computer is switched off. The amount of RAM directly affects how many programs can run simultaneously and the overall smoothness of the computer\'s operation.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-05 15:07:01',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1777993458525_lq0uwy1x9',1,'2026-05-05 15:06:54','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-05 15:07:01',NULL),(1909,159,1095,1,34,'<p>HTTP stands for Hypertext Transfer Protocol, and HTTPS stands for Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure. As the name suggests, HTTPS is more secure than HTTP, meaning that it is better for personal data because it is built to protect the users data while on the site.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-05 15:12:46',326,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe the purpose of <strong>HTTP</strong> and <strong>HTTPS</strong> and explain why HTTPS is preferred for websites that handle personal data.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>HTTP stands for Hypertext Transfer Protocol, and HTTPS stands for Hypertext Transfer Protocol Secure. As the name suggests, HTTPS is more secure than HTTP, meaning that it is better for personal data because it is built to protect the users data while on the site.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified the full names for both HTTP and HTTPS, showing a good foundational understanding.</li><li>To improve, explain what HTTP does with data and explicitly mention that it is unencrypted, making it vulnerable.</li><li>Expand on how HTTPS achieves its security, specifically by using encryption to protect data.</li><li>Consider detailing why HTTPS is crucial for personal data, perhaps mentioning specific types of sensitive information and data protection compliance.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly explain the core difference in how each protocol handles data security, focusing on the presence or absence of encryption.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>HTTP (Hypertext Transfer Protocol) is used to transfer web pages and data between a server and a browser. Data transferred via HTTP is unencrypted and can be intercepted and read during transmission. HTTPS (HTTP Secure) adds a layer of encryption, typically using TLS (Transport Layer Security), to secure this data. All information exchanged between the browser and server over HTTPS is encrypted, meaning it cannot be read even if intercepted. HTTPS is preferred for websites handling personal data, such as payment details or login credentials, because it protects user privacy, prevents sensitive information from being accessed by unauthorized parties, and helps websites comply with data protection legislation.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-05 15:12:53',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1777993458525_lq0uwy1x9',1,'2026-05-05 15:12:46','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-05 15:12:53',NULL),(1910,62,189,1,7,'<p>Equality legalisaltion affects software design by ensuring inclusivity and accessibility in software, this means that there accessible features for those who need it. For example arrangements for people with poor sight like enlarged text or written descriptions. While inclusivity includes ensuring no group of people is discriminated or unable to use the software.</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-05 20:55:47',272,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how equality legislation affects software design. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Equality legalisaltion affects software design by ensuring inclusivity and accessibility in software, this means that there accessible features for those who need it. For example arrangements for people with poor sight like enlarged text or written descriptions. While inclusivity includes ensuring no group of people is discriminated or unable to use the software.</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained how equality legislation promotes accessibility in software design, providing a great example of features for users with poor sight.</li><li>You effectively highlighted the importance of preventing discrimination in software usage for all groups, which is a key aspect of inclusive design.</li><li>To strengthen your answer further, consider explicitly naming specific legislation, such as the Equality Act, to show a deeper understanding of the legal framework.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly reference the specific legislation that mandates these requirements, such as the Equality Act 2010, to demonstrate a more precise understanding of the legal framework.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Equality legislation, such as the Equality Act, significantly affects software design by mandating inclusivity and accessibility. This ensures that software is usable by all individuals, preventing discrimination based on characteristics like age or disability. Designers must implement features such as adjustable text sizes, keyboard navigation, and alternative text descriptions to ensure inclusive interfaces for everyone.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-05 20:55:55',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778014265321_wwp4eck87',1,'2026-05-05 20:55:47','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-05 20:55:55',NULL),(1911,164,1117,1,34,'<p>For age you could do a range check to ensure they dont input an impassable number. For email you could use a format check. For the number of tickets you can once again use a range check to ensure the number of tickets booked is between 1 and 10</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-06 08:21:45',206,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>A cinema website requires customers to enter their age, email address, and the number of tickets they want to purchase (maximum 10 tickets per booking).</p><p>Describe a suitable validation check for <strong>each</strong> of these three input fields.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>For age you could do a range check to ensure they dont input an impassable number. For email you could use a format check. For the number of tickets you can once again use a range check to ensure the number of tickets booked is between 1 and 10</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified a range check for the number of tickets and precisely specified the range (1 to 10), which is excellent!</li><li>For the age field, you identified a range check; to enhance your answer, specify a realistic age range (e.g., between 0 and 120).</li><li>You suggested a format check for the email address. To score full marks, explain *what* the format check looks for, such as the presence of an \'@\' symbol and a domain.</li><li>For both age and number of tickets, consider also adding a type check to ensure whole numbers are entered.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4>When describing validation checks, always explain in detail *what specific conditions* the check is enforcing or looking for.<h4>Model Answer</h4><p><strong>Age:</strong> A range check to ensure the value is a realistic age (e.g., between 0 and 120). A type check to confirm it is a positive whole number rather than text or a decimal.</p><p><strong>Email address:</strong> A format check to ensure the input follows a standard email pattern, containing an \'@\' symbol and a domain name. A presence check to ensure the field is not left blank.</p><p><strong>Number of tickets:</strong> A range check to ensure the value is between 1 and 10, as specified by the maximum per booking. A type check to ensure it is a positive whole number.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-06 08:21:54',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778055490178_1hncgo4ro',1,'2026-05-06 08:21:45','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-06 08:21:54',NULL),(1912,155,1084,1,34,'<p>GUI</p><ul><li><p>easy to use</p></li><li><p>quick, saves time</p></li></ul><p></p><p>CLI</p><ul><li><p>may be more precise than gui in terms of usage</p></li><li><p>uses way less ram, which in result can be put towards other programs</p></li></ul>',NULL,'2026-05-06 08:31:30',308,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Give <strong>two</strong> advantages of a <strong>graphical user interface (GUI)</strong> over a <strong>command-line interface (CLI)</strong>.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>GUI</p><ul><li><p>easy to use</p></li><li><p>quick, saves time</p></li></ul><p></p><p>CLI</p><ul><li><p>may be more precise than gui in terms of usage</p></li><li><p>uses way less ram, which in result can be put towards other programs</p></li></ul><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully identified two potential advantages of a GUI, \"easy to use\" and \"quick, saves time.\"</li><li>To achieve full marks, remember to explain *why* these are advantages compared to a CLI. Think about what makes a GUI easier or quicker for a user.</li><li>The mark scheme looks for explanations of *how* these advantages benefit the user, rather than just stating them.</li><li>Your points about CLI, while interesting, were not asked for in the question, which specifically focused on GUI advantages.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, briefly explain *why* each advantage you identify is beneficial, specifically in contrast to a command-line interface.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A GUI is easier to use because it presents visual icons, windows, and menus, making tasks intuitive without requiring users to memorise complex commands. This reduces the amount of training needed, as users can often figure out tasks from visual cues. Multitasking is also simpler as multiple applications can be open in separate windows and switched between easily.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-06 08:31:38',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778056047785_jfv91j7qk',1,'2026-05-06 08:31:30','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-05-07 14:17:29',1),(1913,156,1096,1,34,'<p>the purpose of tge tcp/ip protocol layer in computer networking is to split data packets so that it could travel faster and securely to its destination.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-06 10:03:07',495,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the purpose of the <strong>TCP/IP</strong> protocol suite in computer networking.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>the purpose of tge tcp/ip protocol layer in computer networking is to split data packets so that it could travel faster and securely to its destination.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You mentioned that TCP/IP helps split data packets, which is a good start as TCP does break data into smaller segments. To improve, clearly distinguish the specific roles of TCP and IP within the protocol suite.</li><li>The response does not fully explain IP\'s role in addressing and routing data across networks. Next time, remember to include how IP ensures packets reach the correct destination.</li><li>Your answer touches on data transport but doesn\'t detail TCP\'s crucial role in ensuring reliable, ordered delivery, including retransmission of lost data. Consider explaining how TCP guarantees all data arrives correctly.</li><li>While efficiency is a goal, TCP/IP\'s primary purpose is reliable communication across networks, not specifically to make data \"travel faster and securely\" on its own. Focus on the core functions like addressing and reliable delivery.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly separate and explain the distinct functions of TCP (Transmission Control Protocol) and IP (Internet Protocol) within the TCP/IP suite, as they each have unique responsibilities.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The TCP/IP protocol suite is fundamental to computer networking and the internet. IP (Internet Protocol) is responsible for addressing and routing data packets, ensuring they are sent from the source to the correct destination device across different networks using unique IP addresses. TCP (Transmission Control Protocol) handles the reliable, ordered delivery of data; it breaks data into segments, numbers them, manages the connection, and ensures all segments arrive correctly, requesting retransmission if any are lost or corrupted. Together, TCP/IP provides a robust foundation for communication between devices.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-06 10:03:13',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778061279607_ro7e8vcgd',1,'2026-05-06 10:03:07','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-06 10:03:13',NULL),(1914,156,1096,1,34,'<p>the purpose of tcp/ip protocol is to establish secure connection between two computers.</p><p>the ip internet protocol is used to identify the devices</p><p>the tcp transport control protocol is the one that delivers the data by splitting the data packets to send to the destination pc. if the packets are lost or corrupted it then requests to send the data back so they can deliver it to the destintaion pc</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-06 10:09:07',173,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the purpose of the <strong>TCP/IP</strong> protocol suite in computer networking.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>the purpose of tcp/ip protocol is to establish secure connection between two computers.</p><p>the ip internet protocol is used to identify the devices</p><p>the tcp transport control protocol is the one that delivers the data by splitting the data packets to send to the destination pc. if the packets are lost or corrupted it then requests to send the data back so they can deliver it to the destintaion pc</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that IP is used to identify devices. To enhance this, remember to also explain its role in *routing* data packets across networks.</li><li>Your explanation of TCP\'s role in breaking data and handling retransmissions is good. Consider adding that TCP also ensures data is delivered in the *correct order* and manages the *connection setup* (handshake).</li><li>Think about the primary purpose of TCP/IP as the fundamental suite for *communication* across the entire internet, rather than primarily for \"secure connections.\"</li><li>To achieve a strong answer, clearly explain how TCP and IP work *together* to achieve reliable and ordered data transfer.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Deepen your explanation of TCP\'s role by including its management of ordered data delivery and the connection handshake process.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The TCP/IP protocol suite is the foundational set of protocols for the internet, enabling devices to communicate across networks. IP (Internet Protocol) is responsible for addressing and routing data packets, ensuring they are forwarded from a source to the correct destination across potentially multiple networks using unique IP addresses. TCP (Transmission Control Protocol) provides reliable, ordered, and error-checked delivery of data. It breaks data into numbered packets, sends them, and ensures all packets arrive correctly by requesting retransmission of any lost or corrupted ones. TCP also manages the connection between devices through a handshake process. Together, they facilitate robust and reliable communication across global networks.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-06 10:09:15',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778061279607_ro7e8vcgd',2,'2026-05-06 10:09:07','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-06 10:09:15',NULL),(1915,155,1114,1,34,'<p>RAID can protect against data loss as it stores a copy of data on a different disk so if one disk fails, the data is still intact.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-06 10:13:27',67,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe the purpose of a <strong>RAID (Redundant Array of Independent Disks)</strong> system and explain <strong>one</strong> way it can protect against data loss.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>RAID can protect against data loss as it stores a copy of data on a different disk so if one disk fails, the data is still intact.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that RAID protects data by storing copies on different disks, which is a key aspect of its function. To make your answer even stronger, consider elaborating on the primary purpose of RAID, which is to combine multiple hard drives into a single logical unit.</li><li>You clearly explained how data protection works by storing copies on another disk in case of a failure. Next time, try to name the specific RAID level you are describing (e.g., RAID 1 for mirroring) and detail how the system can continue operating without interruption.</li><li>For a more complete answer, you could also briefly mention that RAID is not a substitute for regular backups, as it primarily protects against hardware failure rather than accidental deletion.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly describe the overall purpose of a RAID system and then choose one specific RAID level (e.g., RAID 1 or RAID 5) to explain its protection mechanism in more detail.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A RAID (Redundant Array of Independent Disks) system combines multiple hard drives into a single logical unit to improve performance, provide data redundancy, or both. It protects against data loss by distributing or duplicating data across these drives. For example, in RAID 1 (mirroring), data is written identically to two or more drives simultaneously. If one drive fails, a complete copy exists on the other drive(s), allowing the system to continue operating without data loss, and the failed drive can be replaced and rebuilt without downtime. It\'s important to remember that RAID protects against hardware failure but is not a substitute for backups against accidental data deletion.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-06 10:13:54',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778056047785_jfv91j7qk',1,'2026-05-06 10:13:27','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>I think you should explain RAID0 through to RAID6</p>','A','2026-05-07 14:16:23',1),(1916,165,1143,1,34,'<p>A network protocol is a standardised set of rules which define how devices communicate and exchange data, they are necessary as they need to establish a common language and set of rules which then enable diverse hardware and software from different manufacturers.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-06 10:20:58',6905,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe what is meant by a <strong>network protocol</strong> and explain why protocols are necessary in computer networks.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>A network protocol is a standardised set of rules which define how devices communicate and exchange data, they are necessary as they need to establish a common language and set of rules which then enable diverse hardware and software from different manufacturers.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve provided a clear and accurate definition of a network protocol, correctly identifying it as a standardised set of rules for communication. Great start!</li><li>Your explanation of why protocols are necessary is also excellent; you correctly highlight their role in enabling diverse hardware and software to communicate effectively.</li><li>To make your answer even stronger, consider adding specific examples of what these rules govern, such as how data is broken into packets or how errors are handled.</li><li>Including an example of a specific protocol like TCP/IP or HTTP would also demonstrate a deeper understanding of their practical application.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on the specific functions protocols define (e.g., packet addressing, error correction) and include a named example of a network protocol.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A network protocol is a set of agreed rules and standards that govern how data is formatted, transmitted, received, and interpreted between devices on a network. Protocols are necessary because networks connect devices from many different manufacturers running diverse operating systems and software. Without these agreed standards, devices would have no common language or method to communicate successfully. Protocols define critical aspects such as how data is broken into packets, how these packets are addressed and routed, how errors are detected and corrected, and the precise format of messages exchanged, like TCP/IP or HTTP.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-06 10:21:05',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778055947303_m0tgp0qx6',1,'2026-05-06 10:20:58','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Examples?</p>','A','2026-05-07 14:16:55',1),(1917,156,1096,1,34,'<p>tcp/ip layer is the foundational set of protocols for the internet because it enables devices to communicate across networks</p><p>ip - it address and routes data packets so that it can get from source to the corerect destination  by assigning them with unique ip addresses</p><p>tcp - transmission control protocol provides reliable delivery of data by breaking data into numbered packets before sending it. it ensures all packets arrive correctly plus if a packet is corrupt or lost it requests a retransmission of that packet.</p><p>when put together it creates a robust and reliable communication across global networks</p>',NULL,'2026-05-06 10:24:25',439,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the purpose of the <strong>TCP/IP</strong> protocol suite in computer networking.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>tcp/ip layer is the foundational set of protocols for the internet because it enables devices to communicate across networks</p><p>ip - it address and routes data packets so that it can get from source to the corerect destination  by assigning them with unique ip addresses</p><p>tcp - transmission control protocol provides reliable delivery of data by breaking data into numbered packets before sending it. it ensures all packets arrive correctly plus if a packet is corrupt or lost it requests a retransmission of that packet.</p><p>when put together it creates a robust and reliable communication across global networks</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by identifying TCP/IP as the foundational set of protocols for internet communication and correctly separating IP and TCP for explanation.</li><li>Your explanation of IP is strong, accurately describing its role in addressing and routing data packets to their destinations using unique IP addresses.</li><li>For TCP, you correctly covered reliable delivery, breaking data into numbered packets, and retransmission of lost or corrupt packets, which shows a good understanding.</li><li>To make your answer even more comprehensive, consider adding how TCP also manages the establishment and termination of connections between devices, often through a \'handshake\' process.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, briefly include how TCP manages connection establishment and termination, for example, through a \'handshake\' process, to fully describe its functionality.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>TCP/IP is the foundational suite of protocols for the internet, enabling devices to communicate across various networks. IP (Internet Protocol) is responsible for addressing and routing data packets, ensuring they are forwarded from the source to the correct destination across multiple networks using unique IP addresses. TCP (Transmission Control Protocol) provides reliable, ordered data delivery; it breaks data into numbered packets, sends them, ensures all arrive correctly, and requests retransmission of any lost or corrupted packets. TCP also manages the connection between devices through a handshake process. Together, they form the core communication mechanism of the internet.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-06 10:24:37',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778062614079_e0hteuxxp',3,'2026-05-06 10:24:25','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-06 10:24:37',NULL),(1918,59,1063,1,33,'<p>Firstly, with a start-up company the company most likely has limited resources and a limited budget. This makes IaaS seem the most useful as it is the cheapest cloud computing model when compared to PaaS and SaaS. However, this only slightly affects the problem as they want the most money efficient cloud computing model and just because IaaS is the cheapest option it doesn\'t mean that it is the most cost effective cloud computing model.</p><p>IaaS also provides the most control over the digital environment by making virtual infrastructure that the company controls. This might mean they have to hire someone to manage the virtual infrastructure to make sure it is working efficiently and how it should be working. This adds some extra costs into the decision as PaaS and SaaS would not need a specialist to be hired so that cloud delivery models to perform securely.</p><p></p><p>PaaS provides the highest developer speed and deployment meaning they can make more applications in quicker succession with a PaaS which would most likely bring more funding and attention to LaunchPad Digital for future projects and products. Using an IaaS or a SaaS wouldnt provide the same efficiency that a PaaS would.</p><p></p><p>SaaS gives a more predictable subscription cost, requires the least management and is the easiest to adopt. These highlight how an SaaS would be more beneficial than any other cloud deployment model.</p><p></p><p>In conclusion, LaunchPad Digital needs a cloud delivery model suited to its goals and aims and I believe an IaaS would be the best one when considering LaunchPad Digital\'s needs. They will need to hire a specialist for the IaaS however I believe this extra cost will benefit the company. The IaaS allows for full control over the environment. This allows it to scale rapidly to suit the predicted amount of users the application will have in the future.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-06 19:26:59',1088,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>LaunchPad Digital is a start-up company with five developers that has created a new project management web application. The application is ready for public launch and the team anticipates rapid user growth — potentially from a few hundred users at launch to tens of thousands within six months if marketing goes well. They have no existing physical IT infrastructure. </p><p>The team is debating which cloud service model to adopt. One developer wants to use an IaaS provider to have full control of the environment. Another prefers a PaaS solution to reduce infrastructure management overhead and allow the team to focus on application development. A third has suggested using a SaaS-based development platform instead. </p><p><strong>Key constraints</strong>: small team with no dedicated infrastructure staff, unpredictable growth, limited budget, application must scale rapidly, team is developer-focused not ops-focused. </p><p><em>Evaluate the cloud delivery models available to LaunchPad Digital, comparing the suitability of IaaS, PaaS and SaaS options for their circumstances and recommending the most appropriate approach.</em></p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Firstly, with a start-up company the company most likely has limited resources and a limited budget. This makes IaaS seem the most useful as it is the cheapest cloud computing model when compared to PaaS and SaaS. However, this only slightly affects the problem as they want the most money efficient cloud computing model and just because IaaS is the cheapest option it doesn\'t mean that it is the most cost effective cloud computing model.</p><p>IaaS also provides the most control over the digital environment by making virtual infrastructure that the company controls. This might mean they have to hire someone to manage the virtual infrastructure to make sure it is working efficiently and how it should be working. This adds some extra costs into the decision as PaaS and SaaS would not need a specialist to be hired so that cloud delivery models to perform securely.</p><p></p><p>PaaS provides the highest developer speed and deployment meaning they can make more applications in quicker succession with a PaaS which would most likely bring more funding and attention to LaunchPad Digital for future projects and products. Using an IaaS or a SaaS wouldnt provide the same efficiency that a PaaS would.</p><p></p><p>SaaS gives a more predictable subscription cost, requires the least management and is the easiest to adopt. These highlight how an SaaS would be more beneficial than any other cloud deployment model.</p><p></p><p>In conclusion, LaunchPad Digital needs a cloud delivery model suited to its goals and aims and I believe an IaaS would be the best one when considering LaunchPad Digital\'s needs. They will need to hire a specialist for the IaaS however I believe this extra cost will benefit the company. The IaaS allows for full control over the environment. This allows it to scale rapidly to suit the predicted amount of users the application will have in the future.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You have discussed all three cloud models (IaaS, PaaS, SaaS) and considered aspects like cost, control, and management, which is a great start.</li><li>It\'s important to remember LaunchPad Digital is *building* their own application. SaaS refers to ready-to-use software; they cannot use a SaaS provider to host their unique product, though SaaS tools could support their development.</li><li>When evaluating IaaS, you correctly identified the need for a specialist. However, the scenario specifically states \"no dedicated infrastructure staff\" and \"developer-focused not ops-focused,\" which makes hiring an ops specialist a significant contradiction to their constraints.</li><li>Your response could benefit from a more direct comparison of how each model addresses \"unpredictable rapid growth.\" PaaS often features automatic scaling, which is a major advantage for this constraint compared to the manual scaling required with IaaS.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly differentiate between using a SaaS *product* (like Google Workspace or Jira) to support LaunchPad Digital\'s internal work, and choosing a cloud model (IaaS or PaaS) to *host* the new application LaunchPad Digital is developing.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>LaunchPad Digital needs a cloud solution that supports rapid, unpredictable growth with a small, developer-focused team and a limited budget. Evaluating IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS against these constraints helps determine the best fit.</p><p><strong>IaaS (Infrastructure as a Service):</strong> This model, like AWS EC2 or Azure VMs, provides virtual hardware. While it offers maximum control and customisation, it places the burden of managing operating systems, patching, scaling, and load balancing on the user. For LaunchPad\'s five-person team with no dedicated infrastructure staff, IaaS would introduce significant operational overhead. This would distract developers from their core task of application development, directly contradicting their \"developer-focused not ops-focused\" constraint and adding unexpected costs for an infrastructure specialist. While IaaS can scale, it requires manual configuration, making it less suitable for unpredictable rapid growth.</p><p><strong>PaaS (Platform as a Service):</strong> Solutions like Heroku, Google App Engine, or Azure App Service provide a managed environment where developers simply deploy their code, and the platform handles the underlying infrastructure, scaling, and maintenance. This aligns perfectly with LaunchPad\'s constraints: it requires no infrastructure staff, allows the developer team to focus solely on the application, and inherently supports \"unpredictable rapid growth\" through auto-scaling. The \"limited budget\" is also addressed as PaaS typically has a pay-as-you-go model, scaling costs with usage, without significant upfront investment or the need to hire additional ops staff. While it offers less control than IaaS and has potential for vendor lock-in, the benefits for LaunchPad outweigh these disadvantages.</p><p><strong>SaaS (Software as a Service):</strong> This model delivers complete, ready-to-use applications over the internet (e.g., Salesforce, Google Docs). LaunchPad Digital is *building* a SaaS product; they cannot use a SaaS provider to host their own custom-developed application. While SaaS tools (like GitHub for code management or Jira for project tracking) can be used to *support* their development workflow, SaaS itself is not a hosting solution for their unique application.</p><p><strong>Recommendation:</strong> PaaS is the most appropriate approach for LaunchPad Digital. It directly addresses their \"small team with no dedicated infrastructure staff\" by abstracting infrastructure management, allows the \"developer-focused\" team to concentrate on their application, and handles \"unpredictable rapid growth\" and \"rapid scaling\" through automated mechanisms. Its pay-as-you-go model also suits a \"limited budget\" start-up.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-06 19:27:15',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778094524797_37xu0jj5z',1,'2026-05-06 19:26:59','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-06 19:27:15',NULL),(1919,59,106,1,7,'<p>Consistent naming conventions improve collaboration in a team project as different developers will understand the names given to variables and constants easily if they all mutually understand the naming conventions with the shared knowledge. This is beneficial as it reduces unnecessary communication between the developers and makes the whole project more time efficient</p>',NULL,'2026-05-06 19:30:12',80,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain why consistent naming conventions improve collaboration in a team project. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Consistent naming conventions improve collaboration in a team project as different developers will understand the names given to variables and constants easily if they all mutually understand the naming conventions with the shared knowledge. This is beneficial as it reduces unnecessary communication between the developers and makes the whole project more time efficient</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained how consistent naming conventions help developers understand each other\'s work, which is excellent for reducing confusion and unnecessary communication. This is a strong start!</li><li>To enhance your answer, consider how these conventions make tracking changes and managing different versions of code much easier in tools like Git. Think about \'version control\'.</li><li>It would also be beneficial to mention how clear naming can significantly speed up the process of finding and fixing errors when things go wrong. This is known as \'debugging\'.</li><li>For a higher-level response, you could include specific examples of naming conventions, such as `camelCase` or `snake_case`, to illustrate your points.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, broaden your explanation to include the technical benefits, such as how consistent naming directly aids in debugging code and makes version control systems more effective for tracking changes.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Consistent naming conventions significantly improve collaboration by reducing confusion among team members, making it easier for everyone to understand the purpose of variables, functions, and files without constant communication. This clarity also streamlines the process of debugging by making errors simpler to locate and fix. Furthermore, it helps maintain cleaner version control history, as changes are more clearly defined and tracked. Adopting specific conventions like `camelCase` or `snake_case` ensures a unified and efficient approach across the project.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-06 19:30:21',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778094524797_37xu0jj5z',1,'2026-05-06 19:30:12','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-06 19:30:21',NULL),(1920,156,1091,1,34,'<p>a router in a computer network is to connect the computers into a network through the router so they can use the internet</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 08:14:15',264,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the role of a <strong>router</strong> in a computer network.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>a router in a computer network is to connect the computers into a network through the router so they can use the internet</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>Your answer touches on the idea that a router helps computers use the internet, which is a good starting point. To make it stronger, consider explaining that routers connect *different* networks together, like your home network to the internet.</li><li>You mentioned connecting computers into \"a network,\" but it\'s important to distinguish the router\'s role from a switch. Next time, try to explain that a router specifically directs traffic *between* different networks, not just within one.</li><li>To improve your explanation, think about *how* a router directs data. Consider mentioning that it looks at destination addresses (like IP addresses) on data packets to decide where to send them next.</li><li>Adding details about data packets and IP addresses will help show a deeper understanding of the router\'s specific function.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, clearly explain that a router connects *different* networks (e.g., a LAN to the internet) and describe its specific job of *routing* data packets between these networks using their destination IP addresses.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A router connects two or more different computer networks, such as a local area network (LAN) to the internet (a wide area network). Its primary role is to direct (route) data packets between these networks. It does this by reading the destination IP address of each packet and using a routing table to determine the most efficient path to forward the packet to its intended destination.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-07 08:14:23',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1778141387071_iegoiiqgr',1,'2026-05-07 08:14:15','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Not just the internet...</p>','R','2026-05-07 14:25:49',1),(1921,156,1091,1,34,'<p>a router is two or more networks like a LAN that connects devices by routing them through different ip addresses to give them internet</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 08:16:28',60,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the role of a <strong>router</strong> in a computer network.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>a router is two or more networks like a LAN that connects devices by routing them through different ip addresses to give them internet</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that a router is involved with \"two or more networks\" and \"IP addresses.\" Next time, clarify that a router\'s primary role is to *connect* these different networks, such as your home LAN to the internet.</li><li>Your answer mentions \"routing them,\" which is good, but it would be more precise to explain that a router directs *data packets* between these networks.</li><li>To improve your explanation, specify that the router reads the destination IP address in each packet to determine the best path for it to travel.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly explain that a router connects *different* networks (like a LAN and a WAN/Internet) and forwards *data packets* between them using IP addresses.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A router connects two or more different computer networks together, for example, a local area network (LAN) to the internet (a wide area network, WAN). Its main role is to direct (route) data packets between these networks. It does this by reading the destination IP address in each packet and determining the most efficient path to forward it, using routing tables to make these decisions.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-07 08:16:34',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778141387071_iegoiiqgr',2,'2026-05-07 08:16:28','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-07 08:16:34',NULL),(1922,156,1091,1,34,'<p>a router connects two or more networks like a LAN to the internet. it does this by identifying their ip addresses and routes data packets into a more efficent way to the destination</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 08:19:15',134,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the role of a <strong>router</strong> in a computer network.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>a router connects two or more networks like a LAN to the internet. it does this by identifying their ip addresses and routes data packets into a more efficent way to the destination</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that a router connects two or more different networks, such as a LAN to the internet. To enhance this, consider explicitly stating that this distinguishes it from a switch or hub.</li><li>You mentioned that routers identify IP addresses and route data packets efficiently, which is a great start. Next time, try to explain *how* it finds the \"most efficient way\" by mentioning routing tables.</li><li>To achieve a more comprehensive answer, you could also include other common functions of a router, such as Network Address Translation (NAT).</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on how a router determines the \"most efficient way\" to route packets by explaining its use of routing tables to find the best path.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A router\'s primary role is to connect two or more different networks, such as a local area network (LAN) to a wider network like the internet (WAN). It directs data packets between these distinct networks by examining the destination IP address in each packet. Routers use routing tables to determine the most efficient path to forward packets, ensuring they reach their correct destination. They also commonly provide Network Address Translation (NAT), allowing multiple devices on a private network to share a single public IP address, differentiating them from switches which only operate within a single network.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 08:19:24',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778141387071_iegoiiqgr',3,'2026-05-07 08:19:15','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-07 08:19:24',NULL),(1923,156,1091,1,34,'<p>the router connects two or more devices from a Local Area Network into the internet (WAN) it achieves this by identifying their ip addresses and using routing tables to efficently go to their intended destination</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 08:21:53',118,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the role of a <strong>router</strong> in a computer network.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>the router connects two or more devices from a Local Area Network into the internet (WAN) it achieves this by identifying their ip addresses and using routing tables to efficently go to their intended destination</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that a router connects a Local Area Network (LAN) to the internet (WAN), which is a key function.</li><li>You accurately mentioned the use of IP addresses and routing tables in directing traffic, showing a good understanding of how decisions are made.</li><li>To fully explain the process, specify that a router reads the destination IP address in <strong>data packets</strong> to determine the most efficient path.</li><li>Next time, consider adding details about other functions like Network Address Translation (NAT) or how a router distinguishes itself from a switch.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly explain that a router examines the destination IP address of each <strong>data packet</strong> to determine the <strong>best path</strong> for forwarding it between networks.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A router connects two or more different networks, most commonly a Local Area Network (LAN) to a Wide Area Network (WAN) like the internet. Its primary role is to direct (route) data packets between these networks. It does this by reading the destination IP address in each data packet, consulting its routing tables to determine the best path, and then forwarding the packet to its next hop. Routers also commonly provide Network Address Translation (NAT), allowing multiple devices on a private LAN to share a single public IP address.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 08:22:02',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778141387071_iegoiiqgr',4,'2026-05-07 08:21:53','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-07 08:22:02',NULL),(1924,156,1091,1,34,'<p>a router connects two or more networks like a lan to a wan. it does this by reading data packets from ip addresses before using routing tables to help them efficiently lead them towards their destination. routers also use a nat which helps multiple devices connect from a private lan</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 08:25:25',111,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the role of a <strong>router</strong> in a computer network.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>a router connects two or more networks like a lan to a wan. it does this by reading data packets from ip addresses before using routing tables to help them efficiently lead them towards their destination. routers also use a nat which helps multiple devices connect from a private lan</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that a router connects different networks, like a LAN to a WAN, which is a crucial role.</li><li>You explained that routers read data packets and use routing tables. For more precision, specify that they read the <strong>destination</strong> IP address to determine the best path.</li><li>It\'s great that you included NAT and its function in allowing multiple private devices to share a single public IP.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>To enhance your answer, clearly explain that routers <strong>route</strong> or <strong>forward</strong> data packets by looking at their <strong>destination IP address</strong> and using the routing table to find the optimal path.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A router\'s primary role is to connect two or more different networks, such as a local area network (LAN) to a wide area network (WAN) like the internet. It works by inspecting the destination IP address of incoming data packets, then consulting its routing table to determine the most efficient path to forward (route) the packet to its destination network. Routers also commonly provide Network Address Translation (NAT), which allows multiple devices on a private LAN to share a single public IP address when accessing the internet.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 08:25:38',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778142169247_c73ebj93g',5,'2026-05-07 08:25:25','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Five attempts now. Suggest you go back and actually read your notes before attempting another answer.</p>','A','2026-05-07 14:41:41',1),(1925,156,1105,1,34,'<p>a phishing attack is when someone sends an email pretending to be a legitimate company in order to steal someones credidentials.</p><p>two ways an organisation can deal with this is to have spam block so that they block spam emails or ignoring the email because emails that have spelling mistakes usually indicate its a phishing scam</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 08:50:21',716,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain what is meant by a <strong>phishing</strong> attack and describe <strong>two</strong> ways an organisation can protect against it.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>a phishing attack is when someone sends an email pretending to be a legitimate company in order to steal someones credidentials.</p><p>two ways an organisation can deal with this is to have spam block so that they block spam emails or ignoring the email because emails that have spelling mistakes usually indicate its a phishing scam</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>Your definition of a phishing attack correctly identifies the key elements of fraudulent emails and credential theft. To strengthen your explanation, consider including that it\'s a social engineering attack aiming for sensitive information or malware installation.</li><li>You correctly identified spam blocking (email filtering) as a very effective protective measure. Well done!</li><li>For the second protection, focus on how the *organisation* equips staff, for example, through \'staff training and awareness\' to recognise indicators like spelling mistakes. This empowers employees to make the right choices.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Ensure your protective measures are described from the organisation\'s perspective, like \'staff training and awareness\', rather than just a user\'s action.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A phishing attack is a social engineering technique where an attacker sends fraudulent communications, often emails appearing from a trusted source, to trick recipients into revealing sensitive information like passwords or clicking malicious links that install malware. It exploits human psychology rather than technical vulnerabilities. Two ways an organisation can protect against phishing are through staff training and awareness, which educates employees to recognise suspicious emails and report them, making the workforce a strong defence. Secondly, email filtering systems can automatically detect and quarantine suspected phishing emails before they even reach users\' inboxes, reducing their exposure to such threats.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 08:50:30',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778142447261_9eifzoplr',1,'2026-05-07 08:50:21','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Training is definitely the most important here.</p>','A','2026-05-07 14:13:29',1),(1926,59,98,1,7,'<p>Selection is implemented in Python using if/else statements. This allows for users to select between options in the program to end up with a specific wanted output</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 08:53:33',91,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain with an example how selection is implemented in Python. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Selection is implemented in Python using if/else statements. This allows for users to select between options in the program to end up with a specific wanted output</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that selection in Python uses `if/else` statements, which is a great start!</li><li>To fully answer the question, it\'s important to include a practical code example to demonstrate how selection is implemented.</li><li>For handling multiple conditions, remember to also include the `elif` (else if) statement in your explanation.</li><li>Consider briefly discussing the role of Boolean conditions and the importance of indentation in Python for defining code blocks.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Provide a clear, simple code example that uses `if`, `elif`, and `else` to illustrate how selection works in Python.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Selection in Python allows different blocks of code to be executed based on whether a condition is true or false. It is primarily implemented using `if`, `elif` (else if), and `else` statements.</p><p>For example:</p><pre><code>age = 17<br><br>if age &gt;= 18:<br>    print(\"You are an adult.\")<br>elif age &gt;= 13:<br>    print(\"You are a teenager.\")<br>else:<br>    print(\"You are a child.\")<br></code></pre><p>Conditions are evaluated as Boolean (True/False), and indentation is crucial for defining which lines of code belong to each `if`, `elif`, or `else` block.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-07 08:53:40',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1778143902922_rb5rwj0g8',1,'2026-05-07 08:53:33','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','R','2026-05-07 14:12:50',1),(1927,156,1087,1,34,'<p>a feature for a lan is that it covers a small geographical area which is like a small office</p><p>it is owned by the organisation</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 09:08:44',925,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain <strong>two</strong> features of a local area network (LAN).</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>a feature for a lan is that it covers a small geographical area which is like a small office</p><p>it is owned by the organisation</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that a LAN covers a small geographical area, such as a small office, which is a great start!</li><li>You also correctly identified that a LAN is owned by the organisation, showing you understand a key characteristic.</li><li>To fully explain your points, try to add a little more detail about what each feature means or enables for the network.</li><li>Consider elaborating on *why* covering a small area or being owned by an organisation is a significant feature of a LAN.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, for each feature you identify, aim to provide a brief explanation of its implications or what makes it significant, rather than just stating the feature.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Two features of a local area network (LAN) are:</p><p>1.  **Covers a small geographical area:** A LAN typically connects devices within a limited space, such as a single building, floor, or campus. This keeps cable runs short and data transfer speeds high.</p><p>2.  **Owned and managed by the organisation:** Unlike a Wide Area Network (WAN), the infrastructure of a LAN is typically installed, owned, and maintained by the organisation or individual using it, giving them full control over its setup and security.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 09:08:50',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778142447261_9eifzoplr',1,'2026-05-07 09:08:44','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-05-07 14:11:47',1),(1928,84,228,1,12,'<p>The importance of backup strategies for business continuity is that for example, being able to save data that otherwise would\'ve been lost or corrupted, incase of a data breach or power outage, you can access the data that otherwise would be unaccessible. Another reason that backup strategies are important is that they allow for better data protection and accessibility.</p><p>Automatic backups could also help from preventing people forgetting to backup data, this could be extremely important as incase a very important file was just finished, and not saved / backed up it would be in vein and a huge waste of time / effort.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:11:26',285,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the importance of backup strategies for business continuity. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The importance of backup strategies for business continuity is that for example, being able to save data that otherwise would\'ve been lost or corrupted, incase of a data breach or power outage, you can access the data that otherwise would be unaccessible. Another reason that backup strategies are important is that they allow for better data protection and accessibility.</p><p>Automatic backups could also help from preventing people forgetting to backup data, this could be extremely important as incase a very important file was just finished, and not saved / backed up it would be in vein and a huge waste of time / effort.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained how backup strategies prevent data loss and ensure data accessibility after events like data breaches or power outages. Well done, this directly addresses a key aspect of the mark scheme!</li><li>Your point about automatic backups preventing human error and wasted effort is insightful and shows good practical understanding. It adds a valuable dimension to your response.</li><li>To achieve a stronger response, consider discussing different types of backup strategies, such as offsite or cloud-based solutions. These are crucial for protecting against physical disasters affecting your primary location.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, remember to include specific examples of <em>where</em> backups can be stored, such as offsite locations or cloud services, to enhance resilience and fully meet the mark scheme criteria.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Backup strategies are essential for business continuity as they prevent data loss and facilitate quick recovery after various failures, including hardware malfunctions, cyber-attacks, or natural disasters. Regular backups ensure that critical information remains available, significantly reducing downtime and protecting a business from reputational and financial damage. Utilising offsite or cloud-based backup solutions is particularly important to safeguard data against localized disasters, ensuring business operations can resume swiftly.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:11:33',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778162787216_wzlce8cws',1,'2026-05-07 14:11:26','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-05-07 14:12:10',1),(1929,84,213,1,12,'<p>One purpose of encryption is to keep data hidden/personal. This is done by using encryption which is the process of hiding data by using a key, a type of encryption could be changing the letters to symbols and characters which can only be changed back if you\'ve got the key.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:13:20',68,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State one purpose of encryption. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>One purpose of encryption is to keep data hidden/personal. This is done by using encryption which is the process of hiding data by using a key, a type of encryption could be changing the letters to symbols and characters which can only be changed back if you\'ve got the key.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that encryption helps keep data hidden and personal, which is a great start to describing confidentiality.</li><li>You clearly explained that a key is necessary to revert the encryption, showing you understand how it makes data unreadable without authorisation.</li><li>Your example of changing letters to symbols provides a good illustration of the concept.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>To use more formal T-Level/BTEC terminology, try to use the specific term \'data confidentiality\' to describe the purpose of keeping data hidden and personal.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>One purpose of encryption is to protect data confidentiality by making it unreadable to unauthorised users without a decryption key.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:13:26',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1778162787216_wzlce8cws',1,'2026-05-07 14:13:20','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Good</p>','G','2026-05-07 14:15:25',1),(1930,76,22,1,7,'<p>Emerging technologies such as IoT and AI are changing software development in many ways. Help I need a model answer</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:13:46',149,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how emerging technologies such as AI and IoT are changing software development. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Emerging technologies such as IoT and AI are changing software development in many ways. Help I need a model answer</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified the key technologies mentioned in the question, which is a good start.</li><li>To gain marks, you need to explain *how* AI is changing software development, perhaps by linking it to automation or predictive capabilities.</li><li>Similarly, explain specific ways IoT impacts development, such as through data collection from sensors or enabling remote control features.</li><li>Think about discussing the specific benefits or challenges these technologies introduce for software developers.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Provide specific examples of how AI and IoT are changing software development, rather than just stating that they are.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>AI is transforming software development by automating tasks like testing and code analysis, and by enabling the creation of intelligent, predictive features within applications. IoT influences development through the need for robust systems to handle real-time data collection from numerous devices and to manage remote control capabilities, leading to more distributed and complex architectures. These changes offer benefits like increased efficiency and innovative product development, but also introduce challenges concerning data privacy, security, and the need for developers to adapt their skills for real-time, scalable, and data-intensive systems.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:13:53',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1778162838487_na8eexm8r',1,'2026-05-07 14:13:46','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Now have a proper go...</p>','R','2026-05-07 14:15:03',1),(1931,80,90,1,7,'<p>privacy concerns can arise from increase in use of digital systems because it opens vulnerabilities to be exploited to listen in on users.</p><p>aswell as this  it means that more systems could be in place to track people that they may not realise.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:15:48',483,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how privacy concerns arise from increased use of digital systems. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>privacy concerns can arise from increase in use of digital systems because it opens vulnerabilities to be exploited to listen in on users.</p><p>aswell as this it means that more systems could be in place to track people that they may not realise.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that digital systems can lead to increased tracking and monitoring of users, which is a good starting point for discussing surveillance.</li><li>To develop your answer further, explain how the widespread *collection of personal data* itself is a primary privacy concern.</li><li>Consider the concept of a \"digital footprint\" – the trail of data left by online activity – and how this contributes to privacy issues.</li><li>For higher marks, discuss the importance of user *consent* for data collection and the *potential misuse* of this information, possibly linking to relevant legislation.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to incorporate specific terminology like \'data collection\' and \'digital footprints\' to explain how digital systems accumulate information about individuals, and explore the implications of this.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Increased use of digital systems leads to significant privacy concerns primarily through extensive data collection and increased surveillance. Every online interaction contributes to a digital footprint, revealing personal habits and information. Concerns arise from users often not giving explicit consent for this data collection, and the significant risk of misuse of personal information by companies or malicious actors. Legislation like GDPR aims to address these issues by giving individuals more control over their data.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:15:55',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1778162845591_nmrmqgt6q',1,'2026-05-07 14:15:48','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>I\'d probably give this 1 mark in an exam.</p>','R','2026-05-07 14:23:01',1),(1932,83,91,1,7,'<p>Generative AI tools may put a large strain on the already doomed job market. Employers will choose cheaper AI tools over human employees. This will also result in these products being of a much lower quality, but a much lower cost to produce. Another problem, is the fact that photographic evidence will be much harder to believe, leading to both false imprisonment and criminals denying crimes they committed. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:16:30',221,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the societal effects of generative AI tools. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Generative AI tools may put a large strain on the already doomed job market. Employers will choose cheaper AI tools over human employees. This will also result in these products being of a much lower quality, but a much lower cost to produce. Another problem, is the fact that photographic evidence will be much harder to believe, leading to both false imprisonment and criminals denying crimes they committed. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You did a great job identifying key drawbacks of generative AI, such as job displacement and the challenge of verifying photographic evidence, which is a good start for an evaluation. To strengthen your answer, try to expand on other potential drawbacks like algorithmic bias or the spread of fake news.</li><li>To provide a more balanced evaluation, remember to include the significant benefits that generative AI tools can bring to society. Think about how they might enhance creativity, improve productivity, or increase accessibility for various tasks.</li><li>For higher marks, consider the responsibilities of software developers in managing the ethical and legal implications of these powerful tools. Thinking about their role in creating responsible AI can add depth to your analysis.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Provide a balanced evaluation by discussing both the positive societal effects (benefits) and the negative societal effects (drawbacks) of generative AI tools.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Generative AI tools present a mixed bag of societal effects. Positively, they can significantly boost productivity across various industries by automating repetitive tasks and generating creative content, making design and content creation more accessible. They also open new avenues for artistic expression and scientific discovery. However, these tools also pose significant challenges. Job displacement is a major concern as AI can perform roles previously held by humans. There\'s also a high risk of spreading misinformation and deepfakes, eroding trust in digital content. Furthermore, generative AI can perpetuate and amplify existing biases present in its training data, leading to unfair or discriminatory outcomes. Software developers therefore have a crucial role in managing these ethical and legal implications, by implementing transparent design principles, developing robust content authentication methods, and adhering to strict ethical guidelines to mitigate potential harms.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:16:38',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1778163113114_2e3uxx0er',1,'2026-05-07 14:16:30','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Need a much longer, more thorough answer for a 6 marker, probably twice as long as you did.</p><p>For these questions, be prepared to expand upon your points: speak of Generative AI, LLMs and the limitations of these models. Evaluate the positive and the negative before drawing any conclusions. </p><p>Most importantly, remember who actually develops LLMs - it is developers, and the creativity and ingenuity of a developer will always create a better solution than an AI.</p>','R','2026-05-07 14:21:54',1),(1933,84,248,1,12,'<p>One negative impact of using emerging technologies such as IoT could be that all the devices can be hacked quite easily, this is really bad due to the fact that these devices can include smart cameras, speakers, health trackers or those home robot things (basically like an Alexa??) which can be hacked if secured with weak passwords or security features. Another negative impact of using these emerging technologies such as IoT is that they hold large amounts of data, which can be sensitive for example location or health records. If this is not secured properly it can be accessed by people who shouldn\'t have the authorisation. </p><p>However, the IoT can also improve security if used and secured properly, for example by using encryption or strong passwords, regular updates can also be used to secure the devices and the data. </p><p>To conclude, the emerging technologies such as IoT can have major implications for data security because it increases connectivity and data sharing. Also it canraise risks such as being hacked, privacy concerns or unauthorised access.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:25:35',600,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss the implications of emerging technologies like IoT for data security. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>One negative impact of using emerging technologies such as IoT could be that all the devices can be hacked quite easily, this is really bad due to the fact that these devices can include smart cameras, speakers, health trackers or those home robot things (basically like an Alexa??) which can be hacked if secured with weak passwords or security features. Another negative impact of using these emerging technologies such as IoT is that they hold large amounts of data, which can be sensitive for example location or health records. If this is not secured properly it can be accessed by people who shouldn\'t have the authorisation. </p><p>However, the IoT can also improve security if used and secured properly, for example by using encryption or strong passwords, regular updates can also be used to secure the devices and the data. </p><p>To conclude, the emerging technologies such as IoT can have major implications for data security because it increases connectivity and data sharing. Also it canraise risks such as being hacked, privacy concerns or unauthorised access.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You effectively highlighted that IoT devices can be \"hacked quite easily,\" which clearly implies an increased attack surface. Great job in identifying this key implication for data security!</li><li>You clearly discussed the risks to data privacy by mentioning sensitive information like location and health records. This demonstrates a strong understanding of how IoT impacts data confidentiality.</li><li>It\'s excellent that you included encryption as a method to improve security within IoT. This shows you\'re thinking about both the challenges and potential solutions.</li><li>You also mentioned important aspects of secure device management, such as using strong passwords and regular updates. This shows a good awareness of best practices for securing IoT ecosystems.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>When discussing devices being \"hacked quite easily,\" try to explicitly use the term \"increased attack surface.\" This makes your answer more precise and demonstrates a deeper technical understanding of the security implications. </p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Emerging technologies like IoT significantly broaden the data security landscape. A primary implication is the expansion of the attack surface, as a vast number of interconnected devices, often with diverse operating systems and potentially weaker default security settings, provide more entry points for cyber threats. This increases the risk of unauthorised access and data breaches across an entire network.<br><br>Furthermore, IoT devices collect and process large volumes of sensitive personal and operational data, such as health metrics, location information, and behavioural patterns. This raises significant data privacy concerns, as improper handling or storage can lead to severe consequences if this data is compromised or misused.<br><br>However, these risks can be mitigated through robust security measures. Implementing strong encryption protocols is crucial for protecting data in transit and at rest. Additionally, secure device management practices, including regular software updates, strong authentication mechanisms, and network segmentation, are essential to reduce vulnerabilities and maintain data integrity and confidentiality across the IoT ecosystem.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:25:44',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1778162787216_wzlce8cws',1,'2026-05-07 14:25:35','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>\"Those home robot things\" - Smart Assistants</p>','G','2026-05-07 14:27:08',1),(1934,80,201,1,7,'<p>It is important to use secure coding practises when handling user data as not handling data responsibly could lead to user\'s being put in dangerous positions as well as leading to possible fines under GDPR.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:26:30',588,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss the importance of secure coding practices for protecting user data. (8 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>It is important to use secure coding practises when handling user data as not handling data responsibly could lead to user\'s being put in dangerous positions as well as leading to possible fines under GDPR.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made an excellent start by identifying the critical link between secure coding and legal implications like GDPR fines, which is a key part of an excellent answer!</li><li>To strengthen your response, consider explaining what some of these \"secure coding practices\" actually are. Think about specific techniques used.</li><li>Discuss how these particular practices directly prevent exploits and keep user data safe from dangerous situations.</li><li>Adding examples of practices like input validation or encryption would help demonstrate your understanding and earn more marks.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on specific secure coding practices, such as input validation or encryption, and explain how they contribute to protecting user data from vulnerabilities.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Secure coding practices are vital for protecting user data by implementing preventative measures against common vulnerabilities. Input validation ensures only expected data formats are accepted, preventing injection attacks. Encryption protects data both in transit and at rest, rendering it unreadable if accessed without authorisation. Robust error handling prevents sensitive system information from being exposed, which attackers could exploit. Adopting these practices is not only crucial for safeguarding user privacy and preventing exploits but also for adhering to data protection laws like GDPR, avoiding severe fines and reputational damage.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:26:37',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778162845591_nmrmqgt6q',1,'2026-05-07 14:26:30','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Form validation, defensive error trapping, exception handling, encryption, obfuscation...</p>','A','2026-05-07 14:30:49',1),(1935,83,113,1,7,'<p>These laws and guidelines ensure that customers are protected, and have rights over their own data. For example, a website must have options to reject cookies, and users must always be informed about how their data is used, and what data is gathered. Terms and conditions are not bulletproof however, as users always have certain rights over their own data. For example, a company could not put a line like \"You agree that you will give us 70% of your income for the rest of your life\" into the terms and conditions (that they know nobody is going to read) as this violates the rights of the user.</p><p>Software developers also have certain rights that their employers must give them. For example, they must be given frequent screen breaks to prevent eye strain as well as free eye tests, adjustable peripherals and chairs, and training to ensure they are using equipment correctly. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:29:37',689,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss how multiple laws and guidelines (Data Protection, Computer Misuse, Equality, Health & Safety) together shape responsible software practice. (8 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>These laws and guidelines ensure that customers are protected, and have rights over their own data. For example, a website must have options to reject cookies, and users must always be informed about how their data is used, and what data is gathered. Terms and conditions are not bulletproof however, as users always have certain rights over their own data. For example, a company could not put a line like \"You agree that you will give us 70% of your income for the rest of your life\" into the terms and conditions (that they know nobody is going to read) as this violates the rights of the user.</p><p>Software developers also have certain rights that their employers must give them. For example, they must be given frequent screen breaks to prevent eye strain as well as free eye tests, adjustable peripherals and chairs, and training to ensure they are using equipment correctly. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made good points about Data Protection and Health & Safety, showing how they protect users and developers respectively. To strengthen your answer, make sure to explicitly include Computer Misuse and Equality laws in your discussion.</li><li>Consider how these laws ensure *secure* digital systems, beyond just user data rights. For example, think about how the Computer Misuse Act directly prevents hacking and unauthorized access, which is crucial for system security.</li><li>To achieve a higher mark, explicitly link compliance with these laws to benefits like building user trust and enhancing a company\'s reputation. Discuss how following these guidelines makes users feel safer and more valued.</li><li>Think about how upholding these laws contributes to sustainable professional behaviour within the software industry. Explain how ethical and legal compliance creates a better, more responsible working environment for everyone.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, make sure to address all four specified laws and then explicitly connect adherence to them with broader impacts like company reputation, user trust, and sustainable professional practices.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Multiple laws and guidelines collectively establish a framework for responsible software practice. Data Protection laws, like GDPR, ensure secure and fair handling of personal data, giving users rights over their information. This builds user trust and protects a company\'s reputation. The Computer Misuse Act prevents unauthorized access, hacking, and data manipulation, ensuring the security and integrity of digital systems and services, which is vital for maintaining public confidence. Equality laws require software to be accessible and non-discriminatory, promoting fair and inclusive design that serves all users, broadening reach and demonstrating ethical practice. Finally, Health & Safety legislation ensures a safe working environment for software developers, covering aspects like ergonomic equipment and reasonable working hours. Compliance with these laws fosters a professional, ethical, and sustainable software industry, where secure, fair, and safe digital systems lead to stronger user trust and a positive industry reputation.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:29:49',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778163113114_2e3uxx0er',1,'2026-05-07 14:29:37','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-05-07 14:31:37',1),(1936,80,87,1,7,'<p>One benefit of using loops for iteration is that loops are simple to repeat parts of code until a condition is met this means that it will save time. However this could open the possibility for the code to last forever if the end condition is not implemented correctly and it could also mean that the code could crash in certain languages if the code is not allocated time to run manually.</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:31:29',275,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Analyse the benefits and drawbacks of using loops for iteration. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>One benefit of using loops for iteration is that loops are simple to repeat parts of code until a condition is met this means that it will save time. However this could open the possibility for the code to last forever if the end condition is not implemented correctly and it could also mean that the code could crash in certain languages if the code is not allocated time to run manually.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully identified that loops are great for repeating code and saving time, which is a key benefit for automation.</li><li>You clearly highlighted the risk of infinite loops if the exit condition isn\'t handled correctly, a crucial drawback to consider.</li><li>Consider explaining how logic errors within a loop, rather than just \'crashing\' due to time allocation, can lead to unexpected program behaviour or failures.</li><li>To enhance your answer, try to include specific examples of loop types, such as Python\'s <code>for</code> or <code>while</code> loops, to demonstrate your practical understanding.</li><li>Adding details about loop control mechanisms like <code>break</code> or <code>continue</code> would further strengthen your analysis of iteration.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, be sure to reference specific types of loops, like Python\'s <code>for</code> and <code>while</code> loops, and discuss how they are controlled.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Loops offer significant benefits for iteration by automating repetitive tasks, which greatly reduces code redundancy and makes programs more concise and efficient. For example, Python\'s <code>for</code> loop is excellent for iterating over collections, while a <code>while</code> loop continues as long as a condition is true. However, drawbacks include the risk of creating infinite loops if the termination condition is not properly implemented, and the potential for subtle logic errors that can be difficult to debug, leading to unexpected program behaviour or crashes. Effective use of loop control mechanisms like <code>break</code> and <code>continue</code> is vital for managing iteration correctly.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:31:37',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778162845591_nmrmqgt6q',1,'2026-05-07 14:31:29','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-05-07 14:37:45',1),(1937,76,75,1,7,'<p>Abstraction is a part of computational thinking where you take away uneccessary details from a problem leaving only the required information to understand it.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:32:00',56,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>What is meant by abstraction in computational thinking?. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Abstraction is a part of computational thinking where you take away uneccessary details from a problem leaving only the required information to understand it.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve clearly explained that abstraction involves removing unnecessary details from a problem. Well done!</li><li>You successfully identified that the goal is to leave only the required information.</li><li>To make your answer even more comprehensive, consider explicitly stating the ultimate benefit of this process.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state that the purpose of removing details is to simplify complex problems.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Abstraction means removing unnecessary details from a problem to focus only on the relevant information, which helps to simplify complex problems.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:32:04',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1778162838487_na8eexm8r',2,'2026-05-07 14:32:00','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Good.</p>','G','2026-05-07 14:38:10',1),(1938,84,234,1,12,'<p>One way load balancing supports digital service availability is by distributing the incoming data across multiple servers instead of one server which can be helpful when dealing with large amounts of data which can lead to overloading the servers. Another way it supports it is by reducing the downtime, for example if one server was to go down, the data can be balanced through the other available servers which means that the service is fully operational without interruptions. Furthermore, load balancing can improve performance and reliability by ensuring that workloads are shared efficiently and evenly. Lastly, sharing the data between servers means that it allows for scalability as more servers can be added to handle increased data traffic.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:33:03',322,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how load balancing supports digital service availability. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>One way load balancing supports digital service availability is by distributing the incoming data across multiple servers instead of one server which can be helpful when dealing with large amounts of data which can lead to overloading the servers. Another way it supports it is by reducing the downtime, for example if one server was to go down, the data can be balanced through the other available servers which means that the service is fully operational without interruptions. Furthermore, load balancing can improve performance and reliability by ensuring that workloads are shared efficiently and evenly. Lastly, sharing the data between servers means that it allows for scalability as more servers can be added to handle increased data traffic.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained how load balancing distributes data across multiple servers, which is a key aspect of supporting availability.</li><li>You effectively described how this distribution helps prevent server overload, especially when dealing with large amounts of data.</li><li>Excellent job explaining how load balancing reduces downtime by rerouting traffic if a server fails, ensuring continuous service operation.</li><li>You also made strong points about improved performance, reliability, and scalability, demonstrating a comprehensive understanding.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Your answer is very thorough; next time, consider starting each point with a direct link to how it supports \"digital service availability\" to reinforce the core of the question.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Load balancing supports digital service availability by distributing incoming network traffic evenly across multiple servers. This prevents any single server from becoming overloaded, which could lead to service degradation or failure. Furthermore, if one server experiences an issue or goes offline, load balancers can automatically redirect traffic to the remaining healthy servers, significantly reducing downtime and ensuring continuous service operation.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:33:10',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1778162787216_wzlce8cws',1,'2026-05-07 14:33:03','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Good</p>','G','2026-05-07 14:36:47',1),(1939,80,176,1,7,'<p>A variable is a section of memory that is allocated a name that can be assigned a value that can change throughout a program. This allows the program to access the stored value later on in a human readable format.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:35:00',157,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain what a variable is in programming. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>A variable is a section of memory that is allocated a name that can be assigned a value that can change throughout a program. This allows the program to access the stored value later on in a human readable format.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve accurately defined a variable as a named section of memory that can hold a value which changes during program execution. This is a key part of the explanation, well done!</li><li>Your point about variables allowing programs to access stored values in a human-readable format is also very clear and demonstrates a good understanding of their practical use.</li><li>To make your answer even stronger and achieve full marks, try to include examples of the different types of data that variables can store. This would show a more comprehensive understanding.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, remember to mention specific examples of data types a variable can hold, such as integer, float, or string, to show the variety of data they can store.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A variable is a named storage location in a computer\'s memory that holds a value. This value can change or be modified as the program runs. Variables can store various data types, such as whole numbers (integers), decimal numbers (floats), or text (strings).</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:35:08',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778162845591_nmrmqgt6q',2,'2026-05-07 14:35:00','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-05-07 14:36:01',1),(1940,76,74,1,7,'<p>An algorithm is a sequence of instructions carried out in a specific order to carry out a task</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:36:37',162,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define algorithm. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>An algorithm is a sequence of instructions carried out in a specific order to carry out a task</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that an algorithm is a sequence of instructions. That\'s a great start!</li><li>Your answer notes that these instructions are carried out in a specific order, which aligns with them being step-by-step.</li><li>To make your definition even stronger, remember to include that an algorithm is \'precise\'.</li><li>Try to be more specific about the goal of an algorithm, moving beyond \"carry out a task\" to phrases like \"solve a problem\" or \"perform a computation\".</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly include that an algorithm is \'precise\' and clarifies its purpose as \'solving a problem or performing a computation\' to fully meet the definition.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An algorithm is a precise, step-by-step sequence of instructions used to solve a problem or perform a computation.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:36:45',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778162838487_na8eexm8r',1,'2026-05-07 14:36:37','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-05-07 14:37:30',1),(1941,83,112,1,7,'<p>Professional developers must abide by programming conventions if they are going to distribute code among coworkers. For example, professional Python developers must use 4x spaces instead of a tab, snake_case for variables and functions, PascalCase for classes, and FULL_CAPS for constants (Python does not have true constants, but they can be emulated).</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:36:55',165,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the importance of professional development for digital professionals. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Professional developers must abide by programming conventions if they are going to distribute code among coworkers. For example, professional Python developers must use 4x spaces instead of a tab, snake_case for variables and functions, PascalCase for classes, and FULL_CAPS for constants (Python does not have true constants, but they can be emulated).</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>Your response highlights the importance of coding conventions, which are crucial for team collaboration and code readability. For this question, consider how *ongoing learning and skill acquisition* contribute to a professional\'s growth.</li><li>To fully address the mark scheme, think about how continued professional development helps digital professionals stay competent and adaptable in a rapidly changing technological landscape.</li><li>You could also explore how professional development impacts aspects like employability, ethical practice, and the overall quality of work produced.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, broaden your interpretation of \"professional development\" to include continuous learning, training, and skill enhancement throughout a career, rather than focusing solely on coding standards.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Professional development is crucial for digital professionals due to the rapid pace of technological change. It ensures continued competence and adaptability, as professionals must constantly learn new languages, frameworks, and tools to remain effective and prevent their skills from becoming obsolete. This continuous learning directly enhances employability, making individuals more attractive to employers and opening up new career opportunities. Furthermore, professional development contributes to quality assurance by enabling professionals to implement the latest best practices and security measures, leading to more robust and reliable solutions. It also helps professionals stay aware of evolving ethical considerations in technology, ensuring responsible and compliant practice.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:37:03',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1778163113114_2e3uxx0er',1,'2026-05-07 14:36:55','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>I\'m not sure if you understood this question, Rowan. Read it more carefully and you\'d see that \"Professional Development\" is about supporting devs to become better devs.</p>','R','2026-05-07 14:39:36',1),(1942,84,231,1,12,'<p>Data integrity can be maintained in a dayabase is by using validation rules such as a range checks or data type checks which can prevent invalid data from being input(ted?) into the database. Another way is by making sure the primary and foreign keys are enforced, primary keys making sure each peife of data is unique, while foreign keys can prevent inconsistent data. Furthermore, regular backups and recovery strategies also help maintain integrity by allowing data to be restored if incase it gets corrupted, deleted or effected by system failure.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:40:41',328,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how data integrity can be maintained in a database. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Data integrity can be maintained in a dayabase is by using validation rules such as a range checks or data type checks which can prevent invalid data from being input(ted?) into the database. Another way is by making sure the primary and foreign keys are enforced, primary keys making sure each peife of data is unique, while foreign keys can prevent inconsistent data. Furthermore, regular backups and recovery strategies also help maintain integrity by allowing data to be restored if incase it gets corrupted, deleted or effected by system failure.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve clearly explained how validation rules, like range and data type checks, prevent invalid data, which is a key aspect of data integrity. Well done!</li><li>You effectively described how primary and foreign keys enforce referential integrity, ensuring data consistency across tables. This is a strong point.</li><li>Including regular backups and recovery strategies demonstrates a comprehensive understanding of maintaining data integrity, especially in the event of data loss or corruption.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>While you covered key concepts well, explicitly using the term \"constraints\" to group ideas like primary/foreign keys and explaining other specific constraints (e.g., NOT NULL) would make your answer even more robust.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Data integrity can be maintained through several methods. Implementing validation rules, such as range checks or data type checks, ensures that only valid data is entered into the database. Enforcing referential integrity using primary and foreign keys prevents inconsistent data across related tables by ensuring relationships are valid and maintained. Additionally, applying constraints like NOT NULL or UNIQUE on specific fields helps prevent missing or duplicate entries. Regular backups and recovery strategies also contribute significantly by allowing data to be restored in case of corruption, deletion, or system failure, thereby preserving its integrity.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:40:49',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1778162787216_wzlce8cws',1,'2026-05-07 14:40:41','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>I think both input, inputted and entered are all acceptable.</p>','G','2026-05-07 14:46:00',1),(1943,76,187,1,7,'<p>Conditional statements are a part of iteration that involves a true or false statement that controls program flow. For example an if statement has two possible outcomes; true or false. This means that the program flow can be seperated into two separate algorithms that are run depending on the outcome of the if statement. Furthermore, while loops are another kind of conditional statement that involves a loop that can only be exited once the condition for the loop is false otherwise it will repeat. This is useful for when you don\'t know the number of iterations before the first iteration such as how many attempts it will take for a user to enter a date in a adequate format.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:41:51',275,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how conditional statements are used to control program flow. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Conditional statements are a part of iteration that involves a true or false statement that controls program flow. For example an if statement has two possible outcomes; true or false. This means that the program flow can be seperated into two separate algorithms that are run depending on the outcome of the if statement. Furthermore, while loops are another kind of conditional statement that involves a loop that can only be exited once the condition for the loop is false otherwise it will repeat. This is useful for when you don\'t know the number of iterations before the first iteration such as how many attempts it will take for a user to enter a date in a adequate format.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that `if` statements use true/false conditions to direct program flow into different paths, which is a great start. Remember that conditional statements are primarily about *selection*, allowing the program to choose a specific path.</li><li>To fully address how conditional statements control flow through decisions, you could have included `elif` and `else` statements. These are crucial for demonstrating comprehensive decision-making and alternative paths.</li><li>While `while` loops do use conditions, the core of this question focuses on *selection* constructs like `if`, `elif`, and `else` to make decisions in the program. Clarifying the distinction between selection and iteration would strengthen your response.</li><li>Providing a simple example or pseudocode showing an `if`, `elif`, `else` structure would have further enhanced your explanation and shown practical application.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, focus on the selection constructs like `if`, `elif`, and `else` when explaining how conditional statements control program flow through decision-making, and include pseudocode to illustrate their use.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Conditional statements control program flow by allowing a program to make decisions and execute specific blocks of code based on whether a given condition is true or false. An `if` statement checks a condition, and if it\'s true, its associated code block is executed. An optional `else` statement provides an alternative code block to run if the `if` condition is false. For scenarios with multiple choices, `elif` (else if) statements can be used to check additional conditions sequentially. This selective execution ensures the program follows a chosen path. For example:<br><code>IF age >= 18 THEN<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;PRINT \"Eligible to vote\"<br>ELSE<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;PRINT \"Not eligible to vote yet\"<br>END IF</code></p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:42:03',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778162838487_na8eexm8r',1,'2026-05-07 14:41:51','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Don\'t be afraid to cite examples... even in pseudocode if you can\'t recall the exact syntax.</p>','A','2026-05-07 14:47:24',1),(1944,84,213,1,12,'<p>One purpose of encryption is to make sure data stays personal and private. One way of doing this is by changing letters to symbols or characters which can then be changed bakc by using keys which require authorisation.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:43:51',91,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State one purpose of encryption. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>One purpose of encryption is to make sure data stays personal and private. One way of doing this is by changing letters to symbols or characters which can then be changed bakc by using keys which require authorisation.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that a key purpose of encryption is to keep data personal and private, which demonstrates an understanding of confidentiality.</li><li>To fully address the mark scheme, ensure you explicitly state that encryption makes the data unreadable or incomprehensible without the proper key.</li><li>Focus on the direct outcome of encryption (unreadable data for unauthorised users) when stating its purpose, rather than detailing the method of changing characters.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly state that encryption makes data unreadable or incomprehensible to anyone without the correct key, directly linking this mechanism to the purpose of protecting confidentiality.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>One purpose of encryption is to protect data confidentiality by making it unreadable to unauthorised individuals without the correct decryption key.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:43:57',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778162787216_wzlce8cws',2,'2026-05-07 14:43:51','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-05-07 14:46:20',1),(1945,80,200,1,7,'<p>On one hand the use of generative AI in software developments would save lots of time and money for companies instead of hiring a large Team to put together a website.</p><p> On the other hand Generative Ai could be trained of code that is not owned by the Dataset provider for the Ai this means that morally the ai could be seen as stealing code from other developers.</p><p>As well as this ai could also be used to help hackers develop tools to help leak personal information.</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:46:38',590,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the ethical implications of using generative AI tools in software development. (8 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>On one hand the use of generative AI in software developments would save lots of time and money for companies instead of hiring a large Team to put together a website.</p><p> On the other hand Generative Ai could be trained of code that is not owned by the Dataset provider for the Ai this means that morally the ai could be seen as stealing code from other developers.</p><p>As well as this ai could also be used to help hackers develop tools to help leak personal information.</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by identifying intellectual property and potential \"code stealing\" as a key ethical concern with generative AI, which is a strong point.</li><li>To strengthen your answer, consider how generative AI can inadvertently embed <strong>bias</strong> from its training data into software, leading to unfair or discriminatory outcomes.</li><li>Think about <strong>accountability</strong>: who is responsible if AI-generated code has flaws, security vulnerabilities, or causes harm? Expanding on this would add depth.</li><li>Exploring the importance of <strong>transparency</strong> in how AI models are trained and the need for clear <strong>regulation</strong> would also enhance your evaluation.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, make sure to explicitly discuss the ethical concern of <strong>bias</strong> in AI-generated code, explaining how training data can influence unfair outcomes.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Generative AI in software development presents significant ethical implications alongside its potential for innovation. One major concern is <strong>plagiarism</strong> and intellectual property theft; AI models trained on vast codebases may inadvertently reproduce or mimic copyrighted code without attribution, raising questions about ownership and fair use. Secondly, <strong>bias</strong> is a critical issue; if training data contains historical biases, the AI-generated code could perpetuate or even amplify these, leading to discriminatory or unfair software, particularly in sensitive applications. Furthermore, <strong>accountability</strong> is complex; determining who is responsible when AI-generated code contains errors, security vulnerabilities, or leads to harmful outcomes (e.g., enabling malicious tools) is a significant challenge for developers, companies, and legal systems. To mitigate these risks, there is a clear need for greater <strong>transparency</strong> in AI model training and robust <strong>regulation</strong> to ensure ethical use, fair practices, and clear lines of responsibility. Balancing innovation with these ethical considerations requires careful oversight and continuous evaluation.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:46:52',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778164541076_2zn0wr2lh',1,'2026-05-07 14:46:38','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>I personally feel that all AI coding should be read, evaluated and understood by a human developer.</p>','A','2026-05-07 14:48:54',1),(1946,76,180,1,7,'<p>For loop, While loop</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:47:25',134,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Identify two types of loops used in Python. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>For loop, While loop</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified the \'for\' loop and the \'while\' loop, which are the two primary loop constructs in Python. This is a great start!</li><li>You\'ve accurately named the specific Python keywords, demonstrating familiarity with the language syntax.</li><li>To fully meet the criteria for a strong response, remember to also identify the *category* of loop each one represents, such as \'count-controlled\' or \'condition-controlled\'.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, clarify whether each loop is count-controlled (like \'for\') or condition-controlled (like \'while\') to show a deeper understanding of their functionality.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Two types of loops used in Python are the count-controlled (for) loop and the condition-controlled (while) loop.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:47:34',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778162838487_na8eexm8r',1,'2026-05-07 14:47:25','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-07 14:47:34',NULL),(1947,83,78,1,7,'<p>def check_even(input_num: float):<br>    if input_num % 2 == 0:<br>        return True<br>    <br>    else:<br>        return False</p><p></p><p>this code takes a number as the input, and returns true if it is even, and false if it is odd</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:47:25',142,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Write a short Python function that checks if a number is even or odd and explain how it works. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>def check_even(input_num: float):<br>    if input_num % 2 == 0:<br>        return True<br>    <br>    else:<br>        return False</p><p></p><p>this code takes a number as the input, and returns true if it is even, and false if it is odd</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve written a clear Python function that correctly uses the modulus operator (`%`) to determine if a number is even, which is excellent!</li><li>To make your function even clearer and align with examples of excellent responses, consider returning the strings \'Even\' or \'Odd\' instead of `True` or `False`.</li><li>Your explanation accurately describes what the code does, but it could be more detailed by explaining *how* the modulus operator (`%`) works to achieve this.</li><li>Try to include how the `if/else` statements (selection) and the `return` statements contribute to the function\'s overall logic and output.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on the explanation by explicitly stating that the modulus operator (`%`) calculates the remainder of a division, and explain why checking if the remainder when divided by 2 is 0 tells us the number is even.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>```python<br>def check_even_odd(number):<br>    if number % 2 == 0:<br>        return \"Even\"<br>    else:<br>        return \"Odd\"<br>```<br><br>This function takes a `number` as input. It uses the modulus operator (`%`) to find the remainder when the number is divided by 2. The `if` statement is a selection statement that checks if this remainder is equal to 0. If it is (meaning the number is even), the function uses a `return` statement to output the string \"Even\". Otherwise, the `else` block executes, and it returns \"Odd\".</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:47:35',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778163113114_2e3uxx0er',1,'2026-05-07 14:47:25','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-07 14:47:35',NULL),(1948,81,17,1,7,'<p>pre-written libraries are pieces of code which have already been created, here are some notable advantages and disadvantages to using pre-written libraries in software development.</p><p>security</p><p>advantages</p><ul><li><p>pre written libraries are often updated by large amounts of people, who will help keep the software secure and without potentially dangerous bugs</p></li><li><p>pre written libraries are often supported by many contributors, meaning that information on how to use the software safely is Likely readily available online</p></li></ul><p>disadvantages</p><ul><li><p>because pre written libraries are more public than self developed code they are also easier for attackers to understand, meaning that if your code uses publicly available pre written libraries, it as through attackers can partially see your code, which makes it less secure</p></li><li><p>when using pre written code that you don\'t totally understand you are trusting that the person who has written it is not an attacker themselves using it for cybercrime</p></li></ul><p></p><p>simplicity</p><p>advantages</p><ul><li><p>using pre written libraries saves on having to understand how the code functions, meaning that someone without the know-how can still create complicated programs</p></li><li><p>pre written libraries are often documented, meaning it can be simpler to lear how a more complicated programming concept than trying to figure it out yourself</p></li></ul><p>disadvantages</p><ul><li><p>someone who relies to heavily on pre written code may end up creating a program that they cannot further edit or maintain well due to its complexity</p></li><li><p>there is no guaranteed quality of pre written code meaning that an imported library might solve a relatively simple problem in a confusing or convoluted way</p></li></ul><p></p><p>efficiency</p><p>advantages</p><ul><li><p>pre written code cuts down on the time to both think of, and write down code, meaning that fast and rough developments can be made very quickly</p></li><li><p>pre written code often has had a lot of time poured into it, meaning that some of the most efficient solutions to problems  will already exist in pre written libraries</p></li></ul><p>disadvantages</p><ul><li><p>pre written code will in almost all cases not be an exact fit for the specific program that a developer is creating</p></li><li><p>pre written code often has extraneous functionality that is not needed for every project it is used in</p></li></ul><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:48:19',1902,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the advantages and disadvantages of using pre-written libraries in software development. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>pre-written libraries are pieces of code which have already been created, here are some notable advantages and disadvantages to using pre-written libraries in software development.</p><p>security</p><ul><li><p>pre written libraries are often updated by large amounts of people, who will help keep the software secure and without potentially dangerous bugs</p></li><li><p>pre written libraries are often supported by many contributors, meaning that information on how to use the software safely is Likely readily available online</p></li></ul><p>disadvantages</p><ul><li><p>because pre written libraries are more public than self developed code they are also easier for attackers to understand, meaning that if your code uses publicly available pre written libraries, it as through attackers can partially see your code, which makes it less secure</p></li><li><p>when using pre written code that you don\'t totally understand you are trusting that the person who has written it is not an attacker themselves using it for cybercrime</p></li></ul><p></p><p>simplicity</p><p>advantages</p><ul><li><p>using pre written libraries saves on having to understand how the code functions, meaning that someone without the know-how can still create complicated programs</p></li><li><p>pre written libraries are often documented, meaning it can be simpler to lear how a more complicated programming concept than trying to figure it out yourself</p></li></ul><p>disadvantages</p><ul><li><p>someone who relies to heavily on pre written code may end up creating a program that they cannot further edit or maintain well due to its complexity</p></li><li><p>there is no guaranteed quality of pre written code meaning that an imported library might solve a relatively simple problem in a confusing or convoluted way</p></li></ul><p></p><p>efficiency</p><p>advantages</p><ul><li><p>pre written code cuts down on the time to both think of, and write down code, meaning that fast and rough developments can be made very quickly</p></li><li><p>pre written code often has had a lot of time poured into it, meaning that some of the most efficient solutions to problems  will already exist in pre written libraries</p></li></ul><p>disadvantages</p><ul><li><p>pre written code will in almost all cases not be an exact fit for the specific program that a developer is creating</p></li><li><p>pre written code often has extraneous functionality that is not needed for every project it is used in</p></li></ul><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve provided a comprehensive list of advantages and disadvantages, covering many relevant aspects like security, efficiency, and ease of use. This shows a good understanding of the topic.</li><li>To further strengthen your evaluation, try to incorporate specific examples of pre-written libraries, such as `matplotlib` for data visualisation or `pandas` for data manipulation. This helps illustrate your points with practical applications.</li><li>Consider explicitly discussing drawbacks like \"dependency risk\" and \"version conflicts,\" where different libraries might require incompatible versions of other components. This is a common challenge in software development.</li><li>You touched on the idea of not understanding the code; you could expand this into how over-reliance on libraries might reduce a developer\'s understanding of core programming logic or algorithms. This adds depth to your \"simplicity\" disadvantage.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Integrate specific examples of pre-written libraries into your advantages and disadvantages to demonstrate practical application and enhance your reasoning.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Using pre-written libraries offers significant advantages by accelerating development time and reducing the amount of code a developer needs to write from scratch. Libraries like `pandas` for data analysis or `Requests` for web interactions are often highly optimised, reliable due to community testing, and come with extensive documentation, making complex tasks more accessible. This allows developers to focus on unique project logic rather than reinventing common functionalities.</p><p>However, there are notable disadvantages. Relying on external libraries introduces dependency risk; if a library becomes unmaintained or contains security vulnerabilities, it can impact the project. Version conflicts can also arise when different libraries require incompatible versions of shared components, leading to integration issues. Furthermore, excessive reliance on libraries without understanding their underlying logic can hinder a developer\'s learning of core programming concepts and make debugging or customising functionality more challenging if the library isn\'t an exact fit for specific project goals. This can also lead to code bloat if libraries include much more functionality than is actually needed.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:48:34',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1778163369760_6fm4vzbwv',1,'2026-05-07 14:48:19','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Thought this was a good answer. <strong>5 marks.</strong></p>','G','2026-05-07 14:51:33',1),(1949,84,211,1,12,'<p>Data redundancy is basically having copies of data in multiple places, this can lead to storage being lowered with unnecessary data, and can also lead to inconsistencies if the copies aren\'t all up to date / the same.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:48:24',107,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State what is meant by data redundancy. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Data redundancy is basically having copies of data in multiple places, this can lead to storage being lowered with unnecessary data, and can also lead to inconsistencies if the copies aren\'t all up to date / the same.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly identified that data redundancy involves having \"copies of data in multiple places,\" which is a great start.</li><li>To make your answer even stronger, explicitly state that this duplication of data is *unnecessary*.</li><li>Remember to specify the typical context for data redundancy, such as \"within a database or storage system.\"</li><li>Be careful when discussing consequences; redundant data typically *increases* storage requirements, rather than lowering them.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, ensure your definition specifically states that data redundancy is the *unnecessary duplication* of data *within a database or storage system*.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Data redundancy is the unnecessary duplication of data within a database or storage system.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:48:31',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1778162787216_wzlce8cws',1,'2026-05-07 14:48:24','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Didn\'t quite get your argument here.</p>','R','2026-05-07 14:50:05',1),(1950,84,216,1,12,'<p>A fireball is a security measure, that can monitor incoming and out going data, this means that it can protect networks by blocking whatever isn\'t authorised,while allowing through the legitimate communications</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:52:06',109,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State what a firewall does. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>A fireball is a security measure, that can monitor incoming and out going data, this means that it can protect networks by blocking whatever isn\'t authorised,while allowing through the legitimate communications</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that a firewall monitors incoming and outgoing network traffic, which is a key function.</li><li>You also accurately stated that it protects networks by blocking unauthorised communications and allowing legitimate ones, demonstrating an understanding of its filtering role.</li><li>Your response clearly indicates that filtering is based on a distinction between authorised and legitimate traffic, which aligns with the concept of security rules.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Be careful with your spelling next time; ensure you write \"firewall\" instead of \"fireball\" to maintain accuracy in your technical terms.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A firewall monitors and filters incoming and outgoing network traffic based on predefined security rules to protect a network from unauthorised access.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:52:13',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1778162787216_wzlce8cws',1,'2026-05-07 14:52:06','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Mention hardware and software fireballs... I mean firewalls next time. :-)</p>','G','2026-05-07 14:53:43',1),(1951,80,13,1,7,'<p>#this runs the piece of code for every item in the list</p><p>largest = 0</p><p>for x in range(Len(list)):</p><p>	if largest &lt;list[x]:</p><p>		largest = list[x]</p><p>print(f\"the largest number is {largest}\")</p><p>		</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:52:24',306,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Using Python, write and explain an algorithm that finds the largest number in a list. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>#this runs the piece of code for every item in the list</p><p>largest = 0</p><p>for x in range(Len(list)):</p><p>	if largest &lt;list[x]:</p><p>		largest = list[x]</p><p>print(f\"the largest number is {largest}\")</p><p>		</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>Your use of a <code>for</code> loop to go through the items in the list is a great start towards iterating through the data.</li><li>Your code correctly uses an <code>if</code> statement to compare numbers and updates the <code>largest</code> variable when a larger value is found.</li><li>To make your algorithm robust for all possible lists (e.g., those with negative numbers), it\'s best to initialize <code>largest</code> with the first element of the list rather than a fixed number like 0.</li><li>Expand your explanation to clearly describe the comparison step and when the <code>largest</code> variable gets updated, as well as the initial setup.</li><li>Remember that Python function names like <code>len()</code> are lowercase, and it\'s good practice to avoid using built-in names like <code>list</code> for your variables.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Make your algorithm more robust by initializing your <code>largest</code> variable with the first element of the list, rather than a fixed number like 0, to handle lists containing only negative numbers effectively.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p># Define a sample list of numbers<br>numbers_list = [12, 5, 23, 8, 17]<br><br># Initialize \'largest_number\' with the first element of the list.<br># This ensures it works correctly even with negative numbers.<br>largest_number = numbers_list[0]<br><br># Iterate through each number in the list<br>for current_number in numbers_list:<br>    # Compare the current number with the \'largest_number\' found so far<br>    if current_number > largest_number:<br>        # If the current number is larger, update \'largest_number\'<br>        largest_number = current_number<br><br>print(f\"The largest number in the list is: {largest_number}\")<br><br># Explanation:<br># The algorithm works by:<br># 1. Initialization: It sets an initial `largest_number` using the first item in the list.<br># 2. Iteration: It then loops through every item (`current_number`) in the list.<br># 3. Comparison: Inside the loop, it compares `current_number` with the `largest_number` found so far.<br># 4. Updating: If `current_number` is found to be greater, `largest_number` is updated to this new value.<br># This ensures that by the end of the iteration, `largest_number` holds the true maximum value. Python also has a built-in `max()` function for this purpose.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:52:42',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778164541076_2zn0wr2lh',1,'2026-05-07 14:52:24','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-07 14:52:42',NULL),(1952,84,205,1,12,'<p>I\'m not sure</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:53:16',10,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State one purpose of a business case. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>I\'m not sure</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>It\'s okay to feel unsure, but always try to write down anything you think might be relevant, even if it\'s just a guess. This can sometimes earn you partial marks.</li><li>A business case is a formal document, so think about why an organisation would create such a document before starting a project.</li><li>Consider what information an organisation would need to know before deciding whether to proceed with a new idea or project.</li><li>The mark scheme suggests thinking about how a business case helps justify a project by looking at benefits, costs, and risks.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Even if you\'re not fully confident, try to answer the question with what you think might be plausible. Writing something relevant is better than nothing and helps you identify specific areas for learning.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A business case justifies the need for a project or investment by outlining its potential benefits, costs, and risks.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:53:22',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1778162787216_wzlce8cws',1,'2026-05-07 14:53:16','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>We need to revisit this for everyone perhaps...</p>','R','2026-05-07 14:54:19',1),(1953,80,74,1,7,'<p>algorithm is a set of simple steps that can be followed to solve a problem</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:55:25',24,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define algorithm. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>algorithm is a set of simple steps that can be followed to solve a problem</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by identifying that an algorithm involves steps to solve a problem! This shows a good understanding of the core concept.</li><li>To make your definition more precise, consider how you might describe the nature of these steps more specifically, for example, that they are \'precise\' and form a \'sequence of instructions\'.</li><li>Algorithms are also used for \'computation\', not just solving problems. Adding this would make your definition more complete.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>When defining an algorithm, ensure you emphasize that the steps are \'precise\' and a \'sequence of instructions\', and include that they can also be used to perform a \'computation\'.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An algorithm is a precise, step-by-step sequence of instructions used to solve a problem or perform a computation.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:55:32',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778164541076_2zn0wr2lh',1,'2026-05-07 14:55:25','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-07 14:55:32',NULL),(1954,83,199,1,7,'<p>Software is far more reliable if it has been properly tested as it will allow developers to find and patch common bugs before users experience them.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:55:55',61,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Analyse how software testing methods ensure solution reliability. (8 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Software is far more reliable if it has been properly tested as it will allow developers to find and patch common bugs before users experience them.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by identifying the core purpose of testing – finding and fixing bugs before release to improve reliability.</li><li>To develop your answer further, consider discussing specific types of testing methods, such as unit, integration, or system testing, which are crucial for an 8-mark analysis.</li><li>For each testing method you mention, it would be beneficial to explain its specific benefits in ensuring reliability and any potential drawbacks it might have.</li><li>Additionally, think about how aspects like test automation and comprehensive documentation contribute to a more reliable testing process.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, ensure you name and briefly explain different types of software testing, such as unit, integration, or system testing, to show a deeper understanding.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Software reliability is significantly enhanced through a multi-stage testing approach. Unit testing ensures individual components function correctly, catching bugs early and making them easier to fix. Integration testing then verifies that these components interact as expected, addressing interface issues. Finally, system testing assesses the entire solution against requirements, validating end-to-end functionality and performance in a near-production environment. Each method brings unique benefits; unit testing offers quick isolation of issues, while system testing confirms overall solution stability. Challenges can include the time and resource investment for comprehensive testing, but these are often outweighed by reduced post-release defects. The reliability of these processes is further strengthened by automation, which allows for consistent and frequent execution of tests, and thorough documentation, ensuring tests are understandable and maintainable over time.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:56:02',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778163113114_2e3uxx0er',1,'2026-05-07 14:55:55','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-07 14:56:02',NULL),(1955,81,11,1,7,'<p>pattern recognition and abstraction are both methods of computational thinking, computational thinking is an problem solving technique used to create programs.</p><p>pattern recognition is noticing relationships between elements in a program, and understanding them in relation to each other as a pattern, e.g. recognising that whatever number the user enters in incremented by some multiple of another.</p><p>abstraction is understanding parts of a program in a different context for simplification</p>',NULL,'2026-05-07 14:58:49',492,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the difference between pattern recognition and abstraction in computational thinking. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>pattern recognition and abstraction are both methods of computational thinking, computational thinking is an problem solving technique used to create programs.</p><p>pattern recognition is noticing relationships between elements in a program, and understanding them in relation to each other as a pattern, e.g. recognising that whatever number the user enters in incremented by some multiple of another.</p><p>abstraction is understanding parts of a program in a different context for simplification</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified both pattern recognition and abstraction as computational thinking methods, which is a great start.</li><li>For pattern recognition, try to focus on spotting similarities or trends that occur *across* different problems or tasks, not just within one program.</li><li>Your definition of abstraction is a good attempt, but it could be clearer by emphasising the idea of simplifying by *removing unnecessary details* to focus only on what\'s essential.</li><li>To fully answer the question, ensure you explicitly explain how these two concepts *differ* from each other in their purpose and application.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly state the specific difference between pattern recognition and abstraction, explaining how one identifies recurring elements and the other focuses on simplifying by ignoring irrelevant details.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Pattern recognition involves identifying similarities, trends, or recurring elements across different problems or data sets to find general solutions. Abstraction, on the other hand, is the process of filtering out or ignoring unnecessary details and focusing only on the essential information that matters for solving a specific problem, simplifying its complexity.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-07 14:58:56',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778165368923_ih97qcsci',1,'2026-05-07 14:58:49','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-07 14:58:56',NULL),(1956,59,95,1,7,'<p>A variable is a named storage device that stores data within a program. The data can be changed within the program. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-08 08:27:15',25,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define the term variable in programming. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>A variable is a named storage device that stores data within a program. The data can be changed within the program. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified a variable as a named storage location (or device) for data within a program, which is a key part of the definition.</li><li>You clearly stated that the data stored in a variable can be changed during program execution, highlighting a crucial characteristic.</li><li>To make your answer even more comprehensive, consider adding that variables also have a specific data type, such as integer or string.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, you could enhance your definition by mentioning that variables also hold a specific \'data type,\' which helps the computer understand what kind of information is being stored.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A variable is a named storage location in memory that holds a value which can be changed during the execution of a program. It also has a specific data type.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-08 08:27:22',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778228797756_omvwrxrqm',2,'2026-05-08 08:27:15','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-08 08:27:22',NULL),(1957,59,109,1,7,'<p>One example of emerging digital technologies which affect software design is Artificial Intelligence. Ai can write code for a user however the code will most likely be underdeveloped and contain many errors this could lead to cyber criminals using Ai to program them software which can be used to take people\'s data or commit other crimes. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-08 08:30:25',149,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State two examples of emerging digital technologies affecting software design. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>One example of emerging digital technologies which affect software design is Artificial Intelligence. Ai can write code for a user however the code will most likely be underdeveloped and contain many errors this could lead to cyber criminals using Ai to program them software which can be used to take people\'s data or commit other crimes. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully identified Artificial Intelligence as a relevant emerging technology, which is a great start!</li><li>To earn full marks, remember the question asks for *two* examples of emerging digital technologies. Try to think of another distinct one.</li><li>You began to explain AI\'s impact, which is good. For future answers, try to focus specifically on how these technologies change the software design process or the tools developers use.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Identify a second emerging technology affecting software design and briefly explain its direct impact on how software is designed or developed.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Two examples include Artificial Intelligence (AI), which can assist designers with automated code generation or suggest design patterns, and the Internet of Things (IoT), which requires software designers to consider more distributed architectures and manage data from numerous interconnected devices.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-08 08:30:31',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778228797756_omvwrxrqm',1,'2026-05-08 08:30:25','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-08 08:30:31',NULL),(1958,59,90,1,7,'<p>Privacy concerns arise from increased use of digital systems as more cyber criminals learn how to get past prevention methods which can lead to data breaches and other cyber crime. This causes many concerns to arise as cyber criminals evolve around known prevention methods and bring more attention to the crimes possible when using digital systems. Data breaches also arise concern as a lot of sensitive information can be breached through them for example, if there was a data breach in an online store banking information and delivery addresses can be leaked to said cyber criminals.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-08 08:34:54',226,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how privacy concerns arise from increased use of digital systems. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Privacy concerns arise from increased use of digital systems as more cyber criminals learn how to get past prevention methods which can lead to data breaches and other cyber crime. This causes many concerns to arise as cyber criminals evolve around known prevention methods and bring more attention to the crimes possible when using digital systems. Data breaches also arise concern as a lot of sensitive information can be breached through them for example, if there was a data breach in an online store banking information and delivery addresses can be leaked to said cyber criminals.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You accurately identified data breaches and the potential misuse of sensitive information as significant privacy concerns, which is a great start.</li><li>To strengthen your answer, consider explaining how privacy concerns arise from the routine collection of personal data by digital systems, not just from criminal activity.</li><li>Think about how concepts like surveillance and the continuous creation of a \'digital footprint\' contribute to these concerns.</li><li>For excellent marks, discussing user consent for data handling and referring to relevant legislation like GDPR would be beneficial.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to broaden your explanation beyond just cybercrime to include how privacy is impacted by common practices like data collection, surveillance, and digital footprints.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Increased use of digital systems leads to privacy concerns due to extensive data collection, where personal information is gathered even without malicious intent. This data contributes to an individual\'s \'digital footprint\' and can lead to surveillance, where activities are monitored. Concerns arise from the potential misuse of this personal information, such as for targeted advertising or identity theft, and the lack of explicit user consent for its collection and processing. Legislation like GDPR aims to address these concerns by giving individuals greater control over their data.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-08 08:35:02',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778228797756_omvwrxrqm',1,'2026-05-08 08:34:54','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-08 08:35:02',NULL),(1959,59,25,1,7,'<p>The data protection act affects software developers as they need to make sure whatever data they collect with their software must be to the highest security standards as of publishing. This is to protect their user data as if there is a data breach and its found out the developers did not put any security measures in place it can lead to legal repercussions. This also occurs when security measures are not regularly updated </p>',NULL,'2026-05-08 08:44:46',455,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how the Data Protection Act and GDPR affect software developers. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The data protection act affects software developers as they need to make sure whatever data they collect with their software must be to the highest security standards as of publishing. This is to protect their user data as if there is a data breach and its found out the developers did not put any security measures in place it can lead to legal repercussions. This also occurs when security measures are not regularly updated </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You rightly identified the critical need for software developers to implement high security standards and the legal repercussions of data breaches. This is a crucial aspect of GDPR and DPA compliance.</li><li>To enhance your answer, consider how developers must design software to support principles like \'lawful processing\' and \'data minimisation\' from the outset. This means only collecting essential data with a legitimate reason.</li><li>Remember to include the importance of user consent when collecting data. Developers must ensure their software clearly obtains and manages this consent effectively.</li><li>Think about how software needs to be built to enable users to exercise their rights, such as the right to access, rectify, or erase their personal data.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly mention specific GDPR/DPA principles and user rights, such as data minimisation or the right to erasure, and explain how software must be designed to accommodate them.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The Data Protection Act and GDPR significantly impact software developers by requiring them to build systems that adhere to key principles. Developers must ensure data is lawfully processed, obtain explicit user consent for collection, and implement data minimisation, only collecting necessary information. They are responsible for integrating secure storage and robust access control mechanisms into their software. Additionally, developers must enable user rights, such as the right to access and erase personal data, as non-compliance can severely damage organisational reputation and user trust.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-08 08:44:55',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778228797756_omvwrxrqm',1,'2026-05-08 08:44:46','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-08 08:44:55',NULL),(1960,59,175,1,7,'<p>Decomposition makes problems easier to solve by cutting larger problems down into smaller problems making them easier to understand. They also make it easier to spread tasks out between colleagues in team projects if needed.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-08 08:57:28',427,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State two benefits of using decomposition in software design. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Decomposition makes problems easier to solve by cutting larger problems down into smaller problems making them easier to understand. They also make it easier to spread tasks out between colleagues in team projects if needed.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve clearly identified how decomposition simplifies complex problems, making them much easier to understand and manage. This is an excellent point!</li><li>You also successfully explained how it facilitates teamwork and task distribution among developers, which is a great insight into collaboration.</li><li>Your answer effectively covers two distinct benefits outlined in the mark scheme, showing a strong understanding of the concept.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Consider adding a brief mention of how decomposition can also make debugging easier by isolating potential issues to smaller, more manageable components.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Decomposition simplifies complex problems by breaking them into smaller, more manageable parts, making them easier to understand and design. It also facilitates easier collaboration among developers, as different team members can work independently on distinct components.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-08 08:57:38',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778228797756_omvwrxrqm',1,'2026-05-08 08:57:28','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-08 08:57:38',NULL),(1961,59,10,1,7,'<p>Decomposition is breaking down larger problems into smaller problems which make it easier to understand and solve while also supporting collaboration between team members on team projects</p>',NULL,'2026-05-08 08:58:50',38,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>What is the purpose of decomposition in problem solving? (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Decomposition is breaking down larger problems into smaller problems which make it easier to understand and solve while also supporting collaboration between team members on team projects</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that decomposition involves breaking down larger problems into smaller problems, which is a strong start.</li><li>You also rightly pointed out that this process makes problems easier to understand and solve, showing good insight into its benefits.</li><li>To gain full marks, remember to specify that these smaller problems are solved individually and then recombined to form a complete solution for the original problem.</li><li>The point about supporting collaboration is a valid practical benefit, but the core purpose of decomposition focuses on the individual management and resolution of complexity.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, ensure you explain that the smaller problems are solved individually and their solutions are then integrated to solve the initial complex problem.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Decomposition is the process of breaking down a complex problem into smaller, more manageable sub-problems. This allows each sub-problem to be solved individually, making the overall task easier to tackle, before combining the solutions to form a complete solution for the original problem.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-08 08:58:58',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778228797756_omvwrxrqm',1,'2026-05-08 08:58:50','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-08 08:58:58',NULL);
INSERT INTO `tblresponse` VALUES (1962,59,24,1,7,'<p>IT workers should have regular eye tests due to there time spent staring at the monitor and should be allowed regular breaks to avoid any back pain for example</p>',NULL,'2026-05-08 09:04:59',55,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State two key requirements of the Health and Safety at Work Act relevant to IT workers. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>IT workers should have regular eye tests due to there time spent staring at the monitor and should be allowed regular breaks to avoid any back pain for example</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You have successfully identified regular eye tests as a key requirement of the Health and Safety at Work Act. This shows a good understanding of employee welfare related to IT work.</li><li>You also correctly stated that regular breaks are important to prevent issues like back pain, which is another crucial aspect of IT workplace safety.</li><li>To make your answer even stronger, try to explicitly link these requirements to the employer\'s duties and responsibilities under the Act.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state that these requirements are the *employer\'s* responsibility or duty under the Act, which strengthens the link to the legislation.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Employers have a duty to provide regular eye tests for display screen equipment users, and they must also ensure employees are given regular breaks from display screen work.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-08 09:05:06',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778228797756_omvwrxrqm',1,'2026-05-08 09:04:59','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-08 09:05:06',NULL),(1963,59,81,1,7,'<p>Debugging supports the development of code by checking errors through the robust code. This can lead to the robust code being updated and working efficiently with updated interpreters. Removing errors in robust code leads to easier use of the program by removing the errors</p>',NULL,'2026-05-08 09:09:00',123,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how debugging supports the development of robust code. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Debugging supports the development of code by checking errors through the robust code. This can lead to the robust code being updated and working efficiently with updated interpreters. Removing errors in robust code leads to easier use of the program by removing the errors</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that debugging involves checking and removing errors. To enhance your answer, consider explaining the *types* of errors debugging addresses, such as logic errors or runtime errors.</li><li>The mark scheme looks for how debugging *improves reliability*. Elaborate on how correcting these errors makes the code more dependable and less prone to unexpected failures.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, describe specific debugging methods, such as using print statements or setting breakpoints in an IDE to trace program execution.</li><li>Think about how eliminating errors specifically makes code \"robust\" and \"maintainable,\" rather than just easier to use, by making it resilient to various inputs and future changes.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, include specific debugging techniques (e.g., breakpoints, print statements) and explain how identifying and fixing different error types (logic, runtime) contributes to a program\'s overall robustness and reliability.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Debugging supports the development of robust code by systematically identifying and correcting logic or runtime errors, which significantly improves the software\'s reliability. Developers achieve this by employing methods such as setting breakpoints in an IDE to pause execution and inspect variable states, or using print statements to trace program flow. By eliminating these errors, the code becomes more stable, resilient to unexpected inputs, and easier to maintain and update over time, directly contributing to its robustness and long-term viability.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-08 09:09:08',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778228797756_omvwrxrqm',1,'2026-05-08 09:09:00','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-08 09:09:08',NULL),(1964,85,1060,1,33,'<p>Moorside Council must consider various different change management approaches in the context of their 18-month deadline, critical availability, large number of staff, and data migration risks when migrating from their legacy systems to a Cloud based solution.</p><p>Moorside council should consider a Pilot change management approach as this allows Moorside to gain a better understanding of the receptiveness from users of their new cloud system, as well as any feedback that could make the system better. This is important for Moorside as the resistance to change from employees is growing and therefore by targeting a specific group/location of users/employees Moorside may gain a better understanding of what exactly is causing resistance, and implementing a fix. A Pilot change will also allow Moorside the ability to test the system in a real-world environment with limited risk which will further their understanding of how the new system performs in the real world before fully implementing it.</p><p>However, a Pilot change management approach may not reveal all large-scale issues which may only provide insight into a small minority of issues/feedback that the targeted group identify, leaving out many unforeseen issues which may if damaging, not only increase employee/user backlash, but also effecting availability of their critical services.</p><p>Moorside should also consider a Phased Change Management approach which will allow parts of the legacy system to be used in collaboration with parts of the new cloud system which gives the 400+ employees time to get used to certain aspects before a full implementation. This is highly beneficial as it tackles the issue of employee backlash, which especially applied to developers managing the backend, will need time to get used to the new functionality as well as giving iterative feedback as new parts of the cloud system are introduced.</p><p>However if using a Phased change, Moorside must first validate/check that the legacy system is compatible with the new cloud system as otherwise the system could lose parts of it\'s functionality, effecting it\'s availability which for a local government authority is highly important insofar as impacts on the services provided will effect the public of which they are responsible. Taking into account the 18-month deadline set, a phased change will also take more time and money than the other change management approaches since it will result in ongoing costs when implementing new parts of the new system which must be accounted for due to their reliance on government funding, but will also ensure those employees using the system are comfortable which is arguably more important in the long-term.</p><p>Moorside could also consider a direct change, which would enable them to replace the legacy system with the cloud system immediately solving the issue of the deadline quickly. However, if the fully-implemented change is responded to negatively, then it could not only impact their availability of systems due to employees not knowing how to maintain the continuous operation of services required, but also cost them significant money in potentially modifying the new system or rolling back to the previous version if allowed. With 400+ employees, this change is extremely risky.</p><p>In conclusion, Moorside should consider adopting a hybrid change management approach where they use both a Pilot change and a Phased change as this not only allows time for employees to get used to the new system reducing backlash, but also allows them to test it in a real-environment with real employees before any implementation which will give them a clearer picture of receptiveness and overall feedback to the change which will allow them to iterate on parts of the new system before full implementation. However, Moorside must also consider their government budget as using two change management approaches could cost significant money, especially if the cloud system was already a high-budget decision.</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-08 17:55:36',1670,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Moorside Council is a local government authority responsible for services including waste collection, planning applications and social care. It currently runs its administrative operations on a legacy on-premises system that is over 12 years old. The software vendor has announced it will cease support for the system in 18 months. </p><p>The council\'s IT director has proposed migrating to a modern cloud-based enterprise resource planning (ERP) system. The project will affect over 400 staff across multiple departments, each of which has its own working practices. A change advisory board (CAB) has been established. Several department heads have expressed resistance to the change, citing concerns about data migration, staff training and service continuity during the transition. </p><p><strong>Key constraints: </strong>18-month deadline, 400+ staff across multiple departments, public sector legal obligations, continuity of critical services, significant data migration risk. </p><p><em>Evaluate the change management processes Moorside Council should adopt when migrating from its legacy system to the new cloud-based ERP system, justifying the approaches with reference to the council\'s specific circumstances.</em></p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Moorside Council must consider various different change management approaches in the context of their 18-month deadline, critical availability, large number of staff, and data migration risks when migrating from their legacy systems to a Cloud based solution.</p><p>Moorside council should consider a Pilot change management approach as this allows Moorside to gain a better understanding of the receptiveness from users of their new cloud system, as well as any feedback that could make the system better. This is important for Moorside as the resistance to change from employees is growing and therefore by targeting a specific group/location of users/employees Moorside may gain a better understanding of what exactly is causing resistance, and implementing a fix. A Pilot change will also allow Moorside the ability to test the system in a real-world environment with limited risk which will further their understanding of how the new system performs in the real world before fully implementing it.</p><p>However, a Pilot change management approach may not reveal all large-scale issues which may only provide insight into a small minority of issues/feedback that the targeted group identify, leaving out many unforeseen issues which may if damaging, not only increase employee/user backlash, but also effecting availability of their critical services.</p><p>Moorside should also consider a Phased Change Management approach which will allow parts of the legacy system to be used in collaboration with parts of the new cloud system which gives the 400+ employees time to get used to certain aspects before a full implementation. This is highly beneficial as it tackles the issue of employee backlash, which especially applied to developers managing the backend, will need time to get used to the new functionality as well as giving iterative feedback as new parts of the cloud system are introduced.</p><p>However if using a Phased change, Moorside must first validate/check that the legacy system is compatible with the new cloud system as otherwise the system could lose parts of it\'s functionality, effecting it\'s availability which for a local government authority is highly important insofar as impacts on the services provided will effect the public of which they are responsible. Taking into account the 18-month deadline set, a phased change will also take more time and money than the other change management approaches since it will result in ongoing costs when implementing new parts of the system which must be accounted for due to their reliance on government funding, but will also ensure those employees using the system are comfortable which is arguably more important in the long-term.</p><p>Moorside could also consider a direct change, which would enable them to replace the legacy system with the cloud system immediately solving the issue of the deadline quickly. However, if the fully-implemented change is responded to negatively, then it could not only impact their availability of systems due to employees not knowing how to maintain the continuous operation of services required, but also cost them significant money in potentially modifying the new system or rolling back to the previous version if allowed. With 400+ employees, this change is extremely risky.</p><p>In conclusion, Moorside should consider adopting a hybrid change management approach where they use both a Pilot change and a Phased change as this not only allows time for employees to get used to the new system reducing backlash, but also allows them to test it in a real-environment with real employees before any implementation which will give them a clearer picture of receptiveness and overall feedback to the change which will allow them to iterate on parts of the new system before full implementation. However, Moorside must also consider their government budget as using two change management approaches could cost significant money, especially if the cloud system was already a high-budget decision.</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You effectively evaluated different deployment strategies (Pilot, Phased, Direct) and justified your choices by linking them to staff resistance and the need for service continuity, which is excellent.</li><li>To strengthen your evaluation, next time, explicitly name and apply a recognised change management framework like Kotter\'s 8-Step Model or ADKAR to structure how the council manages the human side of change.</li><li>You rightly identified data migration as a risk; to improve, outline specific strategies such as data auditing, cleansing, and test migrations to mitigate this risk.</li><li>Remember to incorporate the existing Change Advisory Board (CAB) into your plan, explaining its role in governing and approving changes for Moorside Council.</li><li>Consider specific strategies for staff training beyond just giving them \"time to get used to\" the system, such as role-based training or a superuser model.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Focus on integrating named change management frameworks (e.g., Kotter, ADKAR) with specific strategies for data migration and the role of the CAB, providing a more structured and comprehensive approach to the evaluation.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Moorside Council faces a critical and complex migration, requiring a robust change management strategy within its 18-month deadline, affecting 400+ staff across diverse departments while maintaining essential public services.</p><p>Firstly, Moorside should adopt a structured change management framework like **Kotter\'s 8-Step Model**. The initial steps – creating urgency, building a guiding coalition, and developing a vision – are crucial given the 18-month deadline and resistance from department heads. This involves transparent communication about the vendor\'s end-of-life support, engaging key stakeholders (including resistant department heads) to co-create the vision for the new ERP, and establishing a strong, cross-departmental project team. The **ADKAR Model** (Awareness, Desire, Knowledge, Ability, Reinforcement) can complement this by tracking individual staff readiness, ensuring targeted interventions for awareness and desire to change.</p><p>The established **Change Advisory Board (CAB)** will be central to governance. Its role should be clearly defined: evaluating proposed changes, assessing risks (especially data migration and service continuity), approving change requests, and ensuring rollback plans are robust. This provides a formal structure for managing technical changes and maintaining control.</p><p>For **deployment**, a **phased rollout** is the most appropriate approach, rather than a high-risk \'big-bang\'. Deploying to one or two less critical departments first allows the council to learn, refine processes, address technical issues, and gather feedback before expanding. This mitigates risk, builds confidence, and allows for continuous improvement, which is vital for a 400+ staff organisation with critical public services. While slower, it significantly reduces the chance of widespread service disruption and staff backlash. A parallel running phase for critical services could also be considered to ensure continuity during the transition, despite increased resource requirements.</p><p>**Data migration** is a significant risk with a 12-year-old legacy system. Moorside must implement a rigorous strategy:\n<ul><li>**Data Audit & Cleansing:** Identify and rectify poor quality, duplicate, or obsolete data before migration.</li><li>**Data Mapping:** Carefully map legacy data fields to the new ERP schema.</li><li>**Test Migrations:** Conduct multiple test migrations in a non-production environment, involving department leads for validation.</li><li>**Validation:** After live migration, conduct thorough data validation with business users.</li><li>**Legacy Access:** Retain read-only access to the legacy system for a defined period post-migration for historical reference and audit trails.</li></ul></p><p>**Staff training and support** are paramount for 400+ staff with differing practices. A phased, **role-based training** programme should be developed, directly linked to the deployment schedule. The council should identify and train \"superusers\" or departmental champions within each department to provide localised peer support. A dedicated post-go-live \'hypercare\' period with increased IT support will be essential to address immediate issues and build confidence.</p><p>In conclusion, Moorside Council should adopt a structured, hybrid approach. Leveraging Kotter\'s model for macro-level change leadership and ADKAR for individual readiness, alongside a robust CAB for governance. A phased deployment, supported by meticulous data migration and comprehensive, role-based training, offers the best balance of risk mitigation, continuity for critical public services, and successful user adoption within the 18-month deadline.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-08 17:55:53',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778260906797_mnm81ezw9',1,'2026-05-08 17:55:36','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-08 17:55:53',NULL),(1965,59,9,1,7,'<p>Computational thinking is putting real world problems into a computer to try find a solution</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-09 15:31:07',16,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define ˜computational thinking (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Computational thinking is putting real world problems into a computer to try find a solution</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a good start by identifying that computational thinking helps find solutions to real-world problems using a computer.</li><li>To make your definition stronger, consider explaining that it involves a *logical approach* to problem-solving.</li><li>Think about the key steps involved: it focuses on breaking down complex problems into smaller, more manageable parts.</li><li>A full definition should also mention that these solutions are expressed as *algorithms* that can then be coded.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on the *process* of computational thinking, focusing on how problems are broken down and prepared for computer processing using specific steps.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Computational thinking is a logical approach to problem-solving that involves breaking down complex problems into manageable parts so they can be expressed as algorithms. Key techniques include decomposition, pattern recognition, abstraction, and algorithmic design.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-09 15:31:13',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778340637234_xcd0mrdr8',1,'2026-05-09 15:31:07','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-09 15:31:13',NULL),(1966,59,9,1,7,'<p>Computational thinking is a logical problem solving technique when you break down large problems into smaller problems to create an algorithm. Some examples are abstraction and decomposition</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-09 15:32:03',35,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define ˜computational thinking (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Computational thinking is a logical problem solving technique when you break down large problems into smaller problems to create an algorithm. Some examples are abstraction and decomposition</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve done a great job explaining that computational thinking is a logical way to solve problems by breaking them into smaller parts and creating algorithms.</li><li>It\'s excellent that you included abstraction and decomposition as key examples of this process.</li><li>To make your answer even more comprehensive, try to also include \'pattern recognition\' and \'algorithmic design\' as essential components.</li><li>You could also briefly mention that this approach prepares problems for computer processing or \'coding\'.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, aim to include all four key components of computational thinking: decomposition, pattern recognition, abstraction, and algorithmic design.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Computational thinking is a logical approach to problem-solving which involves breaking down complex problems into smaller, manageable parts. It uses techniques like decomposition, pattern recognition, abstraction, and algorithmic design to express solutions as algorithms, making them suitable for computer execution.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-09 15:32:11',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778340637234_xcd0mrdr8',2,'2026-05-09 15:32:03','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-09 15:32:11',NULL),(1967,59,22,1,7,'<p>Emerging technologies are changing software development significantly as AI can now be used to write code however it often has many errors within the code so will usually need an actual programmer to look over and debug the code/program. IoTs also affect software development by making sure the programs and software are compatible with the new IoTs that arise as new technology emerges.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-09 15:35:39',186,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how emerging technologies such as AI and IoT are changing software development. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Emerging technologies are changing software development significantly as AI can now be used to write code however it often has many errors within the code so will usually need an actual programmer to look over and debug the code/program. IoTs also affect software development by making sure the programs and software are compatible with the new IoTs that arise as new technology emerges.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that AI can assist with writing code. To strengthen this point, consider how AI also helps with automation in other areas like testing, or enables predictive functionalities within software, leading to increased efficiency.</li><li>You mentioned the need for IoT compatibility. To develop this further, think about how IoT devices specifically change the *type* of software developed, such as requiring data collection, real-time processing, or remote control features.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, discuss the broader impacts, including both the benefits (e.g., efficiency, innovation) and potential drawbacks (e.g., privacy, security) that these technologies introduce to software development.</li><li>Consider how these emerging technologies require developers to adapt their coding practices, for example, by focusing on distributed systems or real-time data handling.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Expand on the specific impacts of AI and IoT, detailing how they lead to benefits like efficiency or innovation, and new challenges like privacy and security, for software developers.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>AI is significantly changing software development by automating tasks like code generation and testing, which can lead to increased efficiency. It also enables the creation of predictive systems within applications. IoT impacts development by requiring software to handle vast amounts of real-time data from connected devices and support remote control functionalities. This necessitates developers to adapt to new paradigms, focusing on distributed systems, real-time data processing, and addressing new challenges related to privacy and security within these interconnected environments.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-09 15:35:47',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778340637234_xcd0mrdr8',1,'2026-05-09 15:35:39','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-09 15:35:47',NULL),(1968,59,179,1,7,'<p>A boolean operator changes a boolean value. For example the AND operator checks two boolean values and if they are both inputs are True then the output will be True any other input combination will result in a False. The NOT operator simply just switches the input to the opposite value in the output so if the input was True the output would be False</p>',NULL,'2026-05-09 15:37:57',115,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State what a Boolean operator does. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>A boolean operator changes a boolean value. For example the AND operator checks two boolean values and if they are both inputs are True then the output will be True any other input combination will result in a False. The NOT operator simply just switches the input to the opposite value in the output so if the input was True the output would be False</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve done a fantastic job of describing how AND and NOT operators work, which shows a strong understanding of their functionality and the True/False results they produce.</li><li>You clearly demonstrated that these operators produce True/False outputs through your accurate examples.</li><li>To fully meet the mark scheme, consider explicitly stating that Boolean operators perform \"logical comparisons\" as their primary function.</li><li>Mentioning the OR operator alongside AND and NOT would further strengthen your answer by providing a more comprehensive set of examples.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, start by defining the core purpose of a Boolean operator—to perform logical comparisons—before providing examples of how specific operators work.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A Boolean operator performs logical comparisons between values, typically producing a True or False result. Examples include AND, OR, and NOT, which evaluate conditions to determine an outcome.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-09 15:38:05',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778340637234_xcd0mrdr8',1,'2026-05-09 15:37:57','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-05-13 15:27:19',1),(1969,59,92,1,7,'<p>Equality and Diversity legislations for software teams are important to make sure people are excluded or attacked within software teams. This makes sure everyone has a fair chance of being on the team and isn\'t subjected to any offences within or outside the team. This could be beneficial to the team as this prevents someone who is extremely good at programming from being excluded from the team just because they are a minority or any other protected characteristic of the Equality Act</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-09 15:48:47',413,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the importance of equality and diversity legislation for software teams. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Equality and Diversity legislations for software teams are important to make sure people are excluded or attacked within software teams. This makes sure everyone has a fair chance of being on the team and isn\'t subjected to any offences within or outside the team. This could be beneficial to the team as this prevents someone who is extremely good at programming from being excluded from the team just because they are a minority or any other protected characteristic of the Equality Act</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve clearly explained how equality and diversity legislation prevents discrimination and ensures fair treatment within software teams, which is a strong starting point.</li><li>You provided a good example of preventing exclusion based on protected characteristics, showing a good understanding of the Equality Act.</li><li>To strengthen your answer further, consider how diverse teams can lead to more innovative and higher-quality software products.</li><li>Next time, try to connect the legislation\'s importance to the creation of accessible digital solutions that benefit a wider range of users.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Expand on how a diverse team directly contributes to the quality and accessibility of the software products being developed, beyond just the internal team benefits.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Equality and diversity legislation is crucial for software teams as it ensures fair treatment and prevents discrimination, allowing teams to recruit the best talent from all backgrounds. This fosters an inclusive work environment where diverse perspectives and experiences are valued. By embracing a wide range of viewpoints, teams are better equipped to identify unconscious biases, develop more inclusive designs, and create higher-quality software solutions that are accessible and relevant to a broader user base. This ultimately leads to more innovative products and a stronger competitive advantage.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-09 15:48:53',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1778340637234_xcd0mrdr8',1,'2026-05-09 15:48:47','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-05-13 15:26:50',1),(1970,59,177,1,7,'<p>An array contains values that can change a dictionary contains values that cannot</p>',NULL,'2026-05-09 15:57:16',28,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Identify one difference between an array and a dictionary. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>An array contains values that can change a dictionary contains values that cannot</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made an attempt to distinguish between the two, which is a great start!</li><li>To earn full marks, focus on the fundamental structural differences. Consider how items are stored and referenced in an array compared to a dictionary.</li><li>Think about the primary method used to access individual elements in an array (e.g., using numbers) and how that differs from a dictionary.</li><li>It\'s worth noting that in most programming languages, both arrays and dictionaries allow their values to be changed after creation.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, focus on describing how data is organised and accessed within each data structure, rather than whether the stored values can be modified.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An array stores a collection of data in a specific order, typically accessed using a numerical index, while a dictionary stores data as unordered key-value pairs, accessed by a unique key.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-09 15:57:25',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1778340637234_xcd0mrdr8',1,'2026-05-09 15:57:16','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Try again.</p>','R','2026-05-13 15:25:57',1),(1971,59,177,1,7,'<p>An array stores values in a numerical index and can be accessed using a index key whereas a dictionary stores values in an ordered group</p>',NULL,'2026-05-09 16:00:57',190,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Identify one difference between an array and a dictionary. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>An array stores values in a numerical index and can be accessed using a index key whereas a dictionary stores values in an ordered group</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that arrays store values in a numerical index, which is a key part of their structure. Well done for accurately describing this aspect!</li><li>For dictionaries, you mentioned they store values in an \"ordered group,\" but you could be more specific about how this data is organised. Think about what makes a dictionary different from a simple list or array in terms of access.</li><li>To improve your answer, focus on the unique way dictionaries store and retrieve data, which isn\'t just about order but about specific identifiers.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly state that dictionaries store data using key-value pairs, which are used for accessing the stored values.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An array stores data sequentially using a numerical index, whereas a dictionary stores data as key-value pairs, allowing access to values via unique keys.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-09 16:01:04',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1778340637234_xcd0mrdr8',2,'2026-05-09 16:00:57','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Key-Pair is what I am really looking for in dictionaries</p>','R','2026-05-13 15:23:23',1),(1972,59,177,1,7,'<p>An array access its stores values using numerical index keys whereas dictionaries assign values key pairs and access them using specific key values</p>',NULL,'2026-05-09 16:02:47',57,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Identify one difference between an array and a dictionary. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>An array access its stores values using numerical index keys whereas dictionaries assign values key pairs and access them using specific key values</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully identified that arrays use numerical indices to access their stored values. Great start!</li><li>You also correctly explained that dictionaries utilize key-value pairs for accessing data.</li><li>You clearly highlighted a key difference between these two data structures.</li><li>Consider refining your wording slightly for even greater precision, for example, by saying arrays \"store values accessible by numerical index\".</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Focus on making your explanation slightly more concise while maintaining clarity, perhaps by using \"store data\" rather than \"access its stores values\".</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Arrays store data sequentially and are accessed by a numerical index, while dictionaries store data as unordered key-value pairs and are accessed using a unique key.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-09 16:02:52',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1778340637234_xcd0mrdr8',3,'2026-05-09 16:02:47','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-05-13 15:22:46',1),(1973,80,202,1,7,'<p>legislation such as GDPR make organisations responsible to keep customer data safe and secure this means that they can\'t sell data or store it with improper procedures. This means that people using services don\'t have to worry about their personal information being leaked for all to see.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-10 17:14:33',244,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Assess how legislation such as GDPR shapes organisational responsibility for digital data. (8 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>legislation such as GDPR make organisations responsible to keep customer data safe and secure this means that they can\'t sell data or store it with improper procedures. This means that people using services don\'t have to worry about their personal information being leaked for all to see.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that GDPR makes organisations responsible for keeping data safe and secure, which is a key aspect of accountability. To enhance this, consider specific ways organisations demonstrate this accountability, such as through data protection officers.</li><li>To improve your answer, include specific GDPR principles like the requirement for explicit user consent before processing data. Think about how this directly impacts what organisations can do with personal information.</li><li>Your response could be strengthened by discussing the rights individuals have under GDPR, such as the right to access, rectify, or erase their data. Organisations have a responsibility to facilitate these rights.</li><li>You touched on \"improper procedures,\" which relates to compliance. For a stronger answer, it\'s important to also mention the potential penalties or fines organisations face for non-compliance with GDPR regulations.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, ensure you include specific examples of individual rights under GDPR, such as the right to consent and the right to access, as these are central to organisational responsibility.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>GDPR significantly shapes organisational responsibility by requiring explicit user consent for data processing and empowering individuals with rights such as access, rectification, and erasure of their personal information. Organisations must implement robust technical and organisational security measures, demonstrate accountability through data protection impact assessments, and maintain records of processing activities. Compliance is mandatory, and organisations face severe financial penalties, up to millions of Euros or a percentage of global annual turnover, for violations. This drives organisations to embed data protection into their core practices and culture, ensuring ethical and legal handling of digital data.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-10 17:14:41',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778433013603_tsxrfro4a',1,'2026-05-10 17:14:33','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-05-13 15:22:25',1),(1974,85,1064,1,33,'<p>Prestige Finance should consider air-gapping their data centres instead of storing all data in one physical location such that if one department is infected, a smaller amount of sensitive financial data is at risk as opposed to a department being infected and all the data the company stores is at risk.</p><p>Prestige Finance should consider taking the approach to train their employees on the indicators of a phishing email and best security practices to ensure there is a lower risk of their employees clicking phishing links allowing attackers to potentially infiltrate the network and steal sensitive data. In addition to this, Prestige must look at implementing better security in their system to ensure that even if an employee clicks on a link, there is a minimal chance of the attacker gaining the privileges required to encrypt the companies data and potentially affecting the availability of systems for the 200k+ customers. This can be done by implementing a hardware firewall monitoring both incoming and outgoing connections and blocking anything filtered as a threat, and RBAC (Role-based-access-controls) to only assign the specific roles (admin, regular user) to the users/employees requiring those specific roles to prevent the event of privilege escalation. </p><p>Prestige Finance, given there untested backup systems and long duration it took to restore the data should also consider implementing an incremental backup system where each change/modification to files on the system are saved automatically so in the event their backup systems are not tested for a while, at least they have automatic incremental backups running in the background.</p><p>However, Implementing any of these methods requires regulatory compliance from the FCA potentially limiting what they can and cannot implement. </p><p>These changes will also cost Prestige Finance a lot of money as they will also likely need a change management board (CAB) to oversee and assist in navigating from their current single-site infrastructure to multiple data centres as if not done correctly, could not only cost them lots of money but also affect potential uptime of their systems as which has already been mentioned, positions Prestige Finance in high-risk of reputational damage which is still on-going.</p><p>Prestige Finance also do not yet know whether any customer data in the breach was affected which must be found out immediately to ensure that they are not at risk of additional GDPR fines of which will limit their budget in how much they can likely spend on these changes.</p><p>In conclusion, Prestige Finance after checking their data stored to ensure no customer data has been exfiltrated, should migrate their single site infrastructure storing all of their data to multiple different data backup locations to limit the event of a single intrusion leading to an attacker gaining access to all of their data, In addition to implementing incremental backups to ensure new changes are saved automatically preventing any data from being lost or poisoned.  </p>',NULL,'2026-05-11 08:09:35',1599,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Prestige Finance Ltd is a financial services company providing personal loans to over 200,000 customers. The company recently suffered a ransomware attack that encrypted its customer database and brought down its online application portal for 72 hours. Investigation revealed the attackers gained entry via a phishing email that was opened by a member of the finance team. No customer data was confirmed to have been exfiltrated, but this cannot be ruled out. </p><p>The board is now under pressure from the Financial Conduct Authority (FCA) to demonstrate that adequate security measures are in place. The company\'s backup system had not been tested in over a year, and the restore process took far longer than expected. The company operates from a single physical data centre. </p><p><strong>Key constraints: </strong>regulatory scrutiny from the FCA, 200,000+ customers affected by downtime, untested backup systems, single site infrastructure, reputational damage ongoing. </p><p><em>Evaluate the security risks faced by Prestige Finance Ltd and assess the methods the company should implement to improve the resilience of its digital environment and prevent future incidents of this nature.</em></p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Prestige Finance should consider air-gapping their data centres instead of storing all data in one physical location such that if one department is infected, a smaller amount of sensitive financial data is at risk as opposed to a department being infected and all the data the company stores is at risk.</p><p>Prestige Finance should consider taking the approach to train their employees on the indicators of a phishing email and best security practices to ensure there is a lower risk of their employees clicking phishing links allowing attackers to potentially infiltrate the network and steal sensitive data. In addition to this, Prestige must look at implementing better security in their system to ensure that even if an employee clicks on a link, there is a minimal chance of the attacker gaining the privileges required to encrypt the companies data and potentially affecting the availability of systems for the 200k+ customers. This can be done by implementing a hardware firewall monitoring both incoming and outgoing connections and blocking anything filtered as a threat, and RBAC (Role-based-access-controls) to only assign the specific roles (admin, regular user) to the users/employees requiring those specific roles to prevent the event of privilege escalation. </p><p>Prestige Finance, given there untested backup systems and long duration it took to restore the data should also consider implementing an incremental backup system where each change/modification to files on the system are saved automatically so in the event their backup systems are not tested for a while, at least they have automatic incremental backups running in the background.</p><p>However, Implementing any of these methods requires regulatory compliance from the FCA potentially limiting what they can and cannot implement. </p><p>These changes will also cost Prestige Finance a lot of money as they will also likely need a change management board (CAB) to oversee and assist in navigating from their current single-site infrastructure to multiple data centres as if not done correctly, could not only cost them lots of money but also affect potential uptime of their systems as which has already been mentioned, positions Prestige Finance in high-risk of reputational damage which is still on-going.</p><p>Prestige Finance also do not yet know whether any customer data in the breach was affected which must be found out immediately to ensure that they are not at risk of additional GDPR fines of which will limit their budget in how much they can likely spend on these changes.</p><p>In conclusion, Prestige Finance after checking their data stored to ensure no customer data has been exfiltrated, should migrate their single site infrastructure storing all of their data to multiple different data backup locations to limit the event of a single intrusion leading to an attacker gaining access to all of their data, In addition to implementing incremental backups to ensure new changes are saved automatically preventing any data from being lost or poisoned.  </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified the importance of employee training and Role-Based Access Controls (RBAC) to mitigate phishing risks, which is excellent. To further strengthen prevention, consider implementing Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) for all accounts.</li><li>Your point about air-gapping data or using multiple locations is a good step towards addressing the single data centre risk. For comprehensive resilience, research dedicated Disaster Recovery (DR) sites or cloud-based failover solutions to ensure business continuity.</li><li>You rightly highlighted the need for better backups. To prevent extended downtime like the 72 hours experienced, regular *testing* of your restore process is critical, and explore immutable backups to protect against ransomware.</li><li>You thoughtfully considered the impact of regulatory compliance and cost. Remember that the FCA primarily *mandates* robust operational resilience measures rather than limiting their implementation.</li><li>You considered the risk of GDPR fines if data was exfiltrated, showing good awareness of regulatory consequences. To prevent lateral movement within the network, implementing network segmentation would be a very effective control.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>To significantly boost resilience and avoid prolonged downtime, ensure your backup strategy includes regular, tested restore procedures and considers immutable backups to protect against ransomware encryption.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Prestige Finance Ltd faces several critical security risks. The initial attack vector was a phishing email, highlighting a significant human factor vulnerability. This led to a ransomware attack, which encrypted the customer database and caused 72 hours of downtime, severely impacting their 200,000+ customers and causing reputational damage. The fact that the attackers could move from a finance team member\'s machine to the customer database suggests inadequate network segmentation. The single physical data centre represents a single point of failure, and the untested backup system directly contributed to the extended recovery time, making the company highly vulnerable to disruption. The potential for data exfiltration also poses a significant GDPR compliance risk and further FCA scrutiny.</p><p>To improve resilience and prevent future incidents, Prestige Finance should implement a multi-faceted approach:</p><p><strong>Prevention Measures:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Enhanced Email Security:</strong> Implement advanced anti-phishing filters, DMARC/SPF/DKIM records, and sandboxing for email attachments to block malicious emails before they reach users.</li><li><strong>Robust Staff Training:</strong> Conduct regular, mandatory security awareness training, including simulated phishing exercises, to improve staff\'s ability to identify and report suspicious emails. Foster a culture of security awareness.</li><li><strong>Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA):</strong> Deploy MFA across all user accounts to prevent unauthorised access, even if credentials are compromised via phishing.</li><li><strong>Network Segmentation:</strong> Implement network segmentation (e.g., micro-segmentation) to isolate critical systems like the customer database from less sensitive areas. This would limit lateral movement of ransomware if an endpoint is compromised.</li><li><strong>Principle of Least Privilege (RBAC):</strong> Ensure user accounts, particularly for non-IT staff like the finance team, have only the minimum necessary permissions to perform their job functions, preventing widespread damage from a compromised account.</li><li><strong>Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR):</strong> Deploy EDR solutions to monitor endpoints for suspicious activity and automatically contain threats like ransomware before they spread.</li></ul><p><strong>Resilience and Recovery:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Comprehensive Backup Strategy:</strong> Implement the 3-2-1 backup rule (3 copies, 2 different media, 1 offsite/cloud). Crucially, incorporate *immutable backups* that cannot be altered or deleted by ransomware, and ensure at least one copy is air-gapped.</li><li><strong>Regular Backup Testing:</strong> Conduct frequent, simulated restore exercises to verify backups are viable and that the recovery process meets defined Recovery Time Objectives (RTO) and Recovery Point Objectives (RPO). The 72-hour downtime highlights a critical failure in this area.</li><li><strong>Disaster Recovery (DR) Site:</strong> Establish a secondary physical or cloud-based disaster recovery site to provide failover capability for critical systems, addressing the single data centre vulnerability. This ensures business continuity even if the primary site is compromised.</li><li><strong>Business Continuity Plan (BCP):</strong> Develop and regularly test a comprehensive BCP detailing procedures for maintaining essential business functions during and after a major security incident.</li></ul><p><strong>Regulatory Compliance:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>FCA Operational Resilience:</strong> Prestige Finance must demonstrate to the FCA that it has identified its important business services and set clear impact tolerances for disruption, which the 72-hour outage likely exceeded. Implementing the above resilience measures is key to satisfying PS21/3.</li><li><strong>GDPR Compliance:</strong> If data exfiltration is confirmed, Prestige Finance must immediately notify the ICO within 72 hours and inform affected customers, demonstrating compliance with Article 33/34 of GDPR.</li></ul><p>In conclusion, Prestige Finance must move beyond ad-hoc security and implement a robust framework encompassing both preventative measures (like enhanced email security, MFA, and network segmentation) and comprehensive resilience strategies (including tested, immutable backups and a DR site). Addressing the human factor through training and limiting privileges will be as crucial as technical controls. This holistic approach, aligned with FCA operational resilience mandates, will significantly improve their digital environment\'s security posture and rebuild trust.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-11 08:09:58',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778484745287_mph9u1cab',1,'2026-05-11 08:09:35','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-05-13 15:22:08',1),(1975,155,1077,1,34,'<p>One benefit of commissioning bespoke software for a business is that it is tailored to the business for their exact needs. This means that no features that are wanted from the software need to be implemented into another piece of software and saves money for using another piece of software.</p><p></p><p>Another benefit of commissioning bespoke software for a business is that the business does not need to teach the users of the business how to use another software - this in result saves time and money for employees as they can do all the tasks they need in the bespoke software.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-11 11:30:26',311,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain <strong>two</strong> benefits of commissioning <strong>bespoke software</strong> for a business.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>One benefit of commissioning bespoke software for a business is that it is tailored to the business for their exact needs. This means that no features that are wanted from the software need to be implemented into another piece of software and saves money for using another piece of software.</p><p></p><p>Another benefit of commissioning bespoke software for a business is that the business does not need to teach the users of the business how to use another software - this in result saves time and money for employees as they can do all the tasks they need in the bespoke software.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully identified and explained two distinct benefits of commissioning bespoke software, which is great!</li><li>Your first benefit about tailoring the software to exact needs is clearly explained and directly relevant to the advantages of bespoke solutions.</li><li>The second benefit you discussed, relating to reduced training for users, is a thoughtful point and well-justified in terms of saving time and money.</li><li>To enhance your answer further, consider explicitly linking the \'tailored to exact needs\' point to how it precisely fits existing workflows or avoids unnecessary features.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>For your first point, you could elaborate slightly more on *how* being tailored to exact needs leads to cost savings beyond just not needing other software, perhaps by mentioning increased efficiency or avoiding redundant features.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>One benefit of commissioning bespoke software is that it is precisely tailored to a business\'s exact requirements. This means the software will include only the features the business needs, fitting their specific workflows perfectly, which can increase efficiency and avoid the costs associated with unused features found in off-the-shelf solutions.</p><p>Another benefit is that bespoke software can be designed for seamless integration with a business\'s existing systems. This allows for smoother data flow and operations between different applications, preventing compatibility issues and reducing the need for manual data transfer or workarounds.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-11 11:30:34',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1778498744228_x7n32icqf',1,'2026-05-11 11:30:26','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-05-13 15:21:51',1),(1976,165,1144,1,34,'<p>IPV4 uses 32-bit numeric addresses which are exhausted whereas, IPV6 uses 128-bit alphanumeric addresses</p>',NULL,'2026-05-12 13:08:09',149,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the purpose of an <strong>IP address</strong> and describe the difference between <strong>IPv4</strong> and <strong>IPv6</strong>.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>IPV4 uses 32-bit numeric addresses which are exhausted whereas, IPV6 uses 128-bit alphanumeric addresses</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that IPv4 uses 32-bit addresses and that they are becoming exhausted, and that IPv6 uses 128-bit addresses. That\'s a great start on distinguishing between the two versions!</li><li>To strengthen your answer, remember to explain the fundamental purpose of an IP address itself before diving into the differences. Think about why devices on a network need them.</li><li>While you mentioned \"alphanumeric\" for IPv6, consider adding more specific details about its format (e.g., hexadecimal) and the huge number of addresses it provides compared to IPv4.</li><li>For a more complete explanation of the differences, you could also include an example of each address type to illustrate their format.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, start by explaining the primary purpose of an IP address – how it helps devices communicate on a network – before detailing the differences between IPv4 and IPv6.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An IP address is a unique numerical label assigned to every device on a network, used to identify the source and destination of data packets so routers can forward information to the correct device.</p><p>IPv4 uses 32-bit addresses (e.g., 192.168.1.1) and supports about 4.3 billion unique addresses, which are now largely exhausted. IPv6 uses 128-bit addresses, often expressed in hexadecimal groups separated by colons (e.g., 2001:0db8:85a3::8a2e:0370:7334), providing an astronomically larger number of unique addresses (approximately 3.4 x 10^38). IPv6 was developed to overcome IPv4\'s address exhaustion and also offers improvements in routing efficiency and built-in security features.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-12 13:08:17',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1778591094849_zlrgoy0tm',1,'2026-05-12 13:08:09','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>WHY do we need IPv6 now?</p>','R','2026-05-13 15:21:31',1),(1977,85,1057,1,33,'<p>ClearVision Retail must consider the potential impacts of using AI and Machine Learning to train their LLM models on detecting potential shoplifters, as by training their models they will require vast amount\'s of customer data such as face\'s and body movements to feed into the LLM to make more accurate decisions on detecting potential shop-lifters which if not agreed upon with the customers may be a breach of their privacy potentially violating GDPR and other data protection regulations.</p><p>ClearVision Retail also mentioned how using AI in their systems would lead to them forecasting stock demand and reducing waste which while is true in how AI can lead to making better informed decisions on data allowing it to predict, they cannot rule out the potential inaccuracies when using AI to predict stock demand as this would have serious consequences such as leading ClearVision to falsely interpret data such as customer favourite stock which may see them stocking up on least favourite products, running out of the customer favourite\'s which could damage ongoing customer expenditure leading them to lose money and worsen their reputation. </p><p>ClearVision given their constraint on significant investment, must take into account the costs of training an LLM as well as integrating AI into their systems as given they are a mid-sized retailer, the infrastructure and GPU\'s required to train their LLM\'s on the gathered data will be up in the thousands of pounds for price especially considering they have 45 different stores which each require the integration of AI into their systems (CCTV cameras) and software.</p><p>ClearVision when integrating AI into their systems however will see them competing at the top of the market with other fashion retailers who have started to or already integrated AI into their systems which could give ClearVision a competitive advantage compared to the retailers not integrating AI and the latest technologies into their systems, since regardless of potential inaccuracies in AI interpreted data, the majority of insights will provide ClearVision with new perspectives on what works best and what doesn\'t allowing them to improve their feedback loops and gain a significant advantage on their best selling products.</p><p>AI powered CCTV systems will allow ClearVision to cut down on shoplifters potentially saving them money in the long-term by reducing the amount of shop-lifters stealing their products and increasing security at the stores identified as high-targets.</p><p>In conclusion, ClearVision should adopt AI into their systems, but only in the case they have a suitable allocated budget for short-term expenditure\'s and explicit permission from the specific customers they want to use to train their LLM\'s on to make them more accurate in identifying/prosecuting shop-lifters. AI integrated systems will also allow ClearVision to further predict and forecast stock demand which will give them a significant advantage in the fashion retailer market, however they should always double verify the insights gathered from AI on data to ensure it is credible and reliable for use.</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-12 15:59:48',1488,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>ClearVision Retail is a mid-sized fashion retailer with 45 stores and a growing e-commerce presence. The board is exploring the use of artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning to improve its operations. </p><p>Proposals under consideration include: using generative AI to produce product descriptions and marketing copy; using machine learning to forecast stock demand and reduce waste; and deploying AI-powered CCTV to detect shoplifting. </p><p>Some members of the board are enthusiastic about the potential cost savings and competitive advantage. Others are concerned about the ethical implications, the reliability of AI-generated content and the impact on staff roles. The IT director has highlighted risks around data bias and privacy. </p><p><strong>Key constraints: </strong>significant investment required, ethical concerns from staff and customers, potential regulatory issues, existing customer data could be used to train models. </p><p><em>Evaluate the potential impacts of adopting AI and machine learning technologies at ClearVision Retail, considering the benefits and risks for the organisation, its staff and its customers.</em></p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>ClearVision Retail must consider the potential impacts of using AI and Machine Learning to train their LLM models on detecting potential shoplifters, as by training their models they will require vast amount\'s of customer data such as face\'s and body movements to feed into the LLM to make more accurate decisions on detecting potential shop-lifters which if not agreed upon with the customers may be a breach of their privacy potentially violating GDPR and other data protection regulations.</p><p>ClearVision Retail also mentioned how using AI in their systems would lead to them forecasting stock demand and reducing waste which while is true in how AI can lead to making better informed decisions on data allowing it to predict, they cannot rule out the potential inaccuracies when using AI to predict stock demand as this would have serious consequences such as leading ClearVision to falsely interpret data such as customer favourite stock which may see them stocking up on least favourite products, running out of the customer favourite\'s which could damage ongoing customer expenditure leading them to lose money and worsen their reputation. </p><p>ClearVision given their constraint on significant investment, must take into account the costs of training an LLM as well as integrating AI into their systems as given they are a mid-sized retailer, the infrastructure and GPU\'s required to train their LLM\'s on the gathered data will be up in the thousands of pounds for price especially considering they have 45 different stores which each require the integration of AI into their systems (CCTV cameras) and software.</p><p>ClearVision when integrating AI into their systems however will see them competing at the top of the market with other fashion retailers who have started to or already integrated AI into their systems which could give ClearVision a competitive advantage compared to the retailers not integrating AI and the latest technologies into their systems, since regardless of potential inaccuracies in AI interpreted data, the majority of insights will provide ClearVision with new perspectives on what works best and what doesn\'t allowing them to improve their feedback loops and gain a significant advantage on their best selling products.</p><p>AI powered CCTV systems will allow ClearVision to cut down on shoplifters potentially saving them money in the long-term by reducing the amount of shop-lifters stealing their products and increasing security at the stores identified as high-targets.</p><p>In conclusion, ClearVision should adopt AI into their systems, but only in the case they have a suitable allocated budget for short-term expenditure\'s and explicit permission from the specific customers they want to use to train their LLM\'s on to make them more accurate in identifying/prosecuting shop-lifters. AI integrated systems will also allow ClearVision to further predict and forecast stock demand which will give them a significant advantage in the fashion retailer market, however they should always double verify the insights gathered from AI on data to ensure it is credible and reliable for use.</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You effectively evaluated the impacts of ML for stock forecasting and AI CCTV for shoplifting, including both benefits and risks for the organisation and customers. Well done for discussing GDPR in relation to AI CCTV.</li><li>To improve your evaluation, remember to discuss *all three* proposals mentioned in the question. You focused mainly on stock forecasting and CCTV, but the generative AI for marketing content was largely overlooked.</li><li>You clearly covered the impacts on ClearVision as an organisation and its customers. Next time, make sure to also explicitly discuss the potential impacts on *staff roles* as mentioned in the scenario, such as job displacement or reskilling needs.</li><li>Your conclusion provided a balanced recommendation by considering the significant investment required, which showed good application to the scenario\'s constraints. Keep linking your points directly to the specific details of ClearVision Retail.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4>Ensure you address all three AI proposals and all three stakeholder groups (organisation, staff, customers) explicitly in your evaluation to achieve a comprehensive response.<h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Adopting AI and machine learning at ClearVision Retail presents significant opportunities and challenges across the organisation, staff, and customers. </p><p><strong>Generative AI for Product Descriptions & Marketing Copy:</strong>\n*   <strong>Benefits (Organisation):</strong> Faster content production, reduced copywriting costs, and consistent brand messaging across 45 stores and e-commerce.\n*   <strong>Risks (Organisation/Customers):</strong> Potential for AI \"hallucinations\" leading to inaccurate product claims (legal/regulatory risk under ASA standards), loss of authentic brand voice, and customer mistrust if content is perceived as inauthentic. Copyright concerns could arise from training data. </p><p><strong>ML for Stock Forecasting:</strong>\n*   <strong>Benefits (Organisation/Customers):</strong> Reduced waste and improved profitability through more accurate stock levels, leading to better product availability for customers.\n*   <strong>Risks (Organisation/Staff/Customers):</strong> Model accuracy heavily depends on quality and volume of historical data; bias in training data (e.g., from COVID-affected periods) could lead to poor predictions, resulting in overstocking unwanted items or shortages of popular ones, impacting sales and customer satisfaction. Significant investment in data infrastructure is required. For staff, this may reduce demand for traditional buying/merchandising roles or require extensive reskilling. </p><p><strong>AI-powered CCTV for Shoplifting:</strong>\n*   <strong>Benefits (Organisation):</strong> Potential reduction in stock loss, leading to increased profitability and reduced reliance on security staff in the long term. Real-time alerts can improve response times.\n*   <strong>Risks (Organisation/Staff/Customers):</strong> Algorithmic bias is a significant risk; if trained on biased data, the system could disproportionately flag certain demographics, leading to false accusations and potential liability under the Equality Act 2010. This could severely damage ClearVision\'s reputation and lead to customer distrust. Privacy is a major concern: continuous biometric-style processing requires a clear lawful basis under UK GDPR, and transparent communication with customers is essential. False positives could lead to wrongly accusing innocent customers, resulting in legal action and reputational harm. Staff may also feel under increased surveillance.</p><p><strong>Cross-Cutting Impacts:</strong>\n*   <strong>Investment & ROI:</strong> All proposals require significant upfront investment in technology and training, which needs careful cost-benefit analysis.\n*   <strong>Data Bias & Privacy:</strong> The IT director\'s concerns are valid across the board; using existing customer data to train models requires robust data governance and adherence to GDPR principles.\n*   <strong>Staff Impact:</strong> A key ethical concern is potential staff displacement across all three areas, requiring ClearVision to plan for reskilling, redeployment, or redundancy with sensitivity.\n*   <strong>Regulation:</strong> While UK AI regulation is evolving, compliance with existing laws like GDPR, Equality Act, and advertising standards is crucial. </p><p><strong>Conclusion:</strong> ClearVision should proceed cautiously, starting with a pilot phase for ML stock forecasting where the benefits are clear and risks, while present, are more manageable. AI CCTV offers security benefits but carries high ethical and legal risks related to bias and privacy, necessitating a robust legitimate interest assessment and transparent public communication. Generative AI for content could be beneficial but requires careful oversight to maintain brand authenticity and accuracy. Addressing staff concerns through training and transparent communication will be vital for successful adoption across all initiatives.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-12 16:00:06',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1778599918804_0t903cirf',1,'2026-05-12 15:59:48','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>This is comprehensive, but you took a long time on it.</p>','A','2026-05-13 15:20:46',1),(1978,85,76,1,7,'<p>Modularisation allows programs/systems to be broken down into specific modules allowing developers/staff to be assigned to specific individual modules which can increase flexibility during development. However, modularisation can have result in performance trade-offs such as communicating across different modules.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 13:35:18',173,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe one advantage and one disadvantage of modularisation in programming. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Modularisation allows programs/systems to be broken down into specific modules allowing developers/staff to be assigned to specific individual modules which can increase flexibility during development. However, modularisation can have result in performance trade-offs such as communicating across different modules.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly identified a valid advantage of modularisation, highlighting how it supports team development and increases flexibility.</li><li>Your explanation of a disadvantage, focusing on performance trade-offs due to inter-module communication, was accurate and well-articulated.</li><li>To make your advantage even stronger, consider also including how modularisation directly aids in making code easier to test or maintain.</li><li>You could also expand on the disadvantage by mentioning the increased design complexity when modules need to interact, beyond just performance.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>When describing advantages, try to include classic benefits like improved maintainability or reusability to broaden your answer.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An advantage of modularisation is that it makes a program easier to test and maintain, as issues can often be isolated to a specific module. A disadvantage is that it can add complexity, particularly when modules need to communicate or share data, requiring careful design of their interfaces.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 13:35:28',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779370154104_jcc3btfbh',1,'2026-05-21 13:35:18','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 13:35:28',NULL),(1979,83,89,1,7,'<p>Artificial intelligence is when a computer program behaves in a way that is more related to an actual human being. For example, in a regular search, a single character being off may stop a result from appearing, as the computer sees this as a completely different value. In an AI powered search however, the system may not behave purely logically, and may be able to recognize what the user is attempting to do.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:04:27',140,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define the term artificial intelligence in the context of emerging issues. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Artificial intelligence is when a computer program behaves in a way that is more related to an actual human being. For example, in a regular search, a single character being off may stop a result from appearing, as the computer sees this as a completely different value. In an AI powered search however, the system may not behave purely logically, and may be able to recognize what the user is attempting to do.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by defining AI as computer programs that behave in a human-like way, and your example clearly illustrates this concept of understanding user intent.</li><li>To strengthen your definition, try to specify that AI involves *systems performing tasks* that typically require human intelligence, rather than just behaving.</li><li>Consider including specific examples of such tasks, like decision-making or pattern recognition, as these are core functions of AI.</li><li>For a more complete answer, you could also briefly mention the growing application of AI in areas like automation or software development.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state that AI systems perform *tasks* that normally require human intelligence, such as decision-making or pattern recognition.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Artificial intelligence refers to systems that perform tasks normally requiring human intelligence, such as problem-solving, decision-making, or pattern recognition. It is increasingly used in automation and software development.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:04:35',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779371998716_cegqx36z1',1,'2026-05-21 14:04:27','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:04:35',NULL),(1980,81,75,1,7,'<p>abstraction is a computational thinking method used for problem solving, it is the process of identifying the important parts of the task and removing unnecessary  information to simplify a problem</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:06:37',168,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>What is meant by abstraction in computational thinking?. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p><p>abstraction is a computational thinking method used for problem solving, it is the process of identifying the important parts of the task and removing unnecessary  information to simplify a problem</p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that abstraction involves removing unnecessary information to simplify a problem, which is excellent!</li><li>You also clearly explained the purpose of focusing on the important parts of a task, demonstrating a strong understanding of the concept.</li><li>Your response aligns very well with the key points expected for a high-quality answer.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Your answer is already very good! For future questions, always aim to be as concise as possible while retaining all key information.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Abstraction is the process of simplifying a complex problem by removing unnecessary details and focusing only on the essential, relevant information.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:06:42',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779372215483_nu258yy70',1,'2026-05-21 14:06:37','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:06:42',NULL),(1981,85,96,1,7,'<p>Comments are used in Python programs and in other languages as they provide an explanation of what certain lines of code/functions do upon execution improving user readability without disrupting the flow of execution on runtime.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:07:38',82,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain why comments are used in Python programs. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Comments are used in Python programs and in other languages as they provide an explanation of what certain lines of code/functions do upon execution improving user readability without disrupting the flow of execution on runtime.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly explained that comments provide an explanation of what certain lines of code or functions do, which is a key purpose.</li><li>It was great that you mentioned comments improve user readability, making the code easier to understand for anyone reading it.</li><li>You also rightly pointed out that comments do not disrupt the flow of execution on runtime, showing a good understanding of their non-functional nature.</li><li>To achieve a stronger response, consider expanding on how comments help *other* developers maintain, debug, or extend a program in the future.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on the collaborative aspect of comments, explaining how they are crucial for team projects or when revisiting code, enabling others to understand and work with the program more easily.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Comments are used in Python programs to describe the purpose of code, which significantly improves readability for anyone reviewing the program. They are crucial for helping other developers maintain, debug, or extend the program without altering its execution behaviour.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:07:46',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779372341126_vvw75e30d',1,'2026-05-21 14:07:38','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:07:46',NULL),(1982,81,75,1,7,'<p>abstraction is a problem solving method in computational thinking, in the process of abstraction, unecissary information is removed leaving only relevant information, this simplifies the problem and improves the efficiency of problem solving</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:09:26',126,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>What is meant by abstraction in computational thinking?. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>abstraction is a problem solving method in computational thinking, in the process of abstraction, unecissary information is removed leaving only relevant information, this simplifies the problem and improves the efficiency of problem solving</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly explained that abstraction involves removing unnecessary information, which is a key part of its definition.</li><li>You clearly stated that the aim is to focus only on relevant information, demonstrating a good grasp of the purpose of abstraction.</li><li>Your response also highlighted that abstraction simplifies the problem, which is an important outcome of this computational thinking technique.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Your answer is very strong and comprehensive. For future responses, ensure you explicitly state that abstraction simplifies \'complex\' problems, aligning perfectly with the most detailed definitions.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Abstraction in computational thinking is the process of removing unnecessary details to focus only on the essential and relevant information, which helps to simplify complex problems.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:09:31',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779372215483_nu258yy70',2,'2026-05-21 14:09:26','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:09:31',NULL),(1983,85,183,1,7,'<p>Identifying and focusing on the key aspects of a program and ignoring any unnecessary detail. For example, if designing a car\'s software, you would focus on the key aspects such as the velocity, engine efficiency and compatibility with other types of hardware ignoring details like the cars colour, interior etc.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:10:39',106,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define ‘abstraction’ in problem solving. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Identifying and focusing on the key aspects of a program and ignoring any unnecessary detail. For example, if designing a car\'s software, you would focus on the key aspects such as the velocity, engine efficiency and compatibility with other types of hardware ignoring details like the cars colour, interior etc.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by correctly identifying that abstraction involves focusing on the key aspects of a problem. This is a crucial element of the definition.</li><li>You also rightly explained that abstraction means ignoring unnecessary details, which effectively reduces clutter and complexity.</li><li>To make your answer even stronger, consider explicitly stating that the ultimate goal of abstraction is to simplify the problem or solution.</li><li>Your example of designing car software is excellent and very clearly illustrates the practical application of abstraction.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state that abstraction aims to simplify the problem or solution to achieve a clearer understanding or more manageable implementation.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Abstraction in problem solving involves focusing on the essential details and key aspects of a problem, while deliberately removing or ignoring unnecessary complexity, to simplify the solution and make it easier to understand or manage.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:10:46',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779372341126_vvw75e30d',1,'2026-05-21 14:10:39','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:10:46',NULL),(1984,83,11,1,7,'<p>Abstraction, is where information not necessary to an end goal is omitted. For example, if you wanted to find out a person\'s speed from the sentence: \"He walked from home to the shops, which is a 5 mile journey, in half an hour\", you would omit the fact that he walked from home to the shops, and keep \"time = 30 mins\" and \"distance = 5 miles\" as they are the only necessary pieces of information here. </p><p>Pattern recognition on the other hand, is where trends and patterns are found over time. As this is quite an abstract task, it is often performed by either a human or a neural network. An example of pattern recognition, would be noticing that the power goes out roughly half an hour after a thunderstorm. This information can be used to mitigate the issue (either switching to backup power, or gracefully shutting down the servers).</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:12:03',427,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the difference between pattern recognition and abstraction in computational thinking. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Abstraction, is where information not necessary to an end goal is omitted. For example, if you wanted to find out a person\'s speed from the sentence: \"He walked from home to the shops, which is a 5 mile journey, in half an hour\", you would omit the fact that he walked from home to the shops, and keep \"time = 30 mins\" and \"distance = 5 miles\" as they are the only necessary pieces of information here. </p><p>Pattern recognition on the other hand, is where trends and patterns are found over time. As this is quite an abstract task, it is often performed by either a human or a neural network. An example of pattern recognition, would be noticing that the power goes out roughly half an hour after a thunderstorm. This information can be used to mitigate the issue (either switching to backup power, or gracefully shutting down the servers).</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You have provided a clear and accurate definition of abstraction, supported by a very effective example that shows how irrelevant details are filtered out. Well done!</li><li>Your definition of pattern recognition is also correct, explaining it as identifying trends and patterns. This shows a good understanding of the concept.</li><li>To achieve full marks, your response needed to explicitly contrast pattern recognition and abstraction, explaining how they differ or complement each other within computational thinking.</li><li>Consider providing an example for pattern recognition that more directly relates to computational problem-solving, such as identifying recurring code structures or data sequences.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state how pattern recognition and abstraction are different, perhaps by explaining that pattern recognition helps identify similarities, while abstraction focuses on simplifying those identified elements.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Pattern recognition involves spotting similarities, trends, or repeated elements within problems or data sets. Abstraction, on the other hand, is the process of filtering out unnecessary details and focusing only on the essential information needed to solve a problem. For instance, recognising a repeated input validation sequence in several different forms (pattern recognition) would lead to abstracting that common logic into a single reusable function or module.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:12:12',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779371998716_cegqx36z1',2,'2026-05-21 14:12:03','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:12:12',NULL),(1985,81,88,1,7,'<p>algorithmic efficiency is a term for describing how well an algorithm uses its resources in its functioning, it can be measured in a few ways, a greater amount of lines it typically considered less efficient than a program which can perform the same task with fewer lines; another way in which a program can be more or less efficient than another is the amount of processing power it uses, for example a search algorithm using bubble sort on a very small list would be inefficient because it uses to much processing power for little gain</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:14:46',276,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain why algorithm efficiency matters and how it can be measured. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>algorithmic efficiency is a term for describing how well an algorithm uses its resources in its functioning, it can be measured in a few ways, a greater amount of lines it typically considered less efficient than a program which can perform the same task with fewer lines; another way in which a program can be more or less efficient than another is the amount of processing power it uses, for example a search algorithm using bubble sort on a very small list would be inefficient because it uses to much processing power for little gain</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by defining algorithm efficiency as how well it uses resources and mentioning processing power, which directly addresses why it matters. To strengthen this, consider explicitly linking efficiency to benefits like faster execution times and reduced memory usage.</li><li>You correctly identified that efficiency can be measured, which is excellent! Think about standard ways this is done, such as counting the fundamental operations an algorithm performs or measuring its actual execution time.</li><li>While lines of code can sometimes correlate, they aren\'t a direct measure of an algorithm\'s efficiency in terms of time or memory. A single line can sometimes do a lot of work!</li><li>To achieve a higher mark, remember to consider concepts like how an algorithm\'s performance changes with different input sizes (scalability) or under best, worst, and average-case scenarios.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, focus on providing specific, recognised methods for measuring algorithm efficiency, such as counting operations or measuring execution time, rather than relying on the number of lines of code.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Algorithm efficiency matters because it directly impacts the performance and resource consumption of software. Efficient algorithms lead to reduced processing time, allowing programs to run faster, and minimised memory usage, which is crucial for handling large datasets or running on systems with limited resources. This ultimately improves user experience and can reduce operational costs for businesses.</p><p>Efficiency can be measured in several ways. One common method is to count the number of fundamental operations an algorithm performs, such as comparisons or assignments, which can then be expressed using Big O notation to describe its scalability. Another way is to measure the actual execution time the algorithm takes to run for various input sizes, or to analyse its memory footprint. Consideration of best, worst, and average-case scenarios helps provide a comprehensive understanding of an algorithm\'s efficiency.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:14:54',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779372594349_ww9txc9t7',1,'2026-05-21 14:14:46','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:14:54',NULL),(1986,85,85,1,7,'<p>Input functions serve as containers for user input, such as a program asking for a user\'s name. Output functions display what has been generated within the program such as displaying a calculation after taking inputs from the user.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:15:02',84,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the purpose of input and output functions in a Python program. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Input functions serve as containers for user input, such as a program asking for a user\'s name. Output functions display what has been generated within the program such as displaying a calculation after taking inputs from the user.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that input functions are used to collect data from the user, which is a great start to your explanation!</li><li>Your understanding of output functions is also spot-on; you\'ve clearly stated they are for displaying information or results generated by the program.</li><li>To make your answer even stronger, try to include the specific names of the Python functions commonly used for input and output, like `input()` and `print()`.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, mention the specific Python functions `input()` and `print()` in your explanation to clearly link the purpose to the code.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Input functions allow a Python program to collect data from the user, enabling interactive programs; for example, the `input()` function can prompt a user for their name. Output functions are used to display information, results, or messages generated by the program back to the user or console, such as using the `print()` function to show a calculated total.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:15:08',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779372341126_vvw75e30d',1,'2026-05-21 14:15:02','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:15:08',NULL),(1987,85,98,1,7,'<p>Selection is a programming construct which can be implemented in Python by using comparison operands and Boolean logic which allow for the program to make decisions based on specific conditions being either True or False. As an example, if I were to check whether a user was eligible to vote, I might use a comparison operand (greater than/less than symbol) to allow the program to make a decision on whether the user is eligible to vote based on the conditions I set.</p><p>Example:</p><p>if user_age &gt;= 16:</p><p>	print(\"You are eligible to vote!\")</p><p>else:</p><p>	print(\"You are not eligible to vote.\")</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:22:31',182,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain with an example how selection is implemented in Python. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Selection is a programming construct which can be implemented in Python by using comparison operands and Boolean logic which allow for the program to make decisions based on specific conditions being either True or False. As an example, if I were to check whether a user was eligible to vote, I might use a comparison operand (greater than/less than symbol) to allow the program to make a decision on whether the user is eligible to vote based on the conditions I set.</p><p>Example:</p><p>if user_age >= 16:</p><p>	print(\"You are eligible to vote!\")</p><p>else:</p><p>	print(\"You are not eligible to vote.\")</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve clearly explained selection as a decision-making process using comparison operands and Boolean logic, which is a great start!</li><li>Your example effectively uses `if` and `else` with a relevant scenario, demonstrating how conditions lead to different outcomes. To fully meet the criteria for a strong answer, consider including an `elif` statement to show more complex conditional logic.</li><li>Your code shows correct indentation, which is crucial in Python for defining code blocks. Briefly mentioning the importance of these indentation rules in your explanation would strengthen your answer.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Expand your example to include an `elif` statement, demonstrating how Python handles multiple conditions sequentially, and explicitly mention the role of indentation in defining these code blocks.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Selection in Python allows a program to make decisions and execute different blocks of code based on specific conditions. It is implemented using `if`, `elif` (short for \'else if\'), and `else` statements. Each condition evaluates to a Boolean value (True or False), and code blocks are clearly defined by strict indentation.</p><p>Example:</p><p>user_age = 19</p><p>if user_age >= 18:</p><p>    print(\"You are eligible to vote!\")</p><p>elif user_age >= 16:</p><p>    print(\"You are eligible to pre-register to vote.\")</p><p>else:</p><p>    print(\"You are not eligible to vote yet.\")</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:22:42',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779372341126_vvw75e30d',1,'2026-05-21 14:22:31','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:22:42',NULL),(1988,83,97,1,7,'<p>Pattern recognition helps to find the root cause of issues that may be encountered when problem solving. If large amounts are data are fed into a neural network for example, it may be able to find links between conditions, and events caused by those conditions. For example, this may be useful in linking power outages to weather behavior. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:23:02',110,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how pattern recognition assists problem solving. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Pattern recognition helps to find the root cause of issues that may be encountered when problem solving. If large amounts are data are fed into a neural network for example, it may be able to find links between conditions, and events caused by those conditions. For example, this may be useful in linking power outages to weather behavior. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a good start by explaining how pattern recognition helps to find links and identify root causes, which is a key part of the process.</li><li>To fully address the mark scheme, try to clarify that pattern recognition specifically helps identify similarities *between different problems*.</li><li>The most crucial missing element is explaining how these identified similarities enable the *reuse of prior solutions*.</li><li>Your example effectively demonstrates finding links in data; consider extending it to show how finding that link might lead to applying a pre-existing solution or strategy.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, make sure to explicitly state that identifying patterns and similarities between problems allows for the reuse or adaptation of successful solutions from the past.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Pattern recognition assists problem solving by identifying similarities between new problems and those that have been previously encountered. This allows individuals to apply or adapt successful solutions from prior experiences, improving efficiency. For example, recognising common errors in code allows the developer to apply known debugging strategies.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:23:09',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779371998716_cegqx36z1',1,'2026-05-21 14:23:02','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:23:09',NULL),(1989,81,27,1,7,'<p>Professional codes of conduct are important for the IT industry because they provide a set of rules to highlight the expected behaviours of IT workers, this helps to keep workers behaving in a consistent manner, requirements enforcing respect to authority and staff, as well as directly forbidding lying about technical ability are designed to improve workplace diversity, efficiency, and fairness</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:26:45',665,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the importance of professional codes of conduct (e.g. BCS, IAP) for software developers. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Professional codes of conduct are important for the IT industry because they provide a set of rules to highlight the expected behaviours of IT workers, this helps to keep workers behaving in a consistent manner, requirements enforcing respect to authority and staff, as well as directly forbidding lying about technical ability are designed to improve workplace diversity, efficiency, and fairness</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a good start by explaining that codes provide rules for expected behaviours and help prevent dishonest actions like lying about technical ability. This links well to promoting ethical practice and competence.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, consider expanding on how upholding these behaviours fosters public trust in the profession as a whole. How do codes assure clients and the public that developers are reliable?</li><li>For a complete evaluation, you could also explore the potential challenges developers might face when applying these codes in real-world commercial situations.</li><li>Think about linking the code\'s importance to accountability and integrity, demonstrating how they ensure developers take responsibility for their work and uphold professional standards.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>To deepen your evaluation, explore how professional codes build public trust and discuss any challenges developers might encounter when putting these abstract principles into practice.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Professional codes of conduct are vital for software developers as they establish clear expectations for ethical practice and professional competence. They promote integrity by guiding developers to act honestly, maintain confidentiality, and accurately represent their skills, thereby preventing conflicts of interest and ensuring high-quality outputs. This commitment to standards builds public trust and confidence in the profession, demonstrating accountability to clients and society. While these codes are crucial for maintaining industry reputation, their application can sometimes be challenging in commercial contexts, requiring careful interpretation of abstract principles to practical scenarios. Despite these potential difficulties, the overarching importance lies in fostering a reputable, trustworthy, and high-performing software development industry.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:26:54',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779372594349_ww9txc9t7',1,'2026-05-21 14:26:45','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:26:54',NULL),(1990,83,110,1,7,'<p>Automation will likely take over many jobs in the digital sector. This is because an AI is far cheaper than a human being, and is able to work 24/7 without breaks. Automation will also create jobs at the same time, as humans will be required to oversee these systems. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:30:58',107,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how automation affects employment in the digital sector. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Automation will likely take over many jobs in the digital sector. This is because an AI is far cheaper than a human being, and is able to work 24/7 without breaks. Automation will also create jobs at the same time, as humans will be required to oversee these systems. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve clearly explained how automation can lead to job displacement by being more cost-effective and efficient than human workers.</li><li>It\'s great that you also balanced this by identifying how automation creates new roles, specifically mentioning the need for human oversight.</li><li>To add even more depth, you could briefly expand on other new job types created, such as roles in the development or maintenance of automated systems.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Consider elaborating on a wider range of new jobs created by automation, such as those involved in system development and maintenance, in addition to oversight.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Automation can lead to job displacement in the digital sector, as automated systems and AI are often more efficient and cost-effective than human labour, able to work continuously without breaks. However, automation also creates new roles, such as jobs in designing, developing, maintaining, and overseeing these complex automated systems and AI, balancing the impact on employment.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:31:05',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779371998716_cegqx36z1',1,'2026-05-21 14:30:58','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:31:05',NULL),(1991,85,14,1,7,'<p>A linear search algorithm searches through each individual value in an array until the target value is found. Linear Algorithm\'s can be useful with array\'s containing a small number of values as each value can be sorted through independently at a quicker rate reducing (O)n time complexity.</p><p>A Binary search algorithm in contrast searches through an array by repeatedly halving the array into smaller portions of the array which could contain the target value until the options are narrowed down to just one or the array is exhausted. Binary search can be useful with array\'s containing a large number of values as by repeatedly halving the array into smaller sections, the target value can be found quickly again reducing time complexity compared to a linear search algorithm which would take a considerably longer amount of time. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:34:40',278,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the difference between a linear and binary search algorithm and when each should be used. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>A linear search algorithm searches through each individual value in an array until the target value is found. Linear Algorithm\'s can be useful with array\'s containing a small number of values as each value can be sorted through independently at a quicker rate reducing (O)n time complexity.</p><p>A Binary search algorithm in contrast searches through an array by repeatedly halving the array into smaller portions of the array which could contain the target value until the options are narrowed down to just one or the array is exhausted. Binary search can be useful with array\'s containing a large number of values as by repeatedly halving the array into smaller sections, the target value can be found quickly again reducing time complexity compared to a linear search algorithm which would take a considerably longer amount of time. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained how a linear search works by checking each value sequentially until the target is found.</li><li>Your explanation of a binary search correctly describes the process of repeatedly halving the array to narrow down options.</li><li>You effectively discussed when each algorithm might be useful, linking linear search to smaller arrays and binary search to larger ones due to efficiency.</li><li>To achieve full marks, remember to explicitly state that a binary search can only be performed on data that is already sorted.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Remember to highlight that a binary search algorithm absolutely requires the data set to be sorted before it can be used.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A linear search algorithm sequentially checks each element in a list until the target value is found or the list is exhausted. It can be used on any list, sorted or unsorted, and is best for small lists or when the data is not ordered. A binary search algorithm works by repeatedly dividing a *sorted* list in half, eliminating the half that cannot contain the target, until the value is found. It is significantly faster (logarithmic time) than a linear search for large datasets but *only works if the data is already sorted*.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:34:47',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779372341126_vvw75e30d',1,'2026-05-21 14:34:40','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:34:47',NULL),(1992,83,196,1,7,'<p>Conditionals are a great method for knowing when an algorithm is finished, and when to break the loop. They also allow for different actions to be carried out based on a certain condition. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:45:38',215,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how loops and conditionals can be combined to create efficient algorithms. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Conditionals are a great method for knowing when an algorithm is finished, and when to break the loop. They also allow for different actions to be carried out based on a certain condition. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that conditionals can determine when to stop a loop, which is a key aspect of combining them. Consider expanding on how this directly contributes to the efficiency of an algorithm, perhaps by preventing unnecessary iterations.</li><li>You also rightly noted that conditionals enable different actions based on conditions, demonstrating an understanding of their role in flexible code. To strengthen your answer, explore how this flexibility can lead to more efficient problem-solving in complex scenarios.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, remember to provide concrete examples, ideally in Python, that illustrate how loops and conditionals work together to create efficient solutions.</li><li>Thinking about specific scenarios where this combination leads to efficiency, like searching or sorting, could further enhance your explanation.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to include a simple Python example that demonstrates how a conditional within a loop can make an algorithm more efficient, such as stopping a search once an item is found.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Loops and conditionals are fundamental programming constructs that, when combined, enable the creation of highly efficient algorithms by controlling the flow of execution based on data or specific criteria. Loops (iteration) allow a block of code to be executed repeatedly, while conditionals (decision-making) allow different actions to be taken based on whether a condition is true or false.</p><p>Their combination introduces efficiency by:</p><ul><li><b>Optimised Termination:</b> A loop can iterate through a dataset, but a conditional statement can allow it to terminate early once a desired condition is met (e.g., finding a specific item in a list). This avoids unnecessary processing of the remaining data, saving time and computational resources.</li><li><b>Adaptive Processing:</b> Conditionals within loops enable algorithms to handle varied data or scenarios differently. For example, processing positive and negative numbers in a list using separate operations or skipping certain items based on a criterion.</li></ul><p>Example: Finding an item in a list efficiently.</p><pre><code>items = [10, 25, 5, 40, 15]<br>search_value = 5<br>found = False<br><br>for item in items:<br>    if item == search_value:<br>        print(f\"{search_value} found!\")<br>        found = True<br>        break  # Efficiently exits the loop once found<br><br>if not found:<br>    print(f\"{search_value} not found.\")</code></pre><p>In this example, the `break` statement inside the `if` conditional ensures the loop stops as soon as the `search_value` is found, making the search more efficient by not checking the rest of the list.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:45:48',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779371998716_cegqx36z1',1,'2026-05-21 14:45:38','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:45:48',NULL),(1993,85,111,1,7,'<p>Accessibility laws influence software design by laws set through the WCAG (web-content-accessibility guidelines) guidelines of which require web developers to take the approach of making their interface\'s/websites perceivable and operable for users with disabilities such as dyslexia of whom might find things harder to read and perceive when operating on the website/interface. This can be ensured via developers adding additional features such as alt text on images/headers, suitable background-colours, and text to voice mode all of which provide users with specific accessibility disadvantages a better experience, ideally equal to that of users without those issues.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:46:07',321,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Analyse how accessibility laws influence software interface design. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Accessibility laws influence software design by laws set through the WCAG (web-content-accessibility guidelines) guidelines of which require web developers to take the approach of making their interface\'s/websites perceivable and operable for users with disabilities such as dyslexia of whom might find things harder to read and perceive when operating on the website/interface. This can be ensured via developers adding additional features such as alt text on images/headers, suitable background-colours, and text to voice mode all of which provide users with specific accessibility disadvantages a better experience, ideally equal to that of users without those issues.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You did a great job linking accessibility laws, specifically WCAG, to the need for inclusive design that helps users with disabilities.</li><li>It\'s excellent that you included specific features like alt text and suitable background colours, which are key aspects of accessible design.</li><li>You clearly explained the positive impact of these features on users, ensuring a better and more equitable experience.</li><li>To strengthen your analysis, consider discussing how organisations face compliance risks, such as legal penalties or reputational damage, if they do not adhere to these laws.</li><li>For an even more comprehensive response, remember to also mention keyboard navigation as a crucial accessibility feature.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, broaden your analysis to include the impact of non-compliance on organisations, such as legal risks or reputational damage, to demonstrate a deeper understanding.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Accessibility laws, informed by standards like the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG), fundamentally shape software interface design to ensure inclusivity for all users. These laws necessitate features such as alt text for non-text content, robust keyboard navigation for interactive elements, and strict adherence to colour-contrast ratios. Implementing these features not only provides a perceivable and operable experience for users with disabilities, but also protects organisations from significant compliance risks, including legal penalties and reputational damage, by ensuring they meet regulatory standards.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:46:16',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779372341126_vvw75e30d',1,'2026-05-21 14:46:07','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:46:16',NULL),(1994,83,103,1,7,'<p>Inefficient algorithms can significantly slow down, or even crash a program completely. Often these algorithms have a poor time complexity, and will exponentially slow down as the workload grows. While this may be manageable with small workloads, a larger workload may cause the process to take so long, it will hang for hours, days, or even months. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:49:52',147,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Analyse the effect of using inefficient algorithms on software performance. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Inefficient algorithms can significantly slow down, or even crash a program completely. Often these algorithms have a poor time complexity, and will exponentially slow down as the workload grows. While this may be manageable with small workloads, a larger workload may cause the process to take so long, it will hang for hours, days, or even months. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You did a great job explaining how inefficient algorithms lead to longer execution times and impact user experience, even causing crashes or hangs.</li><li>You effectively discussed the scalability issue, showing how performance degrades significantly with larger workloads.</li><li>To strengthen your answer, consider explicitly mentioning other resources, such as CPU, memory, or power, that inefficient algorithms consume excessively.</li><li>Including a specific example, like comparing bubble sort to merge sort, would further demonstrate your understanding of different algorithm efficiencies.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Explicitly mention the impact on resource consumption (CPU, memory, power) and provide a concrete example of an inefficient algorithm compared to an efficient one.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Inefficient algorithms lead to significantly longer execution times and higher resource consumption, such as CPU, memory, and power. This can result in a frustrating user experience, with applications running slowly, becoming unresponsive, or even crashing. For instance, using a Bubble Sort algorithm instead of a more efficient Merge Sort on a large dataset will cause execution time to grow exponentially, severely impacting performance and scalability as the data size increases. This makes the software impractical for real-world use with significant workloads.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:49:59',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779371998716_cegqx36z1',2,'2026-05-21 14:49:52','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:49:59',NULL),(1995,83,195,1,7,'<p>Debugging allows for errors to be found before users run into them. Bugs may not only be annoying, but they may even lead to personal user data being exposed, personal files being corrupted or deleted, as well as memory leaks and looping processes slowing down the user\'s computer. Finding these bugs and fixing them before users experience them greatly improves user experience. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-21 14:57:46',444,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate how debugging contributes to the creation of robust code. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Debugging allows for errors to be found before users run into them. Bugs may not only be annoying, but they may even lead to personal user data being exposed, personal files being corrupted or deleted, as well as memory leaks and looping processes slowing down the user\'s computer. Finding these bugs and fixing them before users experience them greatly improves user experience. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained how debugging helps find and fix errors before users encounter them, which is a great start!</li><li>You effectively linked debugging to creating robust code by discussing critical impacts like data exposure and system performance.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, consider elaborating on specific methods or techniques used in debugging, rather than just stating errors are found and fixed.</li><li>Think about how debugging is an ongoing and iterative process throughout development, not just a one-off step.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on the specific techniques and processes involved in debugging, such as the use of trace tables, different testing methodologies, or iterative refinement.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Debugging is crucial for creating robust code as it systematically identifies and corrects errors, vulnerabilities, and inefficiencies before deployment. By uncovering and resolving issues like logic errors, memory leaks, or security flaws, debugging ensures the software is reliable, stable, and performs as expected under various conditions, preventing crashes, data loss, or security breaches. This process often involves systematic testing (e.g., unit, integration), using tools like trace tables to monitor program flow, and debuggers to step through code. It is an iterative cycle of finding, fixing, and re-testing that continuously refines code quality and resilience throughout the development lifecycle.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-21 14:57:53',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779371998716_cegqx36z1',1,'2026-05-21 14:57:46','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-21 14:57:53',NULL),(1996,59,76,1,7,'<p>Modularisation is breaking down large complex programs into shorter simpler modules. One advantage of this is that the modules are not dependent on each other this means a module can be updated or changed without affecting other modules. A disadvantage is that modularisation leads to higher costs through out the project</p>',NULL,'2026-05-28 16:09:56',276,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe one advantage and one disadvantage of modularisation in programming. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Modularisation is breaking down large complex programs into shorter simpler modules. One advantage of this is that the modules are not dependent on each other this means a module can be updated or changed without affecting other modules. A disadvantage is that modularisation leads to higher costs through out the project</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified an advantage related to independent modules and easier updates, which is a great start!</li><li>Your advantage touches on the concept of maintainability, which is a key benefit of modularisation.</li><li>For the disadvantage, consider how splitting a program into many parts might introduce new challenges in how those parts work together.</li><li>Think about the technical complexities rather than just cost, as that often explains why costs might increase.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>For the disadvantage, focus on a technical challenge that modularisation introduces, such as the complexity of module communication or data sharing.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An advantage of modularisation is that it makes programs easier to test and maintain because individual modules can be developed and updated independently. A disadvantage is that it can add complexity when modules need to communicate or share data, potentially requiring more effort to manage interfaces.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-28 16:09:58',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779983586408_z7yxae7if',1,'2026-05-28 16:09:56','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-28 16:09:58',NULL),(1997,59,12,1,7,'<p>Selection helps control program flow in python by allowing the user to select which part of the program that actually want/need to use instead of just going through every part of the program until the user reaches the part they need. Iteration repeats a part of the code until a condition is met which makes sure the program runs effectively and properly.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-28 16:11:42',80,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how iteration and selection are used to control program flow in Python. (2 marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Selection helps control program flow in python by allowing the user to select which part of the program that actually want/need to use instead of just going through every part of the program until the user reaches the part they need. Iteration repeats a part of the code until a condition is met which makes sure the program runs effectively and properly.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that iteration repeats a part of the code until a condition is met, which is great!</li><li>Your description of selection is a good start, but try to explain how the *code* makes choices rather than the *user*.</li><li>To improve, think about how Python\'s selection statements (like <code>if</code>, <code>elif</code>, <code>else</code>) directly control which code path is taken.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>When describing selection, focus on how the program\'s logic (using <code>if</code> statements) dictates the flow, rather than the user\'s direct choice.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Selection (using <code>if</code>/<code>elif</code>/<code>else</code>) controls program flow by allowing the program to choose different paths of execution based on whether specific conditions are true or false. Iteration (using <code>for</code> or <code>while</code> loops) controls flow by repeating a block of code multiple times until a specified condition is met.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-28 16:11:44',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779983586408_z7yxae7if',1,'2026-05-28 16:11:42','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-28 16:11:44',NULL),(1998,59,112,1,7,'<p>Proper training keeps employees updated with new technologies allowing them to learn how to use new technologies. Adaptability turns threats into new opportunities. It also stops skills expiring as AI begins to develop and expand further keeping the employee relevant.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-28 16:24:47',603,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the importance of professional development for digital professionals. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Proper training keeps employees updated with new technologies allowing them to learn how to use new technologies. Adaptability turns threats into new opportunities. It also stops skills expiring as AI begins to develop and expand further keeping the employee relevant.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly addressed how continued learning helps maintain competence with new technologies. To strengthen this, consider giving a brief example of a specific technology or skill.</li><li>You touched on adaptability, which is great. Expanding on how this directly benefits the professional or their organization would add more depth.</li><li>You effectively highlighted how professional development prevents skills from becoming outdated. Think about linking this to the concept of employability.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, you could also consider discussing the link between professional development and ethical practice or quality assurance.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Expand on how adaptability specifically turns threats into new opportunities, perhaps with a quick example.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Professional development is crucial for digital professionals to stay competent and adaptable in a rapidly evolving technological landscape. Continuous learning ensures skills remain current, preventing obsolescence and enhancing employability as technologies like AI advance. It also underpins ethical practice by keeping professionals informed of best practices and data security, and contributes to quality assurance by promoting the adoption of efficient, up-to-date methodologies and tools.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-28 16:24:49',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779983586408_z7yxae7if',1,'2026-05-28 16:24:47','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-28 16:24:49',NULL),(1999,59,77,1,7,'<p>The top-down approach is a specific strategy that uses decomposition as its primary mechanism by starting with a general goal and breaking it down into smaller individual modules</p>',NULL,'2026-05-28 16:38:05',320,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how the top-down approach assists in solving software problems. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The top-down approach is a specific strategy that uses decomposition as its primary mechanism by starting with a general goal and breaking it down into smaller individual modules</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that the top-down approach involves breaking down a problem into smaller modules, which is a great start.</li><li>To achieve full marks, you could elaborate on <strong>how</strong> this decomposition specifically assists in solving software problems, perhaps by making them easier to manage.</li><li>Consider mentioning that this approach often starts with the overall system and refines details later, or focuses on main functions first.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Explain how breaking down the problem into smaller modules makes it easier to solve software problems, for example, by making each part more manageable.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The top-down approach assists by breaking the overall software problem into smaller, more manageable sub-problems or modules. This makes the design and implementation process clearer, as you can focus on the main functions first and refine details later, leading to a more structured solution.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-28 16:38:07',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779983586408_z7yxae7if',1,'2026-05-28 16:38:05','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-28 16:38:07',NULL),(2000,59,101,1,7,'<p>Testing is a proactive process aimed at finding defects and errors and debugging is a reactive process aimed at fixing defects and errors. Testing usually occurs before debugging. Testing produces  a report of bugs and errors and debugging produces code modifications.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-28 16:44:54',367,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how debugging and testing differ during software development. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Testing is a proactive process aimed at finding defects and errors and debugging is a reactive process aimed at fixing defects and errors. Testing usually occurs before debugging. Testing produces  a report of bugs and errors and debugging produces code modifications.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained that testing is proactive and debugging is reactive, which is a great start!</li><li>You correctly identified that debugging is about fixing errors, and testing is about finding them.</li><li>You also mentioned that testing often happens before debugging, which is a good practical point.</li><li>To achieve full marks, remember to also explain that testing checks if the system meets its requirements, not just finding defects.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on the *purpose* of testing beyond just finding errors – specifically, that it validates if the software meets specified requirements or user expectations.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Testing is a proactive process designed to identify defects, errors, and verify that the software meets its specified requirements and user needs. It involves planned execution of test cases. Debugging, in contrast, is a reactive process that occurs after a defect has been identified during testing, aiming to locate, analyze, and fix the specific error in the code.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-28 16:44:56',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779983586408_z7yxae7if',1,'2026-05-28 16:44:54','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-28 16:44:56',NULL),(2001,59,179,1,7,'<p>A boolean operator evaluate conditions to a True or False statement controlling the flow of algorithms or decision-based processes.</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-28 16:49:48',119,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State what a Boolean operator does. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>A boolean operator evaluate conditions to a True or False statement controlling the flow of algorithms or decision-based processes.</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that a Boolean operator evaluates conditions to a True or False statement, which is a key function.</li><li>Your answer shows a good understanding of how Boolean operators influence the flow of algorithms and decision-based processes.</li><li>To gain full marks, remember to specify the common types of logical comparisons, such as AND, OR, and NOT.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, include specific examples of Boolean operators like AND, OR, or NOT to fully demonstrate your knowledge.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A Boolean operator performs logical comparisons such as AND, OR, or NOT, evaluating conditions to produce a True or False result.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-28 16:49:50',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779983586408_z7yxae7if',2,'2026-05-28 16:49:48','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-28 16:49:50',NULL),(2002,59,26,1,7,'<p>The AUP mitigates and protects against data breaches, malware and unauthorised access.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-28 17:05:11',786,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the purpose and content of an Acceptable Use Policy (AUP).(5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The AUP mitigates and protects against data breaches, malware and unauthorised access.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a good start by identifying that an AUP protects against serious security risks like data breaches and malware.</li><li>To improve, you could expand on how the AUP achieves this protection by detailing the specific types of activities it permits and prohibits.</li><li>Consider also mentioning other content an AUP might include, such as communication etiquette or the consequences of not following the policy.</li><li>Think about the broader organisational benefits of an AUP beyond just security, such as maintaining professional standards.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly explain what an AUP actually contains and how it helps achieve its purpose, rather than just stating its benefits.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An Acceptable Use Policy (AUP) outlines the permitted and prohibited activities when using an organisation\'s IT systems and resources. Its purpose is to protect the organisation from misuse, ensure data confidentiality, and maintain professional standards. The content typically includes guidelines on communication etiquette, responsible internet and email usage, software installation rules, and specifies the penalties for policy breaches. AUPs are crucial for safeguarding an organisation\'s assets and reputation.</p>RAG RATING: <div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-28 17:05:14',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1779983586408_z7yxae7if',1,'2026-05-28 17:05:11','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-28 17:05:14',NULL),(2003,62,88,1,7,'<p>Algorithm efficeincy is a crucial part of sorting and searching for values in large or small data sets, the correct efficeciency will determine how long it will take for the value to be searched for. For example in smaller data sets a linear search would be more efficent as it checks values one by one, in comparison to this a bubble search would be better for larger data sets because it breaks the list down into multiple sublists and repeats that process until the value is found. The efficency of the search can be measured by the big o notation to provide a indicator for an efficent search.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-29 14:53:34',435,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain why algorithm efficiency matters and how it can be measured. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Algorithm efficeincy is a crucial part of sorting and searching for values in large or small data sets, the correct efficeciency will determine how long it will take for the value to be searched for. For example in smaller data sets a linear search would be more efficent as it checks values one by one, in comparison to this a bubble search would be better for larger data sets because it breaks the list down into multiple sublists and repeats that process until the value is found. The efficency of the search can be measured by the big o notation to provide a indicator for an efficent search.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that efficiency relates to how long an algorithm takes, which is a great start! To strengthen this, consider mentioning the impact on memory usage as well.</li><li>You correctly identified Big O notation as a way to measure efficiency. To elaborate, you could explain what Big O notation measures (like steps or comparisons).</li><li>The example provided for algorithms was slightly mixed up. A linear search checks one by one, and a binary search breaks a list down, not a bubble search. Focus on getting the algorithm names and their methods precise.</li><li>Think about why reduced processing time and memory use are important for users or systems.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Ensure your examples of algorithms and their methods are accurate; for instance, a binary search (not bubble search) typically breaks down lists for efficiency.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Algorithm efficiency matters because it directly impacts the processing time and memory usage required for a task. Efficient algorithms lead to faster execution, consuming fewer computational resources, which is crucial for handling large datasets, real-time applications, and scalability. This reduces operational costs and improves user experience. Efficiency can be measured by counting the number of steps an algorithm takes, the execution time, or the number of comparisons made. Big O notation is a common way to express efficiency, indicating how an algorithm\'s performance scales with the input size, often considering best, worst, and average-case scenarios.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-29 14:53:37',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780069547751_osq973866',1,'2026-05-29 14:53:34','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-29 14:53:37',NULL),(2004,59,9,1,7,'<p>Computational thinking is a problem solving technique which involves breaking down complex problems into simpler step by step solutions that can be executable by humans or computers</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-29 19:16:42',208,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define ˜computational thinking (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Computational thinking is a problem solving technique which involves breaking down complex problems into simpler step by step solutions that can be executable by humans or computers</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that computational thinking is a problem-solving technique and involves breaking down problems into simpler steps. Well done!</li><li>To improve, consider mentioning that these steps are often expressed as algorithms, which is a key part of the process.</li><li>For a stronger answer, try to include the four core pillars: decomposition, pattern recognition, abstraction, and algorithmic design.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly mention that the \"step-by-step solutions\" are often referred to as algorithms.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Computational thinking is a logical approach to problem-solving that breaks down complex problems into manageable parts, expresses them as algorithms, and can later be coded. It focuses on decomposition, pattern recognition, abstraction, and algorithmic design.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-29 19:16:44',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780081988937_nunajkgim',3,'2026-05-29 19:16:42','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-29 19:16:44',NULL),(2005,59,77,1,7,'<p>The top down approach assists in solving software problems by focusing first on the larger problem and then breaking it down into simpler tasks so that it is easier to share tasks and solve them</p>',NULL,'2026-05-29 19:22:41',152,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how the top-down approach assists in solving software problems. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The top down approach assists in solving software problems by focusing first on the larger problem and then breaking it down into simpler tasks so that it is easier to share tasks and solve them</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that the top-down approach involves breaking a larger problem into smaller tasks, which is a great start.</li><li>To score full marks, try to use more specific terminology related to software development, such as \"sub-systems\" or \"functions.\"</li><li>Consider explaining how this breakdown helps with the development process itself, like by writing main functions first and then refining details.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to incorporate specific programming terms like \'sub-systems\' or \'modules\' when describing the smaller tasks.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The top-down approach assists in solving software problems by starting with the overall system and breaking it down into smaller, manageable sub-systems. This allows developers to focus on the main functions first and then refine the details of each sub-system later.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-29 19:22:43',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780081988937_nunajkgim',2,'2026-05-29 19:22:41','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-05-29 19:22:43',NULL),(2006,59,191,1,7,'<p>Programmers must handle all data securely by using the most updated data protection features. Programmers can also only use necessary data and cannot request or use any data that is not necessary in making their program. Going against these rules can result in fines and losses for the programmers or company as a whole.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-29 19:33:48',645,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how data protection legislation affects software development. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Programmers must handle all data securely by using the most updated data protection features. Programmers can also only use necessary data and cannot request or use any data that is not necessary in making their program. Going against these rules can result in fines and losses for the programmers or company as a whole.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified the importance of handling data securely, which is a key aspect of data protection in software development. Well done!</li><li>You also rightly noted that only necessary data should be collected and used, demonstrating an understanding of data minimisation principles.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, remember to explicitly mention specific legislation like GDPR, which is a major influence on data protection in software.</li><li>Consider discussing lawful processing and user consent as these are fundamental requirements when developing software that handles personal data.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly name relevant data protection legislation, such as GDPR, to show a more specific understanding of the legal framework.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Data protection legislation, like GDPR, significantly impacts software development by requiring that personal data is processed lawfully, fairly, and transparently. Developers must implement measures to obtain explicit user consent for data collection and processing. Software must be designed with \'privacy by design\' principles, ensuring data minimisation and secure storage, and providing users with rights over their data, such as access and erasure.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-29 19:33:51',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780081988937_nunajkgim',2,'2026-05-29 19:33:48','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>You need to mention GDPR whenever this kind of question comes up.</p>','A','2026-06-01 08:29:05',1),(2007,59,27,1,7,'<p>Professional code of conducts are ethical frameworks structured by professional bodies to regulate behaviour, integrity and competence of their members, ensuring public trust and safety. This affects software developers by making sure that programmers are competent enough to complete the work set and also makes sure they have appropriate behaviour in the workplace. The BCS mandates how developers adhere to 4 core principles and IAP structures ethical duties.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-29 19:41:49',451,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the importance of professional codes of conduct (e.g. BCS, IAP) for software developers. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Professional code of conducts are ethical frameworks structured by professional bodies to regulate behaviour, integrity and competence of their members, ensuring public trust and safety. This affects software developers by making sure that programmers are competent enough to complete the work set and also makes sure they have appropriate behaviour in the workplace. The BCS mandates how developers adhere to 4 core principles and IAP structures ethical duties.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly addressed how codes promote ethical practice and competence, which is a great start.</li><li>You mentioned public trust and safety, which is excellent for showing the broader impact of these codes.</li><li>To improve your evaluation, consider discussing how codes of conduct provide accountability and help avoid conflicts of interest.</li><li>For a higher-level response, you could also explore the challenges developers face when applying these principles in real-world commercial situations.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to evaluate the importance by contrasting the benefits of codes (like accountability) with any potential challenges in their practical application for software developers.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Professional codes of conduct, like those from BCS and IAP, are vital for software developers as they establish ethical frameworks that promote integrity, competence, and public trust. They ensure developers maintain high standards, fostering accountability and reducing risks like negligence or data misuse, which directly impacts user safety and system reliability. While codes provide clear guidelines, ensuring quality and avoiding conflicts of interest, their application can be challenging when abstract principles need to be translated into specific commercial contexts, requiring careful judgment from developers. Ultimately, they build confidence in the profession and protect both developers and the public.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-29 19:41:52',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780081988937_nunajkgim',1,'2026-05-29 19:41:49','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>I\'d mark that as a solid 3.</p>','A','2026-06-01 08:26:52',1),(2008,59,180,1,7,'<p>For loops and while loops. For loops repeat a section of code for a selected number of repeats, while loops repeat a section of code until a condition is met.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-29 19:44:43',60,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Identify two types of loops used in Python. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>For loops and while loops. For loops repeat a section of code for a selected number of repeats, while loops repeat a section of code until a condition is met.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully identified two types of loops used in Python: \'for\' and \'while\' loops. Well done!</li><li>You also accurately described how each loop type functions, demonstrating a clear understanding.</li><li>Your response aligns perfectly with the mark scheme\'s requirements.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Continue to provide clear and concise explanations like this in your future answers.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Two types of loops used in Python are \'for\' loops (count-controlled) and \'while\' loops (condition-controlled).</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-29 19:44:44',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780081988937_nunajkgim',1,'2026-05-29 19:44:43','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 08:24:24',1),(2009,59,183,1,7,'<p>Abstraction is the process of simplifying a problem by removing the unnecessary details and only focussing on the essential parts</p>',NULL,'2026-05-30 13:51:59',77,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define ‘abstraction’ in problem solving. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Abstraction is the process of simplifying a problem by removing the unnecessary details and only focussing on the essential parts</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained that abstraction involves removing unnecessary details, which is a key aspect.</li><li>You also correctly identified that abstraction means focusing on the essential parts of a problem.</li><li>Your response fully covers the definition of abstraction in problem-solving.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Your answer is excellent and covers all the key points. Keep up the great work!</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Abstraction is the process of simplifying a problem by hiding or removing complex and unnecessary details, focusing only on the essential information to create a more manageable solution.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-30 13:52:01',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780149033880_6k2d428ah',1,'2026-05-30 13:51:59','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 08:23:18',1),(2010,59,10,1,7,'<p>Decomposition is used in problem solving in breaking up larger complex problems into smaller simpler problems making it easier to share tasks between teams for example.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-30 14:01:47',46,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>What is the purpose of decomposition in problem solving? (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Decomposition is used in problem solving in breaking up larger complex problems into smaller simpler problems making it easier to share tasks between teams for example.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that decomposition involves breaking down large, complex problems into smaller, simpler ones. Well done!</li><li>To achieve a higher mark, consider explaining what happens after the problem is broken down. What is the ultimate goal of making them smaller?</li><li>Think about how these smaller parts relate to the overall solution once they are solved.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on why breaking problems down into smaller parts is beneficial for solving them, and how these smaller solutions contribute to the complete solution.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The purpose of decomposition is to break down a complex problem into smaller, more manageable sub-problems, allowing each part to be solved individually before being combined to form a complete solution.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-30 14:01:49',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780149033880_6k2d428ah',2,'2026-05-30 14:01:47','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 08:23:02',1),(2011,59,10,1,7,'<p>The purpose of decomposition is to break down larger problems into smaller simpler problems, allowing the smaller problems to be solved individually</p>',NULL,'2026-05-30 14:03:36',94,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>What is the purpose of decomposition in problem solving? (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The purpose of decomposition is to break down larger problems into smaller simpler problems, allowing the smaller problems to be solved individually</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that decomposition involves breaking down larger problems into smaller, simpler ones. Well done!</li><li>You also explained that these smaller problems can be solved individually, which is a key part of the process.</li><li>To achieve full marks, remember to also mention that these individual solutions are later combined to form a complete solution to the original complex problem.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, ensure you mention that the smaller solutions are reassembled to solve the overall complex problem.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The purpose of decomposition is to break a complex problem into smaller, more manageable sub-problems so that each can be solved individually and later combined into a complete solution.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-30 14:03:37',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780149033880_6k2d428ah',3,'2026-05-30 14:03:36','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>You\'d have been given this mark.</p>','G','2026-06-01 08:22:42',1),(2012,59,187,1,7,'<p>Conditional statements are used to control program flow to make sure certain sections of code are completed once a condition is met such as while loops this ensures the rest of the program can run correctly with the needed requirements. This ensures code functionality by ensuring the program has the data or information it needs.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-30 14:12:27',263,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how conditional statements are used to control program flow. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Conditional statements are used to control program flow to make sure certain sections of code are completed once a condition is met such as while loops this ensures the rest of the program can run correctly with the needed requirements. This ensures code functionality by ensuring the program has the data or information it needs.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that conditional statements ensure certain code sections are executed when a condition is met, which is a great start.</li><li>To improve, focus on the specific keywords used for conditional statements like <code>if</code>, <code>elif</code>, and <code>else</code>, as these are central to making decisions in program flow.</li><li>While <code>while</code> loops use conditions, the question specifically asks about conditional statements for program flow control, which usually refers to selection rather than iteration.</li><li>Consider providing a simple example or pseudocode to illustrate how these statements guide the program\'s path based on different conditions.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, clearly state the specific conditional keywords (e.g., <code>if</code>, <code>elif</code>, <code>else</code>) and how they enable selective execution of code.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Conditional statements like <code>if</code>, <code>elif</code>, and <code>else</code> are used to control program flow by allowing different blocks of code to be executed based on whether a specific condition is true or false. For example, an <code>if</code> statement checks a condition, and if it\'s true, a certain block of code runs. If false, an <code>elif</code> (else if) condition might be checked, or an <code>else</code> block will execute as a default, ensuring the program takes a specific path depending on runtime conditions. This allows programs to make decisions and respond dynamically to input or changing data.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-05-30 14:12:30',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1780149033880_6k2d428ah',2,'2026-05-30 14:12:27','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Conditional = branching</p><p>ie </p><p><code>if, else, elif and switch</code></p>','R','2026-06-01 08:22:10',1),(2013,64,79,1,7,'<p>Flowcharts and pseudocode are both a great way to display an algorithm to a non technical knowing member / members of staff,. But each have drawbacks to showing the algorithm. For example, a flowchart shows an algorithm via visual shapes and symbols, which provide a clear and structured way to show an algorithm. Pseudocode explains the steps of an algorithm or program via similar structure to programming languages, giving written examples to non technical users. In conclusion, flowcharts are usually easier for non technical users to understand how an algorithm is made, rather than pseudocode.</p>',NULL,'2026-05-30 15:30:50',276,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Compare the use of flowcharts and pseudocode when expressing algorithms. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Flowcharts and pseudocode are both a great way to display an algorithm to a non technical knowing member / members of staff,. But each have drawbacks to showing the algorithm. For example, a flowchart shows an algorithm via visual shapes and symbols, which provide a clear and structured way to show an algorithm. Pseudocode explains the steps of an algorithm or program via similar structure to programming languages, giving written examples to non technical users. In conclusion, flowcharts are usually easier for non technical users to understand how an algorithm is made, rather than pseudocode.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that flowcharts are visual and easier for beginners, which is a key point for comparison.</li><li>You also recognised that pseudocode uses a structure similar to programming languages, showing an understanding of its text-based nature.</li><li>To improve, consider directly comparing their suitability for different audiences, such as programmers versus non-technical staff.</li><li>For a higher mark, you could also evaluate how clearly each expresses the structure of an algorithm.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Explicitly compare the advantages and disadvantages of each method for different users (e.g., beginners, experienced programmers) to show a deeper understanding.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Flowcharts offer a visual representation of an algorithm using symbols and arrows, making them generally easier for beginners and non-technical audiences to understand due to their graphical nature. Pseudocode, however, is a text-based, structured representation that closely resembles actual programming languages. While it may require more familiarity for beginners, it is often preferred by programmers as it translates more directly into code and allows for more detailed expression of logic and data structures than a typical flowchart.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-30 15:30:53',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780154770785_v2q4xqg0k',2,'2026-05-30 15:30:50','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 08:20:49',1),(2014,64,22,1,7,'<p>Emerging technologies such as AI and IoT are changing software development in a way that provides more employment for software devs, as well as providing tehcnical tools to boost efficiency in the workplace. IoT is relevant in the future, which would make software developers needed in the future. This means that companies will be looking to employ software developers to develop the software inside the devices and systems being created. As AI is emerging into the world, its use has turned into a great tool for developers who solve problems and create systems. AI also boosts efficiency for the workers which will lead to faster turnarounds within projects. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-30 15:35:42',241,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how emerging technologies such as AI and IoT are changing software development. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Emerging technologies such as AI and IoT are changing software development in a way that provides more employment for software devs, as well as providing tehcnical tools to boost efficiency in the workplace. IoT is relevant in the future, which would make software developers needed in the future. This means that companies will be looking to employ software developers to develop the software inside the devices and systems being created. As AI is emerging into the world, its use has turned into a great tool for developers who solve problems and create systems. AI also boosts efficiency for the workers which will lead to faster turnarounds within projects. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a good start by identifying that AI and IoT lead to more employment and efficiency in software development, which is a positive benefit.</li><li>To fully meet the criteria, try to explain more specifically how AI links to automation or predictive systems in software development.</li><li>Similarly, for IoT, elaborate on its role in data collection or remote control within software applications.</li><li>Consider discussing how these technologies might introduce new challenges, such as privacy or security concerns, for developers.</li><li>Think about how software developers might need to adapt their coding practices for real-time or distributed systems because of these changes.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to provide more specific examples of how AI automates tasks or how IoT facilitates data collection in software development.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>AI is changing software development by enabling automation in testing and code generation, leading to more efficient development cycles and the creation of predictive systems. IoT is influencing development by requiring software for data collection from numerous devices and for enabling remote control functionalities, leading to more distributed and real-time systems. Developers must now adapt to creating software for these interconnected, data-rich environments, addressing new challenges like data privacy and security, while also benefiting from increased efficiency and innovation.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-30 15:35:45',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780154770785_v2q4xqg0k',1,'2026-05-30 15:35:42','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 08:19:33',1),(2015,64,178,1,7,'<p>An algorithm is a clear, defined set of steps to complete a task or objective</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-05-30 16:00:58',19,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define the term ‘algorithm’. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>An algorithm is a clear, defined set of steps to complete a task or objective</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that an algorithm is a set of steps, which is a key part of the definition.</li><li>You also mentioned that these steps are for completing a task or objective, which aligns well with the mark scheme\'s \"perform a specific task.\"</li><li>To achieve full marks, consider adding that these steps are \"step-by-step instructions\" to make the definition even more precise.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state that an algorithm consists of \"step-by-step instructions\" to enhance the clarity of your definition.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An algorithm is a set of step-by-step instructions designed to perform a specific task or solve a problem.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-05-30 16:01:00',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780154770785_v2q4xqg0k',2,'2026-05-30 16:00:58','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 08:19:07',1),(2016,64,90,1,7,'<p>The increased use of digital systems play a part in concerning for privacy issues by more monitoring of persons. For example, in the workplace, companies are installing digital cameras to track and monitor staff members and what they do, this increases trust issues within the staff and bosses relationships, potentially leading to strikes or resignation. Privacy concerns are also led from an increase in needed data from users to operate digital systems, if the data being stored isn\'t stored well, following guidelines with the GDPR, it can lead to people not trusting the systems. </p>',NULL,'2026-05-30 16:05:19',226,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how privacy concerns arise from increased use of digital systems. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The increased use of digital systems play a part in concerning for privacy issues by more monitoring of persons. For example, in the workplace, companies are installing digital cameras to track and monitor staff members and what they do, this increases trust issues within the staff and bosses relationships, potentially leading to strikes or resignation. Privacy concerns are also led from an increase in needed data from users to operate digital systems, if the data being stored isn\'t stored well, following guidelines with the GDPR, it can lead to people not trusting the systems. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by identifying \"more monitoring\" and linking this to surveillance. To strengthen this, try to broaden your examples beyond just the workplace.</li><li>You correctly mentioned GDPR and the need for data to be \"stored well,\" showing an understanding of data protection. For future answers, try to explicitly mention user consent and how misuse of personal information can arise.</li><li>Consider expanding on the concept of a \"digital footprint\" and how the collection of this data by various systems contributes to privacy concerns.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate more on the concept of surveillance and data collection, perhaps by mentioning how personal data is gathered from various online activities like browsing or social media use.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Increased use of digital systems raises privacy concerns through extensive data collection, often without explicit user consent. Every online interaction contributes to a \'digital footprint\' which, combined with surveillance technologies like CCTV or tracking cookies, can lead to comprehensive profiles of individuals. This personal information is vulnerable to misuse, such as targeted advertising or identity theft, if not handled securely. Legislation like GDPR aims to mitigate these risks by enforcing rules on data processing, ensuring individuals have rights over their personal data and that companies are accountable for its protection.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-05-30 16:05:22',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780154770785_v2q4xqg0k',2,'2026-05-30 16:05:19','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 08:18:50',1),(2017,83,181,1,7,'<p>Validation is ensuring data and user inputs are valid. For example, a user input may be stripped of special characters, or denied if it contains non-numerical characters for a number input. Another example, would be an image file being checked to ensure it is a valid image file, and not corrupt. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:10:15',96,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain what validation means in the context of programming. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Validation is ensuring data and user inputs are valid. For example, a user input may be stripped of special characters, or denied if it contains non-numerical characters for a number input. Another example, would be an image file being checked to ensure it is a valid image file, and not corrupt. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained that validation ensures data and user inputs are valid, which is a great start.</li><li>You provided excellent examples of specific validation checks, such as checking for non-numerical characters or corrupt files.</li><li>To improve, consider explicitly stating that validation happens *before* data is processed.</li><li>Think about why validation is important – what problem does it help prevent?</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state that validation is a check performed on input data *before* it is processed by the program.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Validation in programming means checking that input data meets specific rules or criteria before it is processed. This ensures the data is suitable and prevents errors, such as checking a number is within a valid range or a text input has the correct format.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:10:17',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',1,'2026-06-01 08:10:15','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 08:18:15',1),(2018,83,197,1,7,'<p>Automation will drastically change employment and skill requirements. Many skilled job positions will be taken by AI, but some will still remain to overlook the AI. However, AI will also create jobs, albeit less than are taken. This is because neural networks will always hallucinate, as this is down to the fundemental way they work. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:12:33',120,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss the impact of automation and AI on employment and skill requirements. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Automation will drastically change employment and skill requirements. Many skilled job positions will be taken by AI, but some will still remain to overlook the AI. However, AI will also create jobs, albeit less than are taken. This is because neural networks will always hallucinate, as this is down to the fundemental way they work. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that automation will lead to job displacement and also create new roles. To strengthen your answer, consider expanding on the types of jobs that might be created or changed.</li><li>You mentioned job roles remaining to \'overlook the AI\', which is a good point about new skill requirements. Try to elaborate on what these new skills might be.</li><li>You brought up the concept of AI hallucination; while interesting, ensure your points directly relate to the broader impact on employment and skill requirements rather than specific AI limitations.</li><li>To achieve a higher mark, ensure you balance both the efficiency gains and potential job losses more fully, demonstrating a wider understanding of the societal impact.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Expand on the specific skill requirements that will emerge or become more important due to automation and AI, such as critical thinking, creativity, and digital literacy.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Automation and AI will significantly impact employment by increasing efficiency and productivity, potentially leading to job displacement in routine or highly repetitive roles across various sectors. However, they will also create new jobs in areas such as AI development, maintenance, data analysis, and roles requiring uniquely human skills like creativity, critical thinking, and emotional intelligence. Skill requirements will shift towards a greater demand for digital literacy, problem-solving, adaptability, and complex decision-making. There will also be a growing need for roles focused on ethical AI oversight and human-AI collaboration, balancing technological advancement with societal well-being.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:12:37',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',1,'2026-06-01 08:12:33','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 08:17:29',1),(2019,58,90,1,7,'<p>Privacy concerns have arised because of new emerging technologies involving monitoring systems. One example of this is employee monitoring and while this can encourage them to work, it also invades in their privacy and may make the employees unsecure. Another example of this is a digital footprint and that is something which records everything a person does on the internet and this means that anyone can look up what a certain person has done on the internet without their consent which makes people wonder if they truly are anonymous</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:15:00',316,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how privacy concerns arise from increased use of digital systems. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Privacy concerns have arised because of new emerging technologies involving monitoring systems. One example of this is employee monitoring and while this can encourage them to work, it also invades in their privacy and may make the employees unsecure. Another example of this is a digital footprint and that is something which records everything a person does on the internet and this means that anyone can look up what a certain person has done on the internet without their consent which makes people wonder if they truly are anonymous</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly identified the concept of a digital footprint and how it impacts privacy, which is excellent.</li><li>You provided a good example with employee monitoring, illustrating how surveillance raises privacy concerns.</li><li>To improve, consider discussing the broad collection of personal data by digital systems and how this data might be misused.</li><li>You could also mention the importance of user consent in data handling to strengthen your points further.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Expand on how data collection, beyond just monitoring, leads to privacy issues, specifically mentioning potential misuse of personal information.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Increased use of digital systems leads to significant data collection, often without explicit user consent. This data collection, combined with pervasive digital footprints from online activity, creates concerns about personal information being shared or misused. Surveillance, such as employee monitoring, also raises privacy issues by tracking individual behaviour. Without robust measures and adherence to legislation like GDPR, individuals may lose control over their personal data, leading to a loss of anonymity and potential privacy breaches.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:15:02',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301373964_2qvt3t0od',1,'2026-06-01 08:15:00','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 08:16:16',1),(2020,83,74,1,7,'<p>An algorithm is a set of instructions that are used to process data or complete any other task. Algorithms often loop for an indeterminate length of time, until a set of conditions are met, but this is not always the case. Algorithms often utilize selection, loops, and other operations to complete their task.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:15:13',121,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define algorithm. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>An algorithm is a set of instructions that are used to process data or complete any other task. Algorithms often loop for an indeterminate length of time, until a set of conditions are met, but this is not always the case. Algorithms often utilize selection, loops, and other operations to complete their task.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that an algorithm is a set of instructions, which is a great start.</li><li>To improve your definition, try to include the idea that these instructions are step-by-step and designed to solve a problem or perform a computation.</li><li>Your additional details about loops and selection are good points about how algorithms work, but for a definition, focus on the core meaning first.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, ensure your definition explicitly states that algorithms are a precise, step-by-step sequence of instructions used to solve a problem or perform a computation.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An algorithm is a precise, step-by-step sequence of instructions used to solve a problem or perform a computation.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:15:15',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',1,'2026-06-01 08:15:13','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 08:16:43',1),(2021,83,189,1,7,'<p>Equality legislation allows for software to accommodate a wider range of needs. For example, if a person with a certain disability (such as colour blindness) was recruited when creating a piece of software, they can use their first-hand experience to ensure the software meets the needs of colour blind people. This also applies for most other minorities. </p><p>Equality legislation also helps to eliminate personal biases of employers, and ensures that they do not turn down potential hires because of certain characteristics such as race, gender, or disability. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:19:27',234,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how equality legislation affects software design. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Equality legislation allows for software to accommodate a wider range of needs. For example, if a person with a certain disability (such as colour blindness) was recruited when creating a piece of software, they can use their first-hand experience to ensure the software meets the needs of colour blind people. This also applies for most other minorities. </p><p>Equality legislation also helps to eliminate personal biases of employers, and ensures that they do not turn down potential hires because of certain characteristics such as race, gender, or disability. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that equality legislation leads to software accommodating a wider range of needs, which is a great start.</li><li>You gave a good example of how considering colour blindness affects software design, demonstrating understanding of accessibility.</li><li>To strengthen your answer, explicitly mention the Equality Act and how it mandates inclusive design principles.</li><li>Consider expanding on how inclusive interfaces benefit all users, not just specific minority groups.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly reference the Equality Act and its direct impact on requiring inclusive software design to prevent discrimination.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Equality legislation, such as the Equality Act, requires software design to consider and prevent discrimination based on characteristics like age or disability. This means software designers must implement accessibility features, for example, high contrast modes or keyboard navigation, to ensure inclusive interfaces. The aim is to make software usable by the widest possible range of people, accommodating diverse user needs and abilities.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:19:30',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',1,'2026-06-01 08:19:27','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:19:30',NULL),(2022,59,95,1,7,'<p>A variable is a named storage space where the data stored within it can be changed while the program is in use</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:24:10',174,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define the term variable in programming. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>A variable is a named storage space where the data stored within it can be changed while the program is in use</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that a variable is a named storage location. Well done!</li><li>You also accurately stated that the value stored within a variable can change during program execution. That\'s a key part of the definition.</li><li>To achieve a higher mark, remember that variables also have a data type, which is important for how the program uses the stored data.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to include the concept of a \"data type\" when defining a variable, as this adds important detail to its function.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A variable is a named storage location that holds a value which can change during program execution, and it typically has a defined data type.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:24:12',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780302004062_dq4lgdi0i',3,'2026-06-01 08:24:10','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 08:24:47',1),(2023,70,24,1,7,'<p>Safe environment, including safe furniture, preventing employers from hurting themselves, straining themselves, and ensuring their safety is the main priority. Frequent breaks is also a major Health and Safety requirement to prevent eye strain and allowing employees to remain at a good posture and also shows benefits for their mental health, preventing stress, and other mental health issues</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:24:45',342,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State two key requirements of the Health and Safety at Work Act relevant to IT workers. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Safe environment, including safe furniture, preventing employers from hurting themselves, straining themselves, and ensuring their safety is the main priority. Frequent breaks is also a major Health and Safety requirement to prevent eye strain and allowing employees to remain at a good posture and also shows benefits for their mental health, preventing stress, and other mental health issues</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified the requirement for a safe working environment, including safe furniture, which is a key aspect of the Act for IT workers.</li><li>You also accurately stated the need for frequent breaks to prevent eye strain and maintain good posture, showing a good understanding of relevant requirements.</li><li>Your response goes into good detail about the benefits of breaks, demonstrating a thorough understanding of their importance.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to clearly state who is responsible for these requirements, for example, by mentioning \"employers have a duty to...\"</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Employers must provide a safe working environment, including ergonomically sound workstations and equipment. They also need to ensure employees receive appropriate breaks, especially from display screen equipment, to prevent issues like eye strain and repetitive strain injury.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:24:47',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780301689194_mbeqo3aon',2,'2026-06-01 08:24:45','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 08:25:42',1),(2024,83,192,1,7,'<p>Professional codes of conduct are important to ensure the software development process is structured and progresses smoothly. For example, if different developers were bickering and fighting over the development of the application, not only are they wasting development time, but they will likely create a messy result with no real structure or direction. </p><p>Professional codes of conduct also ensure a safe working environment for all kinds of people - regardless of race, gender, sexuality, or disability. This ensures that development can move smoothly without conflict. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:25:56',280,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss why professional codes of conduct are important in software development. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Professional codes of conduct are important to ensure the software development process is structured and progresses smoothly. For example, if different developers were bickering and fighting over the development of the application, not only are they wasting development time, but they will likely create a messy result with no real structure or direction. </p><p>Professional codes of conduct also ensure a safe working environment for all kinds of people - regardless of race, gender, sexuality, or disability. This ensures that development can move smoothly without conflict. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a good start by highlighting how codes of conduct can prevent conflict and foster a smoother development process, which is a valuable point.</li><li>Consider expanding on how codes of conduct specifically guide ethical behavior in terms of the software itself, beyond just team dynamics.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, you could discuss how these codes build public trust in the software and the developers creating it.</li><li>Think about how professional codes support accountability for developers\' actions and the quality of their work.</li><li>Next time, try to include specific examples of professional bodies or their codes, such as the BCS (British Computer Society) or IAP (Institute of IT Professionals).</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Focus on the ethical implications of software development and how codes of conduct specifically address public trust and accountability in the final product and its creators.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Professional codes of conduct are crucial in software development as they guide ethical behaviour, ensuring developers act responsibly and with integrity. They build and maintain public trust in the software being developed and the professionals who create it, as users expect reliable and secure systems. Furthermore, these codes support accountability, providing a framework for addressing professional misconduct and ensuring developers are responsible for the quality and impact of their work. Examples include codes from bodies like the BCS (British Computer Society) or IAP (Institute of IT Professionals).</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:25:59',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',2,'2026-06-01 08:25:56','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:25:59',NULL),(2025,59,77,1,7,'<p>The top down approach assists in solving software problems as it focuses on the largest problem and then divides the larger problem down into smaller problems which allows for each task to be solved individually</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:27:12',99,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how the top-down approach assists in solving software problems. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The top down approach assists in solving software problems as it focuses on the largest problem and then divides the larger problem down into smaller problems which allows for each task to be solved individually</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained that the top-down approach breaks down a large problem into smaller ones, which is a great start!</li><li>To earn full marks, try to include how this approach helps manage complexity.</li><li>Consider adding a detail about the order of development, such as starting with main functions.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on how breaking down problems helps in managing the overall complexity of software development.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The top-down approach assists by starting with the overall software system and then breaking it down into smaller, more manageable sub-systems or modules. This allows for the main functions to be designed first, making the problem easier to solve by refining details later.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:27:14',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780302004062_dq4lgdi0i',3,'2026-06-01 08:27:12','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:27:14',NULL),(2026,62,184,1,7,'<p>Pattern recognision makes it easier to understand problems and develop solutions, being able to recognise patterns can help spot bugs and help understand problems more deeply.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:27:32',791,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how pattern recognition can support efficient problem solving. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Pattern recognision makes it easier to understand problems and develop solutions, being able to recognise patterns can help spot bugs and help understand problems more deeply.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that pattern recognition helps in understanding problems and developing solutions. This is a good start to explaining its role.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, consider explaining *how* recognising patterns leads to more efficient solutions, perhaps by reusing known solutions.</li><li>Adding a specific example, like how recognising a sorting pattern could allow you to apply a known algorithm, would significantly strengthen your answer.</li><li>Your point about spotting bugs is interesting but less directly related to *efficient problem-solving* in the context of initial solution development.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on how recognising patterns allows for the reuse of previous solutions or established methods, making the problem-solving process quicker.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Pattern recognition supports efficient problem solving by allowing individuals to identify similarities or recurring trends in new problems. This enables the reuse of existing solutions or established algorithms, rather than developing new ones from scratch. For example, recognising a problem requires sorting allows for the immediate application of an efficient sorting algorithm like quicksort, saving time and effort.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:27:35',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301649912_nz8qtk6n0',2,'2026-06-01 08:27:32','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:27:35',NULL),(2027,65,86,1,7,'<p>When you get an error message from the code when it\'s not working, you can use that error message to fix your code piece by piece. And once your code is completely working and fixed and will not break from a user input. This means that the code is robust. And if there are any errors whilst you think the code is robust, you can use those error messages to fix the code and maintain the robustness.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:27:52',321,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe the role of error messages in maintaining robust programs. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>When you get an error message from the code when it\'s not working, you can use that error message to fix your code piece by piece. And once your code is completely working and fixed and will not break from a user input. This means that the code is robust. And if there are any errors whilst you think the code is robust, you can use those error messages to fix the code and maintain the robustness.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that error messages help developers fix issues, which contributes to robustness. Well done!</li><li>To strengthen your answer, try to explain *how* these messages help, for instance, by indicating the specific problem or location in the code.</li><li>Consider adding how clear error messages can also help the *user* understand what went wrong, preventing frustration.</li><li>Think about how good error messages improve the overall maintainability of a program.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, specify that error messages provide information that helps developers understand *what* went wrong, which is crucial for fixing the code effectively.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Error messages are crucial for maintaining robust programs as they provide meaningful information to developers, helping them understand what went wrong and how to fix it. Clear messages prevent frustration for users by explaining issues simply and improve program maintainability by guiding developers efficiently during debugging and updates.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:27:54',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301981621_pup9pci11',1,'2026-06-01 08:27:52','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:27:54',NULL),(2028,61,12,1,7,'<p>Selection lets your program choose between paths</p><p>Iteration repeats a block of multiple code until a condition is met</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:28:14',165,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how iteration and selection are used to control program flow in Python. (2 marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Selection lets your program choose between paths</p><p>Iteration repeats a block of multiple code until a condition is met</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that selection allows the program to choose between paths, which is a great start!</li><li>You also accurately stated that iteration repeats a block of code until a condition is met.</li><li>To improve, consider adding specific examples for each concept, like \'if/elif/else\' for selection or \'for/while loops\' for iteration, to show how they are implemented in Python.</li><li>You could also explain how these concepts *control program flow* more explicitly.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Include specific Python keywords or examples (e.g., if/elif/else, for loops) for both selection and iteration to demonstrate how they control flow.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Selection, using constructs like <code>if</code>, <code>elif</code>, and <code>else</code>, allows a program to choose which code path to execute based on whether a condition is true or false. Iteration, using <code>for</code> or <code>while</code> loops, repeats a block of code multiple times until a specified condition is met.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:28:17',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780302264774_kc2vhgdvq',1,'2026-06-01 08:28:14','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:28:17',NULL),(2029,67,109,1,7,'<ol><li><p>Ensuring you\'re app is supported in different languages so users of all languages can access and understand your app/website</p></li><li><p>Accessibility features for users who struggle using apps or websites without aid like screen tinting for dyslexia</p></li></ol>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:28:44',110,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State two examples of emerging digital technologies affecting software design. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><ol><li><p>Ensuring you\'re app is supported in different languages so users of all languages can access and understand your app/website</p></li><li><p>Accessibility features for users who struggle using apps or websites without aid like screen tinting for dyslexia</p></li></ol><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve identified important aspects of good software design, focusing on user experience and accessibility.</li><li>To improve, consider what \"emerging digital technologies\" means. These are new technologies, not standard design practices like multi-language support.</li><li>Think about technologies that are currently changing how software is built and designed, not just how it\'s used.</li><li>For next time, research or recall examples of brand new technologies that are having a significant impact.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Focus on identifying specific new technologies that are changing software design, rather than user-facing features or design best practices.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>1. Artificial Intelligence (AI)<br>2. Quantum Computing</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:28:46',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1780301577691_t7jm7efaf',1,'2026-06-01 08:28:44','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>What you said was good, but not what they were looking for. It\'s always going to be AI and Quantum</p>','R','2026-06-01 08:30:27',1),(2030,68,178,1,7,'<p>An algorithm is a set of instructions followed in a specific order</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:29:23',22,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define the term ‘algorithm’. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>An algorithm is a set of instructions followed in a specific order</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that an algorithm is a set of instructions, which is a great start!</li><li>To strengthen your definition, try to include the purpose of these instructions. What are they designed to do?</li><li>Consider what an algorithm aims to achieve or solve. Thinking about this will help you capture the full essence of the term.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Expand on the purpose of the instructions; specifically, what task do they perform or what problem do they solve?</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An algorithm is a set of step-by-step instructions designed to perform a specific task or solve a problem.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:29:25',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780302509494_8awy8myxs',1,'2026-06-01 08:29:23','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:29:25',NULL),(2031,59,86,1,7,'<p>Error messages are important in maintaining robust programs as they usually show you what line the code breaks and a generic explanation of why the code broke. This is incredibly helpful in maintaining programs as developers can now easily find the broken line of code and assess it so they can improve upon it.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:29:37',137,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe the role of error messages in maintaining robust programs. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Error messages are important in maintaining robust programs as they usually show you what line the code breaks and a generic explanation of why the code broke. This is incredibly helpful in maintaining programs as developers can now easily find the broken line of code and assess it so they can improve upon it.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You effectively described how error messages help developers identify and fix broken code, which is a great start!</li><li>To strengthen your answer, consider adding how meaningful error messages help the end-user understand what went wrong, not just the developer.</li><li>Think about how clear error messages prevent user frustration and contribute to a program\'s overall maintainability in the long run.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, also discuss how error messages help end-users understand issues and prevent frustration, not just developers.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Error messages are crucial for robust programs as they provide meaningful information to both users and developers. They help users understand what went wrong and how they might resolve it, preventing frustration. For developers, clear error messages pinpoint issues, making it easier to diagnose and fix problems, thereby improving the program\'s maintainability and overall reliability.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:29:40',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780302004062_dq4lgdi0i',2,'2026-06-01 08:29:37','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>There is a classic image of a Microsoft dialog box that says \"Task Failed Successfully\" - how useful is that?</p>','A','2026-06-01 08:32:09',1),(2032,67,183,1,7,'<p>Abstraction is the process of removing unnecessary data to make development smoother as it declutters tasks leaving only the important things</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:30:09',65,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define ‘abstraction’ in problem solving. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Abstraction is the process of removing unnecessary data to make development smoother as it declutters tasks leaving only the important things</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that abstraction involves removing unnecessary details. Great start!</li><li>To strengthen your answer, consider adding that abstraction focuses on the essential aspects of a problem.</li><li>Think about how simplifying a problem by hiding complexity is a key benefit of abstraction.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state that abstraction helps to simplify a problem by focusing on only the essential elements.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Abstraction is the process of simplifying a problem by removing unnecessary details and focusing only on the essential information needed to solve it.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:30:11',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301577691_t7jm7efaf',1,'2026-06-01 08:30:09','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 08:30:46',1),(2033,58,91,1,7,'<p>AI tools can help advance society by increasing the pace of workflow in things such as coding for repetitive tasks and it also allows for employees to multitask such as the employee making code and the ai making the design for a website. However, there are many downsides of generative AI. One such is that it can take away jobs of people like graphic designers, artists and software developers as AI can do all of those things although it is not as good as real people doing them. Another downside is that people eventually become too reliant on AI tools to generate things or do things for them which then leads to a lack of skills for the general population which can be harmful in the long term as people would lose critical thinking skills and the average intelligence of people may become lower  </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:31:22',446,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the societal effects of generative AI tools. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>AI tools can help advance society by increasing the pace of workflow in things such as coding for repetitive tasks and it also allows for employees to multitask such as the employee making code and the ai making the design for a website. However, there are many downsides of generative AI. One such is that it can take away jobs of people like graphic designers, artists and software developers as AI can do all of those things although it is not as good as real people doing them. Another downside is that people eventually become too reliant on AI tools to generate things or do things for them which then leads to a lack of skills for the general population which can be harmful in the long term as people would lose critical thinking skills and the average intelligence of people may become lower  </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You did a great job identifying both benefits and drawbacks of generative AI tools, such as increased workflow and job displacement.</li><li>You clearly discussed how AI can lead to a lack of skills and critical thinking, which is a thoughtful insight into a significant societal effect.</li><li>To improve further, consider discussing other negative aspects like the potential for bias in AI outputs or the spread of misinformation.</li><li>You could also strengthen your answer by analysing how software developers need to consider ethical and legal implications when creating and deploying these tools.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, broaden your discussion of drawbacks to include issues like bias in AI algorithms and the spread of misinformation.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Generative AI tools offer significant societal benefits by enhancing productivity and creativity across various sectors, from automating repetitive tasks in coding to assisting with graphic design, thereby freeing up human workers for more complex problem-solving. They also improve accessibility, allowing more people to create and innovate. However, these tools present considerable drawbacks. There is a risk of job displacement for roles that can be automated, such as some design or writing tasks. Furthermore, generative AI can perpetuate and amplify biases present in its training data, leading to unfair or discriminatory outcomes. The rapid creation of realistic but false content also raises concerns about misinformation and its impact on public trust. Software developers have a critical role in managing these ethical and legal implications by designing AI responsibly, ensuring transparency, and implementing safeguards against bias and misuse.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:31:25',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301373964_2qvt3t0od',1,'2026-06-01 08:31:22','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>I thought what you wrote was perceptive, and certainly would earn a solid 3 or 4 for this question.</p>','A','2026-06-01 08:33:28',1),(2034,67,97,1,7,'<p>By noticing patterns in a problem it makes pinpointing and therefore solving the root problem much easier. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:31:51',85,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how pattern recognition assists problem solving. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>By noticing patterns in a problem it makes pinpointing and therefore solving the root problem much easier. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that pattern recognition helps with pinpointing and solving problems. Well done!</li><li>To gain full marks, consider how identifying patterns helps you connect a new problem to solutions you\'ve used before.</li><li>Think about what you do when you see a pattern – what past knowledge or actions does it allow you to reuse?</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on how recognising patterns allows you to reuse previous solutions or approaches.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Pattern recognition assists problem solving by identifying similarities between the current problem and problems solved previously, allowing for the reuse of known solutions. For example, recognising a common input validation pattern means applying an existing validation routine.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:31:52',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301577691_t7jm7efaf',1,'2026-06-01 08:31:51','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p></p>','A','2026-06-01 08:34:22',1),(2035,70,103,1,7,'<p>Using inefficient algorithms can have some major negative performance issues in terms of software performance. If the algorithm is inefficient, it may not do what the software must do to an extent or at all. This can cause confusion, bad experiences, and even stress for the user, causing them to use alternatives. This means that reputation will be compromised and the amount of users that will use your app or website will be minimal compared to if the algorithm was efficient in what it says it does. If you use inefficient algorithms, security can be a big issue and may cause vulnerabilities in the users safety of their data. Handling data securely is so significant when owning an app as not only will unsecure data protection cause users to feel vulnerable and not want to use your software, legal constraints can cause the app or website to go through major sues, lawsuits or overall fines, costing the company reputation difficulties and fines. One final constraint when using an inefficient algorithm may be that the code can crash easily, this means that user protection is minimised and again may dissatisfy the users experience, if a code crashes and they are doing a task that takes time and the software finds an error, this can corrupt or just not save the users work and means that the user will lose out on time and cause them stress, and choosing other softwares that have more efficient algorithms, Inefficient algortithms can cause software performance to be a deal breaker for users, meaning that they choose other apps or websites as it does not benefit them, making the company lose reputation, money and/or valuable time</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:33:57',516,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Analyse the effect of using inefficient algorithms on software performance. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Using inefficient algorithms can have some major negative performance issues in terms of software performance. If the algorithm is inefficient, it may not do what the software must do to an extent or at all. This can cause confusion, bad experiences, and even stress for the user, causing them to use alternatives. This means that reputation will be compromised and the amount of users that will use your app or website will be minimal compared to if the algorithm was efficient in what it says it does. If you use inefficient algorithms, security can be a big issue and may cause vulnerabilities in the users safety of their data. Handling data securely is so significant when owning an app as not only will unsecure data protection cause users to feel vulnerable and not want to use your software, legal constraints can cause the app or website to go through major sues, lawsuits or overall fines, costing the company reputation difficulties and fines. One final constraint when using an inefficient algorithm may be that the code can crash easily, this means that user protection is minimised and again may dissatisfy the users experience, if a code crashes and they are doing a task that takes time and the software finds an error, this can corrupt or just not save the users work and means that the user will lose out on time and cause them stress, and choosing other softwares that have more efficient algorithms, Inefficient algortithms can cause software performance to be a deal breaker for users, meaning that they choose other apps or websites as it does not benefit them, making the company lose reputation, money and/or valuable time</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You did a great job linking inefficient algorithms to a poorer user experience, which is a key part of software performance. Try to explain *how* the algorithms themselves cause this, rather than focusing on the emotional impact on the user.</li><li>You mentioned crashing and data corruption, which are good points related to performance stability. To strengthen this, consider how inefficient algorithms might directly lead to these issues, perhaps by consuming too many resources.</li><li>You discussed reputation and legal constraints, which are important business impacts. For a question on *software performance*, focus more on the technical aspects like speed and resource usage, and then link these to user satisfaction.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, remember to link inefficiency directly to technical aspects like longer execution times and higher resource usage. Think about what the computer is actually doing when an algorithm is inefficient.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Focus on the technical effects of inefficient algorithms on the software itself, such as increased processing time or memory usage, rather than solely on the user\'s emotional response or business consequences.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Inefficient algorithms significantly degrade software performance by increasing execution times and consuming more system resources like CPU and memory. For example, using a bubble sort instead of a merge sort on a large dataset would lead to much longer processing times. This can result in a poorer user experience due to slow response times or freezing applications. Furthermore, inefficient algorithms can reduce the software\'s scalability, meaning it struggles to handle increased workloads or larger datasets, potentially leading to crashes or unresponsiveness when demand grows.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:34:01',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301689194_mbeqo3aon',1,'2026-06-01 08:33:57','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 08:35:39',1),(2036,70,105,1,7,'<p>Integers are whole numbers, while floats are decimal numbers. for instance an integer would be something like \"4, 5, 8, 20, 103 etc.\" while a float would be \"5.4, 3.8, 10.0 etc.\"</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:35:11',47,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe the difference between integers and floats in Python. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Integers are whole numbers, while floats are decimal numbers. for instance an integer would be something like \"4, 5, 8, 20, 103 etc.\" while a float would be \"5.4, 3.8, 10.0 etc.\"</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that integers are whole numbers and floats are decimal numbers, which is excellent!</li><li>Your examples clearly illustrate the difference between integer and float values.</li><li>To make your answer even stronger, try to explicitly link your examples to how they would be written in Python code.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, specifically show how these examples would look in Python, for instance, by writing `x = 4` for an integer or `y = 5.4` for a float.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Integers in Python are whole numbers, such as `x = 5`. Floats, on the other hand, are numbers that contain a decimal point, representing real numbers, for example, `y = 3.14` or `z = 10.0`.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:35:13',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780301689194_mbeqo3aon',1,'2026-06-01 08:35:11','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 08:35:56',1),(2037,67,174,1,7,'<p>Computational thinking is the process of using problem solving techniques to do various tasks centring around computer science. One of the key components is decomposition which is the act of breaking down a large complex problem into multiple much smaller ones, this makes a big task much more reasonable and easier to manage</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:35:42',99,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define computational thinking and state one of its key components. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Computational thinking is the process of using problem solving techniques to do various tasks centring around computer science. One of the key components is decomposition which is the act of breaking down a large complex problem into multiple much smaller ones, this makes a big task much more reasonable and easier to manage</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully defined computational thinking as a problem-solving process, which is a great start!</li><li>You correctly identified decomposition as a key component and explained it well.</li><li>To fully meet the mark scheme, try to be more specific in your definition of computational thinking by mentioning logical steps.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on the \"problem-solving techniques\" in computational thinking by specifying that it involves breaking problems down into logical steps.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Computational thinking is a problem-solving process that involves breaking down complex problems into logical steps. One of its key components is decomposition, which is the process of breaking a large problem into smaller, more manageable parts.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:35:44',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780302753264_qpe2pgsa3',1,'2026-06-01 08:35:42','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Nailed it.</p>','G','2026-06-01 08:36:55',1),(2038,83,91,1,7,'<p>Generative AI tools will have many drastic effects on society - both positive and negative. </p><p>Generative AI tools - such as large language models - have many educational purposes as well as automating jobs that require huge amounts of people (for example, social media moderation). These tools may also aid in scientific and medical developments - as they may help to cure diseases and discover new technologies. </p><p>These tools also have many downsides however, for example, training AI models often uses vast amounts of processing power, which leads to huge power consumption, and large amounts of water being used as coolant. Even though this water will return to the surface, it may not return in the same spots, leading to certain areas suffering droughts. AI also causes distrust in photographic and video evidence in the justice system, where innocent people are incarcerated for crimes they did not commit, and perpetrators get away scot-free. AI also replaces many jobs, leading to mass unemployment. This makes the rich significantly richer, and the poor without income. There are also risks that AI could be used to generate explicit material of minors or other unwilling people. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:35:57',439,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the societal effects of generative AI tools. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Generative AI tools will have many drastic effects on society - both positive and negative. </p><p>Generative AI tools - such as large language models - have many educational purposes as well as automating jobs that require huge amounts of people (for example, social media moderation). These tools may also aid in scientific and medical developments - as they may help to cure diseases and discover new technologies. </p><p>These tools also have many downsides however, for example, training AI models often uses vast amounts of processing power, which leads to huge power consumption, and large amounts of water being used as coolant. Even though this water will return to the surface, it may not return in the same spots, leading to certain areas suffering droughts. AI also causes distrust in photographic and video evidence in the justice system, where innocent people are incarcerated for crimes they did not commit, and perpetrators get away scot-free. AI also replaces many jobs, leading to mass unemployment. This makes the rich significantly richer, and the poor without income. There are also risks that AI could be used to generate explicit material of minors or other unwilling people. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You effectively discussed a range of benefits, such as educational purposes, job automation in specific areas, and scientific/medical advancements. Great job providing concrete examples!</li><li>You also clearly outlined several drawbacks, including environmental impacts, the issue of misinformation in the justice system, job displacement, and the potential for misuse. This shows a good understanding of the negative societal effects.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, consider expanding on how software developers must manage the ethical and legal implications of these tools. This would add depth to your evaluation.</li><li>Think about how the benefits you mentioned (like productivity and creativity) could be further elaborated, perhaps with specific examples of how they empower individuals or industries.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly address the role of software developers in managing the ethical and legal challenges presented by generative AI.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Generative AI tools present a complex array of societal effects. Positively, they can significantly boost productivity across various industries by automating repetitive tasks, freeing human workers for more creative and complex roles. They enhance creativity by offering new tools for artists, designers, and writers, and improve accessibility for individuals with disabilities through assistive technologies. In education, they can provide personalized learning experiences. However, there are significant drawbacks. Generative AI can perpetuate and amplify biases present in its training data, leading to unfair or discriminatory outcomes. It also contributes to the spread of misinformation and deepfakes, eroding trust in digital content and posing challenges for media literacy and justice systems. Job displacement is a major concern as AI automates roles, potentially widening economic inequality. Software developers bear a crucial responsibility in managing these ethical and legal implications, needing to implement robust safeguards against bias, ensure transparency, and develop secure systems to prevent misuse and protect intellectual property rights.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:36:01',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',2,'2026-06-01 08:35:57','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:36:01',NULL),(2039,65,197,1,7,'<p>i believe that if there is a dramatic increase in automation and AI in the workplace, then this will lead to a massive drop in the needs for the employees. This is because they will not need to be able to do very much before hand because the AI that will be doing most of the work will be doing all of the hard work for them.</p><p>Firstly, this is not a new risk, automation has been going on for a very long time. For example, in building and construction there used to be a high demand that the workers are very physically fit, however now since there are many machines that help a lot with their job they don\'t have to reach that demand anymore, or at least the demand of fitness isn\'t as high.</p><p>Furthermore, its not only construction where this has been happening, automation and AI is slowly becoming a big part in coding. This is because there are many \"Vibe Coders\" who solely use AI and just paste in what the AI has done fore them and claim it as their own work.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:36:10',372,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss the impact of automation and AI on employment and skill requirements. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>i believe that if there is a dramatic increase in automation and AI in the workplace, then this will lead to a massive drop in the needs for the employees. This is because they will not need to be able to do very much before hand because the AI that will be doing most of the work will be doing all of the hard work for them.</p><p>Firstly, this is not a new risk, automation has been going on for a very long time. For example, in building and construction there used to be a high demand that the workers are very physically fit, however now since there are many machines that help a lot with their job they don\'t have to reach that demand anymore, or at least the demand of fitness isn\'t as high.</p><p>Furthermore, its not only construction where this has been happening, automation and AI is slowly becoming a big part in coding. This is because there are many \"Vibe Coders\" who solely use AI and just paste in what the AI has done fore them and claim as their own work.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You effectively discussed the potential for a \"massive drop in the needs for employees\" and provided good historical context with the construction example. Well done!</li><li>You also touched upon how skill requirements change, noting the reduced demand for physical fitness in construction. To strengthen this, consider discussing how new skills might be required.</li><li>To improve, you could explore the \"efficiency gains\" that automation and AI bring, not just the potential job loss.</li><li>Your response focused primarily on the negative impacts. For a more balanced discussion, think about the positive societal implications or new job opportunities that might arise.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Discuss the positive impacts and benefits of automation and AI on employment and skill requirements to provide a more balanced argument.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Automation and AI significantly impact employment by increasing efficiency and productivity, leading to potential job displacement in repetitive tasks. However, it also creates new roles in areas like AI development, maintenance, and data analysis. Skill requirements shift from manual labour to tasks requiring critical thinking, problem-solving, and digital literacy, such as managing automated systems or interpreting AI outputs. While some jobs may be lost, others are augmented, requiring workers to adapt and upskill, fostering a workforce focused on higher-value tasks and innovation. This balance can lead to economic growth and improved working conditions.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:36:14',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301981621_pup9pci11',1,'2026-06-01 08:36:10','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Good reflection. However \"Discuss\" always expects a balanced response and the top marks go to a conclusion at the end of that.</p>','A','2026-06-01 08:38:35',1),(2040,59,90,1,7,'<p>An increased use of digital systems will allow people with malicious intent to understand digital systems better to figure out how to work around them to release malware and gain unauthorised access into other digital systems. The greater understanding the public have over digital systems that they gain from increased use the more likely cyber attacks are to happen as they understand how to get past digital systems security.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:37:48',336,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how privacy concerns arise from increased use of digital systems. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>An increased use of digital systems will allow people with malicious intent to understand digital systems better to figure out how to work around them to release malware and gain unauthorised access into other digital systems. The greater understanding the public have over digital systems that they gain from increased use the more likely cyber attacks are to happen as they understand how to get past digital systems security.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a good start by considering the risks associated with digital systems, but your answer focuses more on cybersecurity threats like malware and unauthorised access rather than privacy.</li><li>To improve, think about what \"privacy\" means in a digital context. It\'s about how personal information is collected, stored, and used.</li><li>Consider how increased use of digital systems leads to more personal data being generated and shared, which can then raise privacy issues.</li><li>The mark scheme mentions data collection, surveillance, and digital footprints; try to incorporate these ideas into your explanation.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Focus your answer on the collection and use of personal data and how this creates privacy concerns, rather than solely on cyberattacks.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Increased use of digital systems leads to greater collection of personal data, creating privacy concerns. Every interaction, from online purchases to social media use, contributes to a digital footprint that can be tracked. This raises worries about who has access to this data, how it might be used (e.g., for surveillance or targeted advertising), and the potential for misuse without explicit user consent. Legislation like GDPR aims to address these concerns by giving individuals more control over their personal information.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:37:50',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780302004062_dq4lgdi0i',2,'2026-06-01 08:37:48','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:37:50',NULL),(2041,70,19,1,7,'<p>To make a test plan for a python program, a flowchart would be sensible. you would carry this out by starting the program, reading the file and outputting the desired output given by the user.</p><p></p><p>Start -&gt; [Read File of Student Scores] -&gt; (Which student score do you want to see?) -&gt;[Validate user input] -&gt; (Output grade of the specified students score) -&gt; END</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:37:57',156,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Design and justify a testing plan for a Python program that reads a file of student scores and outputs grades.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>To make a test plan for a python program, a flowchart would be sensible. you would carry this out by starting the program, reading the file and outputting the desired output given by the user.</p><p></p><p>Start -&gt; [Read File of Student Scores] -&gt; (Which student score do you want to see?) -&gt;[Validate user input] -&gt; (Output grade of the specified students score) -&gt; END</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve started to think about the program\'s flow, which is a good first step! Remember to focus on designing *tests* rather than just the program\'s operations.</li><li>Consider how you would test different parts of the program, like ensuring the file reads correctly or that the grading logic works for all scores.</li><li>Think about specific test cases, including what data you would use (valid and invalid) and what output you would expect for each.</li><li>To fully meet the criteria, you\'ll need to justify *why* each test is important, linking it back to the program\'s required functionality.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Focus on identifying specific types of tests (e.g., unit tests for functions, boundary tests for grade cut-offs) and for each, provide a clear test case with input data and the expected result.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A testing plan for the student grading program would involve unit, boundary, and integration testing. Unit tests would verify individual functions, such as the `read_scores` function for correct file parsing and the `calculate_grade` function for accurate grade assignments. For `calculate_grade`, boundary tests are crucial, using scores exactly at grade cut-offs (e.g., 49, 50, 59, 60) and just above/below to ensure correct grading (e.g., A, B, C, Fail). Integration testing would then ensure the entire process, from file reading to grade output, works seamlessly. This would include testing with a valid score file, an empty file, and a file with invalid data types. Expected results would be correctly processed grades, error messages for invalid files, or appropriate handling for empty files. Justification for these tests is to ensure data integrity, accurate grade calculation, and robust error handling.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:38:01',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301689194_mbeqo3aon',1,'2026-06-01 08:37:57','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:38:01',NULL),(2042,62,99,1,7,'<p>Count controlled loops will output a value to a user a set number of times, this could mean setting the i in range to 5 and ask for the users age 5 times. Condition controlled loops will loop or output a value while the condtion equals true or false, this could be asking a user for their name while the condition equals false and then switching it to true when the users name is correctly inputted.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:38:14',268,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Compare count-controlled and condition-controlled loops. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Count controlled loops will output a value to a user a set number of times, this could mean setting the i in range to 5 and ask for the users age 5 times. Condition controlled loops will loop or output a value while the condtion equals true or false, this could be asking a user for their name while the condition equals false and then switching it to true when the users name is correctly inputted.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that count-controlled loops run for a set number of times, which is a great start to your comparison!</li><li>You also accurately explained that condition-controlled loops repeat based on a condition being true or false. Well done!</li><li>To strengthen your answer, try to explicitly name the common loop types (e.g., `for` for count-controlled and `while` for condition-controlled).</li><li>Consider adding a point about which type of loop might be more suitable in different scenarios or contexts to show a deeper understanding.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Explicitly mention the typical keywords used for each type of loop, such as `for` for count-controlled and `while` for condition-controlled loops, to make your explanation more precise.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Count-controlled loops, typically implemented with `for` statements, execute a fixed number of times, making them suitable when the exact number of iterations is known beforehand. For example, looping 10 times to process 10 items. Condition-controlled loops, often using `while` statements, continue to execute until a specified condition becomes false. They are useful when the number of iterations is unknown and depends on runtime factors, such as continuously asking for user input until valid data is provided. Condition-controlled loops offer more flexibility but require careful handling to prevent infinite loops.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:38:17',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301649912_nz8qtk6n0',1,'2026-06-01 08:38:14','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:38:17',NULL),(2043,67,185,1,7,'<p>Data type conversations are used across python programs to allow for more operations on values. By using data type conversations you could take a string user input and convert it into an integer, this allows you to do math operations on the value which would previously not work before. Their main purpose is to take one value of data and convert it into another.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:38:15',70,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe the purpose of data type conversion functions in Python. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Data type conversations are used across python programs to allow for more operations on values. By using data type conversations you could take a string user input and convert it into an integer, this allows you to do math operations on the value which would previously not work before. Their main purpose is to take one value of data and convert it into another.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained that the main purpose is to convert one data type to another, which is a great start!</li><li>You provided a good example of converting a string input to an integer to enable mathematical operations. This shows a strong understanding of the practical application.</li><li>To make your answer even stronger, consider directly mentioning one of the specific Python functions used for conversion, like <code>int()</code>, <code>float()</code>, or <code>str()</code>.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, include an example of a specific Python function used for data type conversion, such as <code>int()</code> or <code>str()</code>.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Data type conversion functions in Python are used to change a value from one data type to another, for example, converting a string into an integer. This is essential for compatibility between different parts of a program, allowing operations that would otherwise not be possible. For instance, using <code>int()</code> allows you to convert user input received as a string into a number so that mathematical calculations can be performed.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:38:17',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780302753264_qpe2pgsa3',1,'2026-06-01 08:38:15','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>The Computer Science term for data type conversion is \"casting\"</p>','G','2026-06-01 08:39:36',1),(2044,83,181,1,7,'<p>Validation is a step carried out before data processing, where data or user inputs are cleansed of invalid data, or potentially rejected. This is to prevent algorithms or parsers from crashing or behaving strangely after recieving inputs they are not built to handle.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:38:28',85,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain what validation means in the context of programming. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Validation is a step carried out before data processing, where data or user inputs are cleansed of invalid data, or potentially rejected. This is to prevent algorithms or parsers from crashing or behaving strangely after recieving inputs they are not built to handle.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained that validation is a step before data processing, which is a great start!</li><li>You correctly identified that validation helps prevent issues like crashes, showing good understanding of its purpose.</li><li>To fully meet the mark scheme, try to include how validation checks data against expected rules or formats.</li><li>Consider giving an example of a specific rule, like a range check or a format check for an email address.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, mention that validation specifically checks if data meets predefined rules or formats (e.g., a number within a certain range).</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Validation in programming means checking input data against predefined rules or criteria before processing it. This ensures the data is in the expected format or range, preventing errors, crashes, or unexpected behavior in the program.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:38:30',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',2,'2026-06-01 08:38:28','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:38:30',NULL),(2045,65,89,1,7,'<p>Artificial Intelligence is a program that can kind of think based on what they can access and research on the internet, it can have no free thinking ideas because it is controlled and regulated.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:38:54',77,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define the term artificial intelligence in the context of emerging issues. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Artificial Intelligence is a program that can kind of think based on what they can access and research on the internet, it can have no free thinking ideas because it is controlled and regulated.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve touched on the idea of AI being a program that processes information, which is a good start. Try to elaborate on the types of tasks these programs perform.</li><li>Consider focusing on how AI systems mimic human cognitive abilities rather than just \"thinking.\"</li><li>To achieve higher marks, you could mention the specific contexts where AI is increasingly being used, like automation or software development.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Focus on defining AI by the *types of tasks* it performs that typically require human intelligence, such as problem-solving or learning.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Artificial intelligence refers to systems that can perform tasks normally requiring human intelligence, such as decision-making, problem-solving, or pattern recognition. These systems are increasingly being integrated into automation and software development.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:38:56',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301981621_pup9pci11',1,'2026-06-01 08:38:54','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Don\'t forget the more technical term: \"Large Language Models (LLMs)\"</p>','A','2026-06-01 09:13:30',1),(2046,64,14,1,7,'<p>Linear search\'s search data does not need to be sorted before searching, whereas binary searches data needs to be sorted. Linear searching is less complex but it takes more time than binary search. Binary search is more complex than linear as it requires sorted data that then halves itself to organise said data. Linear search checks each data sequentially until the target is found or the list ends. Linear search should be used when you want to find data in a small dataset that can be easily sorted. A binary search should be used to find data within a large dataset that isn\'t sorted.</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:39:17',1051,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the difference between a linear and binary search algorithm and when each should be used. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Linear search\'s search data does not need to be sorted before searching, whereas binary searches data needs to be sorted. Linear searching is less complex but it takes more time than binary search. Binary search is more complex than linear as it requires sorted data that then halves itself to organise said data. Linear search checks each data sequentially until the target is found or the list ends. Linear search should be used when you want to find data in a small dataset that can be easily sorted. A binary search should be used to find data within a large dataset that isn\'t sorted.</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that a linear search checks each element sequentially and that the data for a binary search must be sorted. Well done!</li><li>You also accurately explained that linear search is less complex but takes more time than binary search. This shows a good understanding of their efficiency.</li><li>You mentioned binary search \"halves itself,\" which is a good step, but try to explain this division process more clearly as repeatedly dividing the search space.</li><li>Be careful with your reasoning for when to use each: linear search is suitable for small datasets, but binary search is most effective for large, *already sorted* datasets.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clarify that binary search needs data to be sorted *before* it can be used effectively and that it works by repeatedly dividing the sorted list in half to quickly narrow down the search.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A linear search checks each item in a list sequentially until the target is found or the end of the list is reached. It does not require the data to be sorted. A binary search repeatedly divides a *sorted* list in half, checking the middle element to determine which half the target might be in, until the item is found. Linear search should be used for small datasets or when the data is unsorted. Binary search is much faster and should be used for large datasets that are already sorted.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:39:20',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301740964_rueo49u3t',2,'2026-06-01 08:39:17','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 09:11:53',1),(2047,59,11,1,7,'<p>Pattern recognition is when you look back on previous projects or tasks that are similar to the current project or tasks and apply the same solution or a modified solution to the current project in order to try solve it. Abstraction is when you only focus on the essential details of the project or task and ignore the unnecessary data and information.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:40:36',142,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the difference between pattern recognition and abstraction in computational thinking. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Pattern recognition is when you look back on previous projects or tasks that are similar to the current project or tasks and apply the same solution or a modified solution to the current project in order to try solve it. Abstraction is when you only focus on the essential details of the project or task and ignore the unnecessary data and information.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You have clearly defined both pattern recognition and abstraction well.</li><li>You successfully identified the core concepts of both terms.</li><li>To achieve full marks, try to explicitly contrast the two concepts to highlight their differences more clearly.</li><li>Adding a brief, simple example for either concept would strengthen your explanation.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Explicitly state how pattern recognition and abstraction differ from each other in their purpose or application within computational thinking.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Pattern recognition involves identifying similarities, trends, or recurring themes across different problems or data sets. Abstraction, on the other hand, is the process of simplifying a problem by removing unnecessary details to focus only on the essential information relevant to solving it. For example, recognising that multiple parts of a program require user input validation (pattern recognition) can lead to designing a single, reusable function that handles only the core validation logic (abstraction).</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:40:38',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780302004062_dq4lgdi0i',2,'2026-06-01 08:40:36','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>My mark: 2</p>','G','2026-06-01 09:05:46',1),(2048,70,18,1,7,'<p>Validating data allows its relevance and usability to be significantly more efficient and usable and can also in python, allow inputs given by the user to not crash, even if they give the wrong data type. Doing things like try and except in python can allow for data validation to be maximised allowing the code to try the data type they give and except the data type if it is not what the python program seeks. This means that the program minimises the chance of it crashing and allows to validate the data the user gives, this can also work in pandas, if you are trying to validate if the data is in the data frame.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:40:49',157,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how validation techniques improve data integrity, with Python examples. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Validating data allows its relevance and usability to be significantly more efficient and usable and can also in python, allow inputs given by the user to not crash, even if they give the wrong data type. Doing things like try and except in python can allow for data validation to be maximised allowing the code to try the data type they give and except the data type if it is not what the python program seeks. This means that the program minimises the chance of it crashing and allows to validate the data the user gives, this can also work in pandas, if you are trying to validate if the data is in the data frame.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that validation helps prevent programs from crashing due to incorrect data types, which is a great start.</li><li>You mentioned `try-except` blocks, which are useful for handling errors, but focus on the specific validation checks (like length or range) that determine if data is valid in the first place.</li><li>To improve, provide specific examples of validation checks such as checking if an age is between 0 and 120, or if a password meets a minimum length requirement.</li><li>Consider explaining how these checks directly improve data integrity by ensuring data is accurate and reliable.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Provide specific Python code examples for different validation techniques like range checks or length checks to clearly show how they prevent invalid data entry.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Validation techniques improve data integrity by ensuring that only accurate and appropriate data enters a system, preventing issues like incorrect calculations or system errors. This is achieved through various checks: presence checks ensure data is not missing, length checks verify data meets minimum/maximum character counts, range checks confirm numerical values fall within expected bounds (e.g., age between 0 and 120), type checks verify data is of the correct format (e.g., integer, string), and format checks ensure data adheres to a specific pattern (e.g., email address). For instance, in Python, `if 0 <= age <= 120:` performs a range check. Validation reduces runtime errors, improves user experience by providing immediate feedback, and maintains the reliability and trustworthiness of stored data.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:40:52',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301689194_mbeqo3aon',1,'2026-06-01 08:40:49','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>I liked this answer, but could only award it 4.</p>','A','2026-06-01 08:42:44',1),(2049,65,10,1,7,'<p>Decomposition is extremely useful in problem solving because it breaks down the problem into multiple smaller, more manageable tasks</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:41:00',57,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>What is the purpose of decomposition in problem solving? (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Decomposition is extremely useful in problem solving because it breaks down the problem into multiple smaller, more manageable tasks</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that decomposition breaks a problem into smaller, more manageable tasks, which is a great start!</li><li>To achieve full marks, try to explain *why* breaking it down into smaller parts is useful.</li><li>Consider what happens after the problem is broken down – what\'s the next step?</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explain that breaking down the problem allows each sub-problem to be solved individually, and then combined to form a complete solution.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Decomposition is the process of breaking a complex problem into smaller, more manageable sub-problems so that each can be solved individually and later combined into a complete solution.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:41:02',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780301981621_pup9pci11',2,'2026-06-01 08:41:00','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 08:41:40',1),(2050,67,77,1,7,'<p>Using the top down approach, you can pinpoint the issue of a much larger problem in software development. You take the main large problem and slowly break it down until you can locate the root cause of the issue, this makes problem solving a much smoother process.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:41:27',128,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how the top-down approach assists in solving software problems. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Using the top down approach, you can pinpoint the issue of a much larger problem in software development. You take the main large problem and slowly break it down until you can locate the root cause of the issue, this makes problem solving a much smoother process.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that the top-down approach involves breaking down a larger problem. Well done!</li><li>To fully meet the criteria, you could explain that this breakdown specifically involves creating smaller sub-systems.</li><li>Consider mentioning how this approach aids in writing main functions first and then refining the details.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, clarify that the breaking down of the problem creates smaller, manageable sub-systems.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The top-down approach assists by starting with the overall software system and systematically breaking it down into smaller, more manageable sub-systems. This allows developers to focus on the main functions first and refine specific details later, simplifying problem identification and resolution.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:41:29',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780303113637_fg4unisj1',1,'2026-06-01 08:41:27','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>My Mark: 2</p>','G','2026-06-01 09:04:55',1),(2051,58,87,1,7,'<p>There are many benefits to using loops for iteration and one such benefit is that is simplifies code by significantly reducing the lines of code written. another benefit is that we can loop a certain block of code for as long as we want it to and in cases where we don\'t know how many times the code will be needed to be looped, a while loop would give flexibility on how many times we want to repeat the code without actually doing much and by making a certain condition to end the loop. However if loops are not used carefully, then they could cause more harm than good. An example of this would be forgetting to make a condition to exit a while loop means that the code will run a certain block of code within that loop forever</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:41:37',459,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Analyse the benefits and drawbacks of using loops for iteration. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>There are many benefits to using loops for iteration and one such benefit is that is simplifies code by significantly reducing the lines of code written. another benefit is that we can loop a certain block of code for as long as we want it to and in cases where we don\'t know how many times the code will be needed to be looped, a while loop would give flexibility on how many times we want to repeat the code without actually doing much and by making a certain condition to end the loop. However if loops are not used carefully, then they could cause more harm than good. An example of this would be forgetting to make a condition to exit a while loop means that the code will run a certain block of code within that loop forever</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve clearly identified benefits like code simplification and flexibility, which is a great start!</li><li>You also successfully identified a major drawback: the risk of infinite loops when a condition to exit isn\'t met.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, remember to explicitly reference both `for` and `while` loops and show how each type contributes to iteration.</li><li>Consider expanding on other potential logic errors that can arise when using loops.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, make sure to explicitly mention both `for` and `while` loops in your analysis of benefits and drawbacks.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Loops offer significant benefits for iteration by automating repetitive tasks, greatly reducing code repetition, and making programs more efficient. For example, a `for` loop is ideal when the number of iterations is known, such as processing each item in a list, while a `while` loop provides flexibility for an unknown number of iterations, continuing until a specific condition is met. However, loops also have drawbacks. Incorrect loop conditions can lead to infinite loops, consuming system resources and freezing programs. Furthermore, subtle logic errors within loop conditions or body can cause unexpected behaviour, incorrect results, or even crashes, making debugging more challenging.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:41:40',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301373964_2qvt3t0od',1,'2026-06-01 08:41:37','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Need to use both correct terminology and examples for this: fixed iteration - for loops and conditional iteration - while loops</p>','A','2026-06-01 09:04:12',1),(2052,70,17,1,7,'<p>Advantages of using pre-written libraries like pandas and matplotlib can be that it allows the coder to have more tools in their program making it far more efficient and detailed. A disadvantage of this could be that the coder has to learn more and also include more comments to ensure that the person reviewing their code can understand what it does, even if they have never studied the specific pre-written library. Pre-Written Libraries can allow users to have far more context in a program, allowing them to visualise data using something like matplotlib for instance, or get analysis and data on data inside a data frame using pandas for instance. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:43:42',160,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the advantages and disadvantages of using pre-written libraries in software development. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Advantages of using pre-written libraries like pandas and matplotlib can be that it allows the coder to have more tools in their program making it far more efficient and detailed. A disadvantage of this could be that the coder has to learn more and also include more comments to ensure that the person reviewing their code can understand what it does, even if they have never studied the specific pre-written library. Pre-Written Libraries can allow users to have far more context in a program, allowing them to visualise data using something like matplotlib for instance, or get analysis and data on data inside a data frame using pandas for instance. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified some advantages, such as increased efficiency and the ability to perform complex tasks like data visualisation with libraries like `matplotlib` and `pandas`.</li><li>You touched on a disadvantage related to learning new tools, but you could expand on other drawbacks like dependency issues or potential security risks.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, consider explicitly evaluating the trade-offs rather than just listing points.</li><li>Well done for including specific examples of libraries; this really strengthens your points.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to explore a broader range of disadvantages, such as the risks associated with external dependencies or version conflicts, to provide a more balanced evaluation.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Using pre-written libraries offers significant advantages, such as dramatically reducing development time as developers don\'t need to write code from scratch for common functionalities (e.g., using `pandas` for data manipulation). These libraries are often well-tested by large communities, leading to increased reliability and fewer bugs in the final product. For instance, `matplotlib` provides robust and efficient plotting functions. However, there are disadvantages. Projects become dependent on external code, introducing risks if the library is no longer maintained or contains security vulnerabilities. Version conflicts can also arise when integrating multiple libraries. Furthermore, over-reliance on libraries can limit a developer\'s understanding of the underlying core logic, impacting their problem-solving skills for unique challenges.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:43:45',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301689194_mbeqo3aon',1,'2026-06-01 08:43:42','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>My Mark: 4</p>','A','2026-06-01 09:01:27',1),(2053,65,21,1,7,'<p>Digital inclusion is very important for software design, because when you are designing the program you are going to make you need to think about the digital capabilities of the users and what they can realistically do and work out, this helps the developer think if they need to have instructions on the page and if the final product will be too complicated for the user to understand </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:43:57',170,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define digital inclusion and explain why it is important in software design. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Digital inclusion is very important for software design, because when you are designing the program you are going to make you need to think about the digital capabilities of the users and what they can realistically do and work out, this helps the developer think if they need to have instructions on the page and if the final product will be too complicated for the user to understand </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a good start on explaining why digital inclusion is important, focusing on user capabilities and ease of understanding.</li><li>To fully define digital inclusion, remember to include that it means ensuring *all* users can access and benefit from digital services.</li><li>Consider mentioning the different groups of users who might face barriers, such as those with disabilities, different ages, or limited resources, to strengthen your definition.</li><li>For the importance aspect, you could also link it to removing bias or meeting accessibility standards.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, make sure to explicitly define digital inclusion as providing access to digital services for *everyone*, regardless of their individual circumstances or abilities.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Digital inclusion is about ensuring everyone, regardless of their age, ability, or resources, can access and benefit from digital services and technology. It\'s important in software design to create products that are usable and accessible to the widest possible audience, preventing exclusion and ensuring fair access for all users, often by adhering to accessibility standards.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:44:00',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1780301981621_pup9pci11',1,'2026-06-01 08:43:57','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Accessibility is the key issue: screen contrast and size, screen readers, semantic html, audio prompts, non-mouse navigation etc,</p><p>That issues surrounding poverty: Developing World infrastructure (ie in much of Africa, 4G is the method of connected rather than broadband)</p>','R','2026-06-01 08:53:04',1),(2054,83,194,1,7,'<p>Abstraction is where unnessesary data is stripped away, leaving only the data required to solve a specific problem. This makes the overall task not only easier to digest, but also allowing for it to be carried out by a computer. However, abstraction may lead to crucial data being lost in the process. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:45:02',370,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss the advantages and drawbacks of using abstraction when solving digital problems. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Abstraction is where unnessesary data is stripped away, leaving only the data required to solve a specific problem. This makes the overall task not only easier to digest, but also allowing for it to be carried out by a computer. However, abstraction may lead to crucial data being lost in the process. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly defined abstraction and identified the advantage of simplification, which is great!</li><li>You also correctly identified a key drawback: the potential loss of crucial data. Well done!</li><li>To achieve higher marks, consider expanding on how abstraction aids in problem-solving beyond just making tasks \"easier to digest.\"</li><li>Think about how abstraction specifically relates to designing algorithms or managing complexity in larger systems.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on the practical applications of abstraction in digital problem solving, such as how it facilitates the design of algorithms or helps manage complexity in software development.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Abstraction simplifies complex digital problems by stripping away unnecessary details, allowing developers to focus on essential aspects. This makes the problem easier to understand, manage, and design algorithms for, improving efficiency and clarity in the development process. For instance, when designing a game, developers might abstract complex physics into simpler movement rules. However, a significant drawback is the potential to oversimplify, leading to the omission of crucial details that might impact the accuracy or functionality of the solution. This oversight can result in errors or an incomplete understanding of the problem space.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:45:05',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',1,'2026-06-01 08:45:02','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:45:05',NULL),(2055,66,195,1,7,'<p>Debugging contributes to robust code in multiple ways. One way that debugging contributes to the creation of robust code is through the process of find and eliminating bugs from the code it means that the code will obviously, fail less and mean that less errors effect the code.<br>Another way that debugging contributes to the creation of robust code is that the procceses of debugging while improve secrity features as it would reduce the possiblilties of exploiting or breaking security features, thus improving the robust nature of the code.<br>Another way that debugging contributes to the robust nature of code is that debugging while improve reliblility and reduce the chance of crashes and errors meaning th code is more likly to run fine, thus being more robust.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:47:08',1300,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate how debugging contributes to the creation of robust code. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Debugging contributes to robust code in multiple ways. One way that debugging contributes to the creation of robust code is through the process of find and eliminating bugs from the code it means that the code will obviously, fail less and mean that less errors effect the code.<br>Another way that debugging contributes to the creation of robust code is that the procceses of debugging while improve secrity features as it would reduce the possiblilties of exploiting or breaking security features, thus improving the robust nature of the code.<br>Another way that debugging contributes to the robust nature of code is that debugging while improve reliblility and reduce the chance of crashes and errors meaning th code is more likly to run fine, thus being more robust.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve successfully identified that debugging helps eliminate errors and improves reliability, which is a great start.</li><li>You also touched upon how debugging can improve security by reducing vulnerabilities, showing good insight into the broader impact.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, you could explicitly mention some specific debugging techniques, such as using trace tables or various testing methods.</li><li>Consider elaborating on the iterative nature of debugging, where problems are found, fixed, and then re-tested to ensure code robustness.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to include specific examples of debugging techniques or processes, like using trace tables or different types of testing.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Debugging significantly contributes to robust code by systematically identifying and correcting errors, which directly enhances the software\'s reliability and stability. Through techniques such as step-through debugging, breakpoint analysis, and the use of trace tables, developers can pinpoint the exact location and cause of issues. This iterative process of testing, debugging, and re-testing ensures that the code behaves as expected under various conditions, reducing the likelihood of crashes or unexpected behaviour. Furthermore, debugging can uncover security vulnerabilities, preventing potential exploits. By resolving these issues, the code becomes more resilient, trustworthy, and maintainable, leading to a truly robust solution.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:47:12',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301430024_trdc84ig5',1,'2026-06-01 08:47:08','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 08:50:17',1),(2056,67,99,1,7,'<p>Count controller loops are a form of loop that is set to run a set number of times, this in most scenarios is a for loop which loops until a set objective is met. For example in python using a for loop with range of a number, the for loop goes until it meets the number of times set. Condition controller loops run endlessly until a set condition is met, this is a while loop often. In python, a while loop may be done to create a unique number for example looping until the number is not in already in a list.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:47:19',117,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Compare count-controlled and condition-controlled loops. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Count controller loops are a form of loop that is set to run a set number of times, this in most scenarios is a for loop which loops until a set objective is met. For example in python using a for loop with range of a number, the for loop goes until it meets the number of times set. Condition controller loops run endlessly until a set condition is met, this is a while loop often. In python, a while loop may be done to create a unique number for example looping until the number is not in already in a list.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that count-controlled loops run a set number of times and provided a good example using a Python <code>for</code> loop.</li><li>You also correctly identified that condition-controlled loops (<code>while</code> loops) repeat until a condition is met and gave a clear example.</li><li>To improve, consider directly comparing the \"fixed number of times\" aspect of count-controlled loops with the \"until a condition changes\" aspect of condition-controlled loops.</li><li>For higher marks, you could evaluate when each type of loop might be safer or more efficient in different contexts.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly state the fundamental difference between the two types of loops in terms of when they stop repeating, making a direct comparison.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Count-controlled loops (e.g., a <code>for</code> loop) are designed to execute a predetermined, fixed number of times. The number of iterations is known before the loop begins. Condition-controlled loops (e.g., a <code>while</code> loop), in contrast, continue to execute repeatedly until a specific condition becomes false. The number of iterations is not fixed and depends entirely on when the condition changes. Condition-controlled loops are generally safer when the number of iterations is unknown and could lead to errors if fixed, while count-controlled loops are more efficient when the exact number of repetitions is known in advance.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:47:22',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780303294776_6df9bcnrz',1,'2026-06-01 08:47:19','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 08:49:18',1),(2057,64,74,1,7,'<p>an algorithm is a step by step set of instructions that solve a problem</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:48:08',183,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define algorithm. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>an algorithm is a step by step set of instructions that solve a problem</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that an algorithm is a step-by-step set of instructions. Well done!</li><li>You also clearly stated that algorithms are used to solve a problem. This is a key part of the definition.</li><li>To make your answer even stronger, try to include the idea of \"computation\" as well as \"solving a problem.\"</li><li>Consider mentioning that algorithms are precise. This helps differentiate them from general instructions.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Add the idea that algorithms are used for \"performing a computation\" to make your definition more comprehensive.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An algorithm is a precise, step-by-step sequence of instructions used to solve a problem or perform a computation.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:48:10',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301740964_rueo49u3t',1,'2026-06-01 08:48:08','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 08:48:38',1),(2058,83,90,1,7,'<p>Embedded cameras and microphones in devices such as phones and computers may create privacy risks as malware and other malicious applications may use these to spy on their owners. How users interact with these devices also carries privacy concerns. For example, companies such as google track activity to sell to advertisers. This violates the privacy of the user. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:48:57',211,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how privacy concerns arise from increased use of digital systems. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Embedded cameras and microphones in devices such as phones and computers may create privacy risks as malware and other malicious applications may use these to spy on their owners. How users interact with these devices also carries privacy concerns. For example, companies such as google track activity to sell to advertisers. This violates the privacy of the user. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You did well to identify that malware can use embedded devices for surveillance, which is a good point about privacy risks.</li><li>You correctly linked the tracking of activity by companies like Google to advertising, showing an understanding of data collection for commercial purposes.</li><li>To improve, consider expanding on the concept of a \'digital footprint\' and how consistent data collection over time builds a profile.</li><li>Thinking about user consent and the potential misuse of personal information would strengthen your answer.</li><li>For a higher mark, you could mention relevant legislation like GDPR and how it aims to protect user privacy.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on how the collection of user data contributes to a \'digital footprint\' and the long-term privacy implications.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Increased use of digital systems raises privacy concerns through extensive data collection, surveillance, and the creation of digital footprints. Personal information, from browsing habits to location data, is often collected, sometimes without explicit user consent. This data can be used for targeted advertising, but also has the potential for misuse, such as identity theft or discrimination. Malware can facilitate unauthorised surveillance through device cameras and microphones. Legislation like GDPR aims to protect user privacy by dictating how personal data is collected, processed, and stored, requiring consent and giving individuals rights over their information.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:49:00',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',1,'2026-06-01 08:48:57','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:49:00',NULL),(2059,70,16,1,7,'<p>Naming conventions, code style, and things like white space, comments etc maintain and make code extremely more easy to read, it is an easy method for code reviewers to add and understand what your code already does. </p><p></p><p>Firstly, accurate variable names can allow for far more understanding on what a variable may hold and allows for people to have more context on the program they have and also allows maintenance on the code because it easy to track what has been done and what is yet to be completed in a program. </p><p></p><p>Code style, including indents, white space and functions can allow for code to be easily read and adapted to if needed, if the code style is unreadable, people who review or want to add to the code will not know where to start or what has or hasnt been done.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:50:45',398,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Analyse why naming conventions and code style matter for readability and maintenance. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Naming conventions, code style, and things like white space, comments etc maintain and make code extremely more easy to read, it is an easy method for code reviewers to add and understand what your code already does. </p><p></p><p>Firstly, accurate variable names can allow for far more understanding on what a variable may hold and allows for people to have more context on the program they have and also allows maintenance on the code because it easy to track what has been done and what is yet to be completed in a program. </p><p></p><p>Code style, including indents, white space and functions can allow for code to be easily read and adapted to if needed, if the code style is unreadable, people who review or want to add to the code will not know where to start or what has or hasnt been done.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You effectively explained how naming conventions and code style improve readability and make code easier to understand for others, especially during code reviews.</li><li>You correctly linked good naming to easier maintenance, specifically in tracking progress and understanding variable purpose.</li><li>You mentioned how consistent style helps with adapting code, which is great, but try to elaborate more on specific style elements like camelCase or snake_case for a stronger answer.</li><li>To achieve a higher mark, consider explicitly connecting improved readability to a reduction in logical errors or enhanced team collaboration.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly discuss how consistent styles directly contribute to preventing logical errors and fostering better collaboration within a development team.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Naming conventions and code style are crucial for readability and maintenance because they ensure consistency, making code easier to understand for developers. Consistent styles, such as using camelCase for variables or snake_case for functions, along with proper indentation and commenting, allow teams to quickly grasp the code\'s purpose and flow. This improved readability significantly reduces the likelihood of introducing logical errors during development or when debugging. For maintenance, a clear and consistent style means new team members can onboard faster, and existing members can efficiently locate and modify sections of code. This also fosters better collaboration, as everyone can follow the same predictable structure, making it simpler to extend functionality or fix bugs without extensive effort to decipher poorly formatted code.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:50:49',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301689194_mbeqo3aon',1,'2026-06-01 08:50:45','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>There are document standards like JSDocs which ensure that code is properly documented in line.</p><p>Examples would have helped greatly.</p>','A','2026-06-01 08:55:23',1),(2060,59,183,1,7,'<p>Abstraction is focusing only on the essential details of a task or projects and removing the unnecessary data or information</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:53:41',271,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define ‘abstraction’ in problem solving. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Abstraction is focusing only on the essential details of a task or projects and removing the unnecessary data or information</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained that abstraction involves focusing on essential details, which is excellent!</li><li>You also correctly identified that it includes removing unnecessary data or information. Well done!</li><li>To make your answer even stronger, try to explicitly link these actions to the idea of simplifying the problem or solution.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state that the purpose of removing unnecessary details is to simplify the problem or solution.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Abstraction is the process of focusing on the essential details of a problem while ignoring or removing the unnecessary complexity to simplify the solution.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:53:43',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780302004062_dq4lgdi0i',2,'2026-06-01 08:53:41','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 09:00:25',1),(2061,83,87,1,7,'<p>Loops allow for a set of instructions to be executed as many times as is nessasary. This allows to large amounts of data to be processed, as well as allowing for algorithms that loop endlessly. However, loops may continue forever or for extremely long amounts of time if not implemented correctly, or if an inefficient algorithm is used. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:55:53',278,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Analyse the benefits and drawbacks of using loops for iteration. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Loops allow for a set of instructions to be executed as many times as is nessasary. This allows to large amounts of data to be processed, as well as allowing for algorithms that loop endlessly. However, loops may continue forever or for extremely long amounts of time if not implemented correctly, or if an efficient algorithm is used. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified the benefit of automating repetitive tasks and processing large amounts of data, which is a key advantage of using loops.</li><li>You also accurately highlighted the significant drawback of loops potentially running indefinitely or for very long times due to incorrect implementation or inefficient algorithms. This demonstrates good understanding of a common pitfall.</li><li>To enhance your answer, consider specifically mentioning how loops reduce code repetition, making your programs more concise and easier to maintain.</li><li>For an even stronger response, next time try to reference specific types of loops, like Python\'s \'for\' and \'while\' loops, and perhaps discuss the importance of loop control mechanisms.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly reference different types of loops (e.g., \'for\' and \'while\' loops) to show a deeper understanding of their practical application.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Loops are highly beneficial for iteration as they automate repetitive tasks, significantly reducing code repetition and making programs more efficient and readable. This is particularly useful for processing large datasets or executing a block of code a specific number of times or until a condition is met, using constructs like Python\'s `for` and `while` loops. However, a major drawback is the risk of infinite loops if termination conditions are not correctly defined or met, leading to programs crashing or becoming unresponsive. Logic errors within the loop condition or body can also be difficult to debug, potentially causing incorrect results or performance issues if the loop runs for an excessively long time due to inefficient design.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:55:56',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',1,'2026-06-01 08:55:53','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 08:55:56',NULL),(2062,58,27,1,7,'<p>Professional code of conducts are important to software developers because they create ethical standards and practices for software developers and also allows for a programmer to be recognised for the technical competence. Without these software developers may not be recognised for their skills and may end up not following ethical standards which can then end up effecting their employability meaning that they cannot get a job </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:56:17',628,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the importance of professional codes of conduct (e.g. BCS, IAP) for software developers. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Professional code of conducts are important to software developers because they create ethical standards and practices for software developers and also allows for a programmer to be recognised for the technical competence. Without these software developers may not be recognised for their skills and may end up not following ethical standards which can then end up effecting their employability meaning that they cannot get a job </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by identifying that codes promote ethical standards and practices, which is a key aspect of the mark scheme.</li><li>You also touched upon competence and recognition, showing you understand how codes can validate a developer\'s skills.</li><li>To improve your evaluation, consider discussing how codes build public trust and accountability, and perhaps even touch on avoiding conflicts of interest.</li><li>For a higher mark, think about contrasting the benefits with any potential challenges in applying these codes in real-world commercial situations.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to expand on how professional codes benefit the public and the industry as a whole, not just the individual developer\'s employability.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Professional codes of conduct are crucial for software developers as they establish ethical standards, ensuring integrity and promoting responsible practice within the profession. They also signify competence, assuring clients and the public of a developer\'s technical ability and commitment to quality. This fosters public trust in software and the developers creating it. By providing guidelines, codes help avoid conflicts of interest and maintain accountability, although applying abstract principles in diverse commercial contexts can be a challenge. Ultimately, they elevate the profession\'s standing and uphold high standards of software development.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:56:20',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301373964_2qvt3t0od',1,'2026-06-01 08:56:17','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>I would score that answer as a 2. It was okay, but for a 5 marker you need a lot more.</p>','A','2026-06-01 08:59:28',1),(2063,67,21,1,7,'<p>Ensuring your app is supported in different languages so users of all languages can access and understand your app/website</p><p>Accessibility features for users who struggle using apps or websites without aid like screen tinting for dyslexia</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 08:58:22',113,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define digital inclusion and explain why it is important in software design. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Ensuring your app is supported in different languages so users of all languages can access and understand your app/website</p><p>Accessibility features for users who struggle using apps or websites without aid like screen tinting for dyslexia</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that digital inclusion is about making software accessible to a wider range of users, which is a great start.</li><li>You provided excellent specific examples like language support and screen tinting for dyslexia, showing a good understanding of practical applications.</li><li>To improve, consider broadening your definition to explicitly include all users regardless of ability, age, or resources, not just language and specific accessibility needs.</li><li>Think about how factors beyond language and specific disabilities, such as socio-economic status or older age groups, might impact access to digital services.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Expand your definition of digital inclusion to encompass all users, regardless of age, resources, or ability, to fully capture its breadth.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Digital inclusion is ensuring that all individuals, regardless of their age, ability, or socio-economic background, can access and effectively use digital services and technologies. It\'s important in software design because it helps to create equitable experiences, preventing exclusion and ensuring that the benefits of technology are available to everyone. This includes considering accessibility standards and reducing biases in design choices.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 08:58:25',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780304183489_fyqk3tvbc',1,'2026-06-01 08:58:22','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>You\'d get 2 from me on this.</p>','G','2026-06-01 09:00:11',1),(2064,66,88,1,7,'<p>Algorithmic efficency is important because an algorithms efficiensy is how quickly it comes to the intended solution. So essintialy the time it takes from algorithm start to outputing or solving to the correct resault. One example that demonstrates the importance if algorithmic efficieny is 2 search algorithms, if one takes 10ms to find the item and the 2nd take 20ms, it makes a very small diffrence, but when scalled up to very large data sets where Terabytes of even Petabytes of data might need to be search through it is important the the algorithm is efficient.<br>Algorithmic efficiency can  be measured in time complixity, or the time it will take for the algorithm to search in the worst possible case (in the format O N^2 for example) it can also be measuered in direct compition between algorithms or measuered in milliaseconds.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:00:40',767,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain why algorithm efficiency matters and how it can be measured. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Algorithmic efficency is important because an algorithms efficiensy is how quickly it comes to the intended solution. So essintialy the time it takes from algorithm start to outputing or solving to the correct resault. One example that demonstrates the importance if algorithmic efficieny is 2 search algorithms, if one takes 10ms to find the item and the 2nd take 20ms, it makes a very small diffrence, but when scalled up to very large data sets where Terabytes of even Petabytes of data might need to be search through it is important the the algorithm is efficient.<br>Algorithmic efficiency can  be measured in time complixity, or the time it will take for the algorithm to search in the worst possible case (in the format O N^2 for example) it can also be measuered in direct compition between algorithms or measuered in milliaseconds.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained why efficiency matters, linking it to the time taken to find a solution, especially with large datasets, which is excellent.</li><li>You correctly identified time complexity (Big O notation) as a way to measure efficiency, and mentioned the \"worst possible case.\"</li><li>Consider also mentioning the impact of efficiency on memory usage, as this is another key benefit of efficient algorithms.</li><li>To enhance your measurement explanation, you could also describe measuring efficiency by counting specific operations like comparisons or steps, in addition to execution time.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly include memory usage as a reason why algorithm efficiency is important.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Algorithm efficiency matters because it directly impacts the resources consumed, specifically processing time and memory. An efficient algorithm can process data quicker, leading to faster user experiences and reduced operational costs, especially when dealing with large datasets or high-volume transactions. Less efficient algorithms can cause slowdowns, crashes, or require more expensive hardware. Efficiency can be measured in several ways. Time complexity analyzes the number of operations an algorithm performs as the input size grows, often expressed using Big O notation (e.g., O(n), O(n^2)), considering best, worst, and average cases. Space complexity measures the amount of memory an algorithm uses. Alternatively, efficiency can be measured empirically by recording execution time in milliseconds or by counting specific operations, such as comparisons or steps, for different input sizes.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:00:46',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780301430024_trdc84ig5',1,'2026-06-01 09:00:40','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>My mark: 5</p>','G','2026-06-01 09:02:19',1),(2065,83,22,1,7,'<p>AI is automating many of the tasks traditionally given to software developers. This will reduce the number of software developers required for a tasks, decreasing total costs but also reducing the number of job positions. This leads to mass unemployment and layoffs. </p><p>The wider adoptation of IOT devices leads to more software that needs to be created. This increases the number of software development jobs, especially as many of these applications are crucial and should not be developed by AI.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:01:37',229,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how emerging technologies such as AI and IoT are changing software development. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>AI is automating many of the tasks traditionally given to software developers. This will reduce the number of software developers required for a tasks, decreasing total costs but also reducing the number of job positions. This leads to mass unemployment and layoffs. </p><p>The wider adoptation of IOT devices leads to more software that needs to be created. This increases the number of software development jobs, especially as many of these applications are crucial and should not be developed by AI.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that AI is automating tasks in software development, which is a great start. To strengthen this point, consider how AI specifically helps with things like code generation or testing.</li><li>You also recognised that IoT creates a need for more software, linking it to an increase in job positions. Try to expand on the *types* of software development unique to IoT, such as embedded systems or real-time data processing.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, remember to discuss both the benefits and potential drawbacks beyond just job numbers, such as privacy or security implications for new software.</li><li>Consider how developers themselves must adapt their skills and coding practices to work with these emerging technologies.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, expand on the specific ways AI assists software development tasks (e.g., testing, debugging) and how IoT impacts the *types* of software created (e.g., real-time, distributed systems).</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>AI is changing software development by automating tasks like code generation, testing, and debugging, which can improve efficiency and allow developers to focus on more complex problems. It also enables the creation of more intelligent, predictive systems. IoT devices drive the need for new software, particularly for real-time data collection, remote control, and managing distributed systems. This requires developers to adapt their skills for areas like embedded systems and cloud integration. While these technologies bring innovation and efficiency, they also introduce new challenges related to data privacy, security, and the complexity of managing highly connected systems.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:01:40',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',1,'2026-06-01 09:01:37','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:01:40',NULL),(2066,65,180,1,7,'<p>While loop (condition controlled), For loop (Count controlled)</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:04:51',1158,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Identify two types of loops used in Python. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>While loop (condition controlled), For loop (Count controlled)</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You have correctly identified two types of loops used in Python, a \'While loop\' and a \'For loop\'.</li><li>You have accurately described the control mechanism for each loop, \'condition controlled\' and \'count controlled\'.</li><li>This response fully meets the requirements of the question.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Your answer is excellent; keep up the great work!</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>For loop (count-controlled), While loop (condition-controlled)</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:04:53',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780301981621_pup9pci11',1,'2026-06-01 09:04:51','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 09:06:07',1),(2067,60,99,1,7,'<p>Count controlled loops are used when there is a fixed amount of loops, for example 4, or 9.</p><p>Condition-controlled loops are used when you don\'t know how many times to loop, and wait until a certain condition is met, for example \'while isAlive == True:\'</p><p>Most of the time, condition controlled loops will be used, as count-controlled loops are very situational and only used to repeat a block of code a certain amount of times. Condition-controlled loops are more interactive</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:06:16',121,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Compare count-controlled and condition-controlled loops. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Count controlled loops are used when there is a fixed amount of loops, for example 4, or 9.</p><p>Condition-controlled loops are used when you don\'t know how many times to loop, and wait until a certain condition is met, for example \'while isAlive == True:\'</p><p>Most of the time, condition controlled loops will be used, as count-controlled loops are very situational and only used to repeat a block of code a certain amount of times. Condition-controlled loops are more interactive</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained the core difference: count-controlled loops run a fixed number of times, and condition-controlled loops repeat until a condition changes. Well done!</li><li>You provided excellent examples for both types of loops, which helps illustrate your understanding.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, consider explicitly naming the typical loop structures used for each type, e.g., \'for\' and \'while\'.</li><li>You touched upon the idea of when each loop type is used, which is a good step towards evaluating their efficiency or safety. Try to elaborate on this further next time.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Explicitly name the common loop structures (e.g., \'for\' for count-controlled, \'while\' for condition-controlled) to strengthen your comparison.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Count-controlled loops (e.g., `for` loops) execute a fixed number of times, determined at the start of the loop. Condition-controlled loops (e.g., `while` loops) repeat until a specified condition becomes false. While count-controlled loops are predictable and safer against infinite loops, condition-controlled loops are more flexible as they can handle situations where the number of repetitions is unknown, making them more suitable for interactive programs or processing external data. However, `while` loops require careful design to avoid infinite loops.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:06:19',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780304437719_mcqoqzak5',1,'2026-06-01 09:06:16','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Should have mentioned \'for\' loops. My Mark: 2</p>','A','2026-06-01 09:07:46',1),(2068,70,90,1,7,'<p>Increasing dependencies on digital systems, like banking, and managing significant things can unfortunately come with risks, if the bank/website/app is hacked, you are susceptible to losing access to accounts, data taken, losing money and raising vulnerability rather than having physical cards and using them instead of things  like apple pay, and overall physical copies are gonna be more secure as digital copies are easy to intercept if DDOS attacks occur on big banking apps</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:06:53',147,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how privacy concerns arise from increased use of digital systems. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Increasing dependencies on digital systems, like banking, and managing significant things can unfortunately come with risks, if the bank/website/app is hacked, you are susceptible to losing access to accounts, data taken, losing money and raising vulnerability rather than having physical cards and using them instead of things  like apple pay, and overall physical copies are gonna be more secure as digital copies are easy to intercept if DDOS attacks occur on big banking apps</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that losing access to accounts and having data taken are privacy concerns. Try to expand on how this data collection happens in general use, not just through hacking.</li><li>You touched on the idea of vulnerability. Consider discussing how continuous monitoring (surveillance) by digital systems contributes to privacy concerns beyond just a security breach.</li><li>You mentioned digital interactions like Apple Pay. Think about how the \"digital footprint\" we leave behind with every online action creates privacy concerns.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, remember to link your points to user consent and the potential misuse of personal information, perhaps mentioning relevant legislation.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Focus on explaining how privacy concerns arise from the *normal operation* of digital systems (e.g., data collection, surveillance) rather than solely on risks from cyberattacks like hacking or DDoS.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Privacy concerns arise from the extensive data collection by digital systems, often without explicit user consent, leading to large digital footprints. This data can be used for surveillance or profiling, creating concerns about who has access to personal information and how it might be misused. The potential for data breaches and the lack of transparency in how data is processed further exacerbate these worries, highlighting the importance of legislation like GDPR to protect individual privacy rights.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:06:56',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301689194_mbeqo3aon',1,'2026-06-01 09:06:53','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>PRIVACY!</p>','A','2026-06-01 09:09:20',1),(2069,58,26,1,7,'<p>The purpose of an AUP is to outline the behaviours and regulations in a document a person has to follow and agree to when using a business or corporate computer network. It is used to make a person accountable for their actions for things involving the equipment and data of the company</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:07:29',256,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the purpose and content of an Acceptable Use Policy (AUP).(5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The purpose of an AUP is to outline the behaviours and regulations in a document a person has to follow and agree to when using a business or corporate computer network. It is used to make a person accountable for their actions for things involving the equipment and data of the company</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by clearly explaining the core purpose of an AUP, which is to outline expected behaviours and make users accountable.</li><li>To fully address the \"content\" aspect of the question, consider what specific types of activities an AUP might permit or prohibit.</li><li>You could also expand on the broader organisational benefits, such as how an AUP helps protect the company.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to include specific examples of what content would be found within an AUP, like communication etiquette or rules for data handling.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The purpose of an Acceptable Use Policy (AUP) is to clearly define the permitted and prohibited activities when using an organisation\'s IT systems and networks. Its content typically includes guidelines for appropriate communication, internet usage, software installation, data handling, and the use of company equipment. AUPs also outline the potential penalties for breaching the policy. This helps protect the organisation from misuse, ensures data confidentiality, and maintains professional standards among users.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:07:31',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301373964_2qvt3t0od',1,'2026-06-01 09:07:29','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Needs more in examples. My Mark: 2</p>','A','2026-06-01 09:08:39',1),(2070,83,15,1,7,'<p>Data type conversion functions allow for data to be formatted in such a way that the data will be consistent and easy to process. For example, a string input can be converted into an integer or float to allow it to be used in numerical operations. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:08:35',376,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss how data type conversion functions support robust code in Python. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Data type conversion functions allow for data to be formatted in such a way that the data will be consistent and easy to process. For example, a string input can be converted into an integer or float to allow it to be used in numerical operations. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that conversion allows different data types to be used in operations, like converting a string to an integer for numerical tasks.</li><li>To strengthen your answer, consider specifically mentioning common conversion functions like <code>int()</code>, <code>float()</code>, <code>str()</code>, and <code>bool()</code>.</li><li>Think about how these conversions specifically *prevent errors* in your code, making it more robust.</li><li>Next time, try to provide a more concrete example, perhaps involving user input from <code>input()</code> and how it\'s converted.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Elaborate on *how* data type conversions make code robust by preventing type errors and ensuring correct behavior of calculations, providing examples of specific functions used.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Data type conversion functions like <code>int()</code>, <code>float()</code>, <code>str()</code>, and <code>bool()</code> are crucial for robust Python code by preventing type errors and ensuring data is in the correct format for operations. For instance, user input obtained via <code>input()</code> is always a string; converting it to an <code>int()</code> or <code>float()</code> allows arithmetic calculations to be performed correctly without raising a <code>TypeError</code>. This ensures consistency in data handling and allows mixed-type operations to execute predictably, supporting more reliable and error-free programs. While robust, it\'s also important to consider validation to handle cases where conversion might fail (e.g., trying to convert \"hello\" to an integer).</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:08:38',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',1,'2026-06-01 09:08:35','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:08:38',NULL),(2071,60,18,1,7,'<p>Validation techniques imrpove data integrity, one example of this is checking if a username is in a database before checking if the password is correct.</p><p>\'\'\'if username in Database:\'\'\'</p><p></p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:09:03',50,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how validation techniques improve data integrity, with Python examples. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Validation techniques imrpove data integrity, one example of this is checking if a username is in a database before checking if the password is correct.</p><p>\'\'\'if username in Database:\'\'\'</p><p></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that validation improves data integrity and provided a relevant example of checking a username. Great start!</li><li>To improve, consider explaining different types of validation checks beyond just existence, such as type, length, or range checks.</li><li>For each type of check, try to provide a brief Python code example to illustrate how it works.</li><li>Think about how these checks specifically prevent invalid data from entering a system, rather than just checking existing data.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Expand your answer to include several distinct types of validation checks (e.g., presence, length, range, type, format) and provide a Python example for each.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Validation techniques ensure data integrity by preventing invalid data from entering a system. This improves reliability and reduces errors. Common checks include: <br><ul><li><b>Presence checks:</b> Ensuring data is not left blank. E.g., `if not username:`</li><li><b>Length checks:</b> Verifying data meets a minimum/maximum length. E.g., `if len(password) < 8:`</li><li><b>Range checks:</b> Confirming numerical data falls within an expected range. E.g., `if not 0 <= age <= 120:`</li><li><b>Type checks:</b> Ensuring data is of the correct type. E.g., `if not isinstance(age, int):`</li><li><b>Format checks:</b> Validating data matches a specific pattern (e.g., email address format). E.g., using regular expressions for email patterns.</li></ul><br>These checks catch errors early, improving user experience by providing immediate feedback and reducing runtime errors in the application. However, validation should be carefully balanced to avoid rejecting valid inputs.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:09:06',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1780304847437_b29u2be80',1,'2026-06-01 09:09:03','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>A bit of a meta-example. Focus on the more mundane:</p><p><code>if (name.length==0) { # reject here }</code></p><p></p>','R','2026-06-01 09:11:28',1),(2072,59,12,1,7,'<p>Iteration is used to repeat a set block of code multiple times using for/while statements. Selection allows the user to chose which path the program takes using if/elif/else statements.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:11:38',426,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how iteration and selection are used to control program flow in Python. (2 marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Iteration is used to repeat a set block of code multiple times using for/while statements. Selection allows the user to chose which path the program takes using if/elif/else statements.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that iteration repeats code and selection chooses a path, which is a great start!</li><li>You\'ve accurately named the Python statements used for both iteration (for/while) and selection (if/elif/else).</li><li>To enhance your answer, consider adding a brief mention of what criteria or conditions drive these choices or repetitions.</li><li>Think about how a condition being true or false affects the flow for both selection and iteration.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, briefly explain that iteration repeats until a condition is met, and selection chooses a path based on a condition.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Iteration repeats a block of code multiple times using \'for\' or \'while\' loops until a specified condition is met. Selection (using \'if\', \'elif\', \'else\' statements) allows the program to choose different paths of execution based on whether a condition is true or false.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:11:40',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780302004062_dq4lgdi0i',2,'2026-06-01 09:11:38','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 09:12:23',1),(2073,66,110,1,7,'<p>Automation affects employment in the digital sector in multiple different ways. Some new jobs are created for the development and management of automated systems but broadly in the digital sector large layoffs due to automated systems replacing human employees, a specific problem in the digital sector is the replacement of software developers, graphic designers and other digital sector workers by AI. This has began to decrease employment in the digital sector despite it still being a growing sector.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:12:36',667,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how automation affects employment in the digital sector. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Automation affects employment in the digital sector in multiple different ways. Some new jobs are created for the development and management of automated systems but broadly in the digital sector large layoffs due to automated systems replacing human employees, a specific problem in the digital sector is the replacement of software developers, graphic designers and other digital sector workers by AI. This has began to decrease employment in the digital sector despite it still being a growing sector.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully identified that automation creates some new jobs, demonstrating a good understanding of one aspect of its impact.</li><li>You clearly explained how automation can lead to job displacement, providing specific examples within the digital sector like software developers and graphic designers.</li><li>To achieve full marks, consider expanding on the types of new jobs created, perhaps mentioning roles in maintenance, oversight, or ethical AI development.</li><li>Think about how automation increases efficiency, as this is a core reason for its adoption and subsequent impact on employment.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on the specific kinds of new jobs created by automation, such as roles in AI ethics, system maintenance, or data analysis, to provide a more balanced view.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Automation in the digital sector increases efficiency by automating repetitive tasks, which can lead to the reduction of certain roles as human employees are replaced. However, it also creates new jobs in areas such as the development, maintenance, and oversight of automated systems and AI. This includes roles in AI ethics, data science, and specialised technical support, balancing the impact on overall employment.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:12:39',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301430024_trdc84ig5',1,'2026-06-01 09:12:36','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:12:39',NULL),(2074,65,105,1,7,'<p>integers are whole numbers, whereas floats are decimal numbers</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:12:46',24,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe the difference between integers and floats in Python. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>integers are whole numbers, whereas floats are decimal numbers</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that integers are whole numbers, which is a great start.</li><li>You also accurately stated that floats are decimal numbers, covering the core difference.</li><li>To achieve full marks, remember to mention that floats represent \"real numbers,\" which is the more formal term.</li><li>Providing a quick example for each type, like `x=5` for an integer and `y=5.5` for a float, would further strengthen your answer.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to include a simple Python example for both an integer and a float to illustrate your description.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Integers are whole numbers without decimal points (e.g., `x=5`), while floats are real numbers that can have decimal points (e.g., `y=5.5`).</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:12:48',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780305128014_kb1anqa1k',1,'2026-06-01 09:12:46','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:12:48',NULL),(2075,65,94,1,7,'<p>breaking down a large task into smaller, more manageable tasks</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:13:16',23,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>What is meant by decomposition?.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>breaking down a large task into smaller, more manageable tasks</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You have successfully identified the core concept of breaking down a large task into smaller ones, which is excellent!</li><li>To achieve a stronger answer, consider adding why this process is beneficial in programming.</li><li>Think about how breaking problems down can help with coding and fixing errors.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, briefly explain *why* breaking down problems is helpful in the context of programming, such as making it easier to code or debug.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Decomposition is the process of breaking a large or complex problem into smaller, more manageable sub-problems. This approach supports modular coding and makes debugging easier.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:13:18',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780305128014_kb1anqa1k',1,'2026-06-01 09:13:16','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>I\'ve give you that mark.</p>','G','2026-06-01 09:13:53',1),(2076,67,229,1,12,'<p>Cloud computing brings many benefits to a company or user with some drawbacks. Cloud computing means companies don\'t have to spend money maintaining their own server and handling their own means of security or backups. Cloud computing is also much cheaper than hosting and maintaining your own server, however this is also a drawback. Cloud computing comes with a monthly recurring charge, most people would consider this is a drawback. As well as this, if someone was to get access to your account credentials thats enough to get access to your entire cloud.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:13:41',312,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss the benefits and challenges of cloud computing. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Cloud computing brings many benefits to a company or user with some drawbacks. Cloud computing means companies don\'t have to spend money maintaining their own server and handling their own means of security or backups. Cloud computing is also much cheaper than hosting and maintaining your own server, however this is also a drawback. Cloud computing comes with a monthly recurring charge, most people would consider this is a drawback. As well as this, if someone was to get access to your account credentials thats enough to get access to your entire cloud.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified cost-effectiveness as a benefit, noting reduced server maintenance. Well done!</li><li>You also clearly highlighted security risks, specifically mentioning account credential compromise. This is a very important point.</li><li>To strengthen your answer further, consider discussing other benefits like scalability or accessibility.</li><li>You could also expand on other challenges such as vendor lock-in or dependency on internet connectivity.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to include a wider range of benefits and challenges to demonstrate a broader understanding of cloud computing.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Cloud computing offers significant benefits such as scalability, allowing resources to be easily adjusted, and cost-effectiveness by reducing hardware and maintenance expenses. It also provides enhanced accessibility, enabling users to access data from anywhere. However, challenges include potential security risks, as data is stored by third-party providers, and dependency on internet connectivity. There\'s also the risk of vendor lock-in, making it difficult to switch providers.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:13:43',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780304867739_vg2bb8xm8',1,'2026-06-01 09:13:41','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>My Mark: 3</p>','A','2026-06-01 09:20:44',1),(2077,64,190,1,7,'<p>The computer misuse act protects organisations by making sure employees follow certain laws while using computers. This means that if an employee were to leak data within the company, they will face consequences such as prison or unemployment. this alone doesnt fully protect organisations from bad actors, but it gives serious consequence for the actions.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:14:15',570,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how the Computer Misuse Act protects organisations. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The computer misuse act protects organisations by making sure employees follow certain laws while using computers. This means that if an employee were to leak data within the company, they will face consequences such as prison or unemployment. this alone doesnt fully protect organisations from bad actors, but it gives serious consequence for the actions.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that the Act provides serious consequences for actions such as leaking data, which is a good start.</li><li>You mentioned employees, but the Act also criminalises actions by external \"bad actors\" like hackers. Consider broadening your scope next time.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, explicitly state that the Act criminalises \"unauthorised access\" and \"unauthorised modification\" of computer material.</li><li>Think about how these criminalisations act as a \"deterrent\" to protect organisations.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly state the specific actions that the Computer Misuse Act criminalises, such as unauthorised access or modification of computer systems.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The Computer Misuse Act protects organisations by criminalising unauthorised access to computer material (hacking) and unauthorised modification of computer material (such as deleting or altering data). This provides a legal framework that deters individuals, both internal and external, from misusing computer systems and information, thereby safeguarding organisational data and operations through potential serious consequences like imprisonment.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:14:17',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301740964_rueo49u3t',1,'2026-06-01 09:14:15','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:14:17',NULL),(2078,67,220,1,12,'<p>UAT testing is mainly used to ensure a program is ready for day-to-day usage and will work sufficiently enough to cause no issues for customers.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:14:41',42,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State one purpose of user acceptance testing (UAT). (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>UAT testing is mainly used to ensure a program is ready for day-to-day usage and will work sufficiently enough to cause no issues for customers.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that UAT aims to ensure a program is ready for use, which is a great start.</li><li>You mentioned the goal of avoiding issues for customers, which touches on the \"meets user needs\" aspect of UAT.</li><li>To fully meet the mark, try to explicitly link this to verifying that the system satisfies the original requirements or user expectations.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, specifically mention that UAT verifies the system meets user requirements or needs before it goes live.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>One purpose of UAT is to verify that the system meets the specified user requirements and is fit for its intended purpose before deployment.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:14:43',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780304867739_vg2bb8xm8',1,'2026-06-01 09:14:41','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:14:43',NULL),(2079,83,17,1,7,'<p>Pre written libraries allow for a large portion of the software development process to be skipped entirely. Not only are these libraries often written by experts in whatever area they cover, but in scripting languages like python, they often execute much faster than native code. </p><p>However this may come with licencing issues, as well as reducing flexibility when developing an application. Often these libraries may be closed source, which prevents editing of code. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:15:04',310,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the advantages and disadvantages of using pre-written libraries in software development. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Pre written libraries allow for a large portion of the software development process to be skipped entirely. Not only are these libraries often written by experts in whatever area they cover, but in scripting languages like python, they often execute much faster than native code. </p><p>However this may come with licencing issues, as well as reducing flexibility when developing an application. Often these libraries may be closed source, which prevents editing of code. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly identified several advantages, such as reduced development time and expert-written code, which is a great start.</li><li>You also brought up important disadvantages like licensing issues and reduced flexibility, showing a good understanding of potential problems.</li><li>To improve, consider expanding on the specific benefits like increased reliability or community testing that libraries often provide.</li><li>Think about other common drawbacks, such as dependency management or the risk of version conflicts, to make your evaluation even more comprehensive.</li><li>You could strengthen your answer by providing specific examples of libraries (like `matplotlib` or `pandas`) and how they demonstrate these points.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Provide specific examples of pre-written libraries and link them to the advantages or disadvantages you discuss.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Using pre-written libraries offers significant advantages by reducing coding time, as much functionality is already implemented and tested. Libraries like `pandas` for data analysis or `matplotlib` for plotting in Python allow developers to leverage expert-written, highly optimised, and community-tested code, leading to greater reliability and faster development cycles. </p><p>However, disadvantages include potential dependency risks, where updates to a library might break existing code. Developers also face version conflicts when multiple libraries require different versions of the same dependency. Additionally, relying heavily on libraries can reduce a developer\'s understanding of core logic, and open-source libraries may introduce licensing complexities or limitations on customisation, reducing flexibility for specific project goals.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:15:07',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',1,'2026-06-01 09:15:04','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:15:07',NULL),(2080,65,75,1,7,'<p>abstraction is simplifying a concept to make it simplified, an example of abstraction is minecraft because its a lot simpler than a full detail game</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:15:16',81,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>What is meant by abstraction in computational thinking?. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>abstraction is simplifying a concept to make it simplified, an example of abstraction is minecraft because its a lot simpler than a full detail game</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that abstraction involves simplifying a concept. Well done!</li><li>To improve, try to explain *how* abstraction simplifies things, rather than just stating it is simplified.</li><li>Think about what is removed when you simplify something through abstraction.</li><li>Consider what information is left behind or kept, and why it\'s important.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, clarify that abstraction simplifies by *removing unnecessary detail* to focus on only the relevant information.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Abstraction in computational thinking means removing unnecessary details from a problem to focus only on the essential, relevant information, thereby simplifying it and making it easier to solve.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:15:17',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780305128014_kb1anqa1k',1,'2026-06-01 09:15:16','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:15:17',NULL),(2081,70,202,1,7,'<p>GDPR allows for safety of consumers of an app or website and means the company is liable for the users safety and is responsible for digital data outbreaks from malicious attacks, they are reposinsible for the users security and must make a secure program before publishing with frequent security updates and patches</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:16:43',100,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Assess how legislation such as GDPR shapes organisational responsibility for digital data. (8 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>GDPR allows for safety of consumers of an app or website and means the company is liable for the users safety and is responsible for digital data outbreaks from malicious attacks, they are reposinsible for the users security and must make a secure program before publishing with frequent security updates and patches</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that GDPR makes organisations responsible for user safety and security, which is a great start!</li><li>To strengthen your answer, consider specific rights GDPR gives users, such as the right to access their data or withdraw consent.</li><li>Think about the consequences for organisations if they don\'t comply with GDPR beyond just being \"liable.\"</li><li>You could also mention the concept of accountability in more detail, showing how organisations must demonstrate their compliance.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly name some of the key individual rights granted by GDPR, such as the right to user consent for data processing.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>GDPR significantly shapes organisational responsibility by mandating user consent for data processing and granting individuals rights such as the right to access their data, rectify inaccuracies, and request deletion. Organisations are accountable for demonstrating compliance with these principles through robust data protection measures. Non-compliance can lead to severe penalties, including substantial fines, making data security and privacy a critical legal and financial responsibility.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:16:45',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301689194_mbeqo3aon',1,'2026-06-01 09:16:43','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:16:45',NULL),(2082,65,96,1,7,'<p>comments are useful so that someone who is reading over the code and trying to figure out what it does, it makes it much easy for them to understand because it explains what each step of the code does</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:17:26',104,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain why comments are used in Python programs. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>comments are useful so that someone who is reading over the code and trying to figure out what it does, it makes it much easy for them to understand because it explains what each step of the code does</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained that comments help others understand the code, which is excellent!</li><li>To strengthen your answer, consider adding that comments also improve the readability of the program.</li><li>Think about how comments help when a program needs fixing or new features added.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to include how comments aid in maintaining or debugging code in the future.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Comments are used in Python programs to explain the purpose of code, making it more readable and understandable for others. They are also vital for maintaining, debugging, or extending a program without altering its behaviour.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:17:28',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780305128014_kb1anqa1k',1,'2026-06-01 09:17:26','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 09:25:38',1),(2083,67,233,1,12,'<p>Regular security audits ensure a companies security is up-to-date and working well enough to protect against the latest security vulnerabilities, malware and attacks. Without security audits a business runs a huge risk of being targeted for malware by attackers as their system would most likely be vulnerable. Security audits help to identify weak points in the system in a controlled environment without actually harming the system.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:18:47',111,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain why regular security audits are essential. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Regular security audits ensure a companies security is up-to-date and working well enough to protect against the latest security vulnerabilities, malware and attacks. Without security audits a business runs a huge risk of being targeted for malware by attackers as their system would most likely be vulnerable. Security audits help to identify weak points in the system in a controlled environment without actually harming the system.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly explained that security audits help identify weak points and vulnerabilities, which is excellent!</li><li>You also highlighted the importance of staying up-to-date against new threats, demonstrating a good understanding of continuous security.</li><li>To achieve full marks, consider also mentioning how audits help ensure a company complies with relevant laws and industry regulations.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, remember to include the aspect of ensuring compliance with legal and regulatory requirements as another key reason for regular security audits.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Regular security audits are essential because they help identify system vulnerabilities and weaknesses before they can be exploited by attackers. They also ensure that a company\'s security measures remain up-to-date against emerging threats and comply with relevant industry standards and legal regulations, protecting both data and reputation.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:18:49',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780304867739_vg2bb8xm8',1,'2026-06-01 09:18:47','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 09:25:14',1),(2084,65,179,1,7,'<p>A boolean operator is True or False and is useful in while loops</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:20:08',38,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>State what a Boolean operator does. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>A boolean operator is True or False and is useful in while loops</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that Boolean operators relate to True or False values, which is a good start!</li><li>To improve, consider what a Boolean operator *does* with these True or False values, rather than just what it *is*.</li><li>Think about how these operators are used to make comparisons or combine conditions.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Explain the action a Boolean operator performs, such as making a comparison or combining conditions, using keywords like AND, OR, or NOT.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A Boolean operator performs logical comparisons such as AND, OR, or NOT to combine or evaluate conditions, resulting in a True or False outcome.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:20:10',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780305128014_kb1anqa1k',1,'2026-06-01 09:20:08','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>A great example using the NOT boolean operator would be:</p><p><code>// Toggle switch</code></p><p><code>boolSwitch = NOT boolSwitch</code></p>','A','2026-06-01 09:22:56',1),(2085,66,14,1,7,'<p>a linear search is a method of searching a list (sorted or unsorted) where the algorithm checks each item in the list to see if it is a match, until either a match is found or the whole list is searched. A binary search is a method of searching a list (sorted) where it checks the middle item in an array and checks if it is higher, lower or a match, then discards half the list and repeates until a match is found.<br><br>A linear search is an easier to implminted and is best used for short unsorted data searching. A binary search is an efficient search algorithm that has to be used on sorted data. But is best used on large order lists of data.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:21:34',465,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the difference between a linear and binary search algorithm and when each should be used. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>a linear search is a method of searching a list (sorted or unsorted) where the algorithm checks each item in the list to see if it is a match, until either a match is found or the whole list is searched. A binary search is a method of searching a list (sorted) where it checks the middle item in an array and checks if it is higher, lower or a match, then discards half the list and repeates until a match is found.<br><br>A linear search is an easier to implminted and is best used for short unsorted data searching. A binary search is an efficient search algorithm that has to be used on sorted data. But is best used on large order lists of data.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly defined both linear and binary search algorithms, highlighting that linear search checks each item sequentially. Well done!</li><li>You clearly stated that binary search requires a sorted list and explained its divide-and-conquer approach, which is excellent.</li><li>You successfully identified appropriate use cases for both algorithms, noting that linear search is good for short, unsorted data and binary search for large, sorted lists.</li><li>To improve, consider adding a brief mention of the efficiency difference, perhaps by describing binary search as much faster for large datasets.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, briefly explain why binary search is considered more efficient (e.g., \"much faster for large datasets\").</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A linear search sequentially checks each item in a list until a match is found or the list ends. It works on both sorted and unsorted data. A binary search repeatedly divides a *sorted* list in half, checking the middle element and discarding the half that cannot contain the target, until the item is found or no elements remain. Linear search is simpler to implement and best for small or unsorted lists, while binary search is significantly faster (more efficient) for large, sorted datasets.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:21:37',NULL,'G','assessed','session_1780301430024_trdc84ig5',1,'2026-06-01 09:21:34','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','G','2026-06-01 09:23:31',1),(2086,67,230,1,12,'<p>An API is used as a middle man between the client and server on apps and websites. The common analogy is that the API is like a waiter between the chef (server) and customer (client), taking requests from the client passing them onto the server to be worked on and then returning what the server gives to the client. APIs are incredibly important across everything on the internet, without them there would be no server connection or a very insecure server connection.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:23:10',133,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe the concept of an API and its role in digital systems. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>An API is used as a middle man between the client and server on apps and websites. The common analogy is that the API is like a waiter between the chef (server) and customer (client), taking requests from the client passing them onto the server to be worked on and then returning what the server gives to the client. APIs are incredibly important across everything on the internet, without them there would be no server connection or a very insecure server connection.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve successfully explained that APIs act as a \'middleman\' facilitating communication, which is a great start.</li><li>The waiter analogy is very effective and clearly illustrates how APIs handle requests and responses between different systems.</li><li>To enhance your answer, consider adding more technical detail about *how* APIs enable communication, such as mentioning specific interface types.</li><li>You\'ve highlighted the importance of APIs; next time, briefly touch on their role in enabling different software applications to work together seamlessly.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Include a mention of specific API types like REST or GraphQL to show a deeper understanding of how these interfaces are implemented.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An API (Application Programming Interface) is a set of rules and protocols that allows different software applications to communicate with each other. It acts as an intermediary, enabling one system (the client) to request services or data from another system (the server) without needing to understand the server\'s internal workings. For example, a weather app uses an API to request weather data from a weather service\'s server. Common API architectural styles include REST and GraphQL.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:23:12',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780305546603_m8boaelz5',1,'2026-06-01 09:23:10','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>Examples like REST and GraphQL would have improved the answer. For this: 3</p>','A','2026-06-01 09:24:47',1),(2087,60,19,1,7,'<p>Firstly, you would need to import pandas (a python module), assuming that the file of student scores is a csv file, this module allows you to open and read data from a csv file. Then, you open the csv file using pd.read_csv(\'file\'). You would then ask for a students name, go through each row and find the grades of that specific student.</p><p>To test this, you could put different things in the student input, such as fake names, characters like @$%, and also numbers like 3.14, this would allow you to see if it works. Next, it would be smart to check every students name and check they all have correct data.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:25:39',213,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Design and justify a testing plan for a Python program that reads a file of student scores and outputs grades.</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Firstly, you would need to import pandas (a python module), assuming that the file of student scores is a csv file, this module allows you to open and read data from a csv file. Then, you open the csv file using pd.read_csv(\'file\'). You would then ask for a students name, go through each row and find the grades of that specific student.</p><p>To test this, you could put different things in the student input, such as fake names, characters like @$%, and also numbers like 3.14, this would allow you to see if it works. Next, it would be smart to check every students name and check they all have correct data.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve started to identify some invalid test data, which is a great first step! Consider how you would define the \"expected result\" for each of these invalid inputs.</li><li>Your response briefly touches on testing student names; expanding on other areas like file handling or how grade boundaries are checked would strengthen your plan.</li><li>To improve, think about different types of testing beyond just input validation, such as checking specific program functions or how different parts work together.</li><li>The mark scheme looks for a clear justification for each test; try to explain why each test is important for verifying the program\'s functionality.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, clearly define the different types of tests (e.g., unit, boundary) you would conduct and specify the expected outcome for each test case, explaining why that outcome is correct.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A comprehensive testing plan would include unit, boundary, and integration tests. Unit tests would verify individual functions, such as the `calculate_grade` function, using various score inputs (e.g., 0, 49, 50, 74, 75, 100, and values outside 0-100) to ensure grade boundaries are correctly applied. For each, the expected output (F, P, M, D) would be predefined to validate logic. Boundary tests would focus on the limits of input data, like testing with an empty score file or a file containing only one student record, to ensure robust file handling. Integration tests would then confirm that reading the file, processing scores, and outputting grades work seamlessly together. Invalid data, such as non-numeric scores in the file or incorrect file paths, would also be tested to ensure appropriate error handling. Advanced considerations might include automating these tests with a framework like Pytest to enable efficient regression testing whenever changes are made.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:25:43',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780304847437_b29u2be80',1,'2026-06-01 09:25:39','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','A','2026-06-01 09:26:09',1),(2088,67,243,1,12,'<p>The use of MFA (Multi-Factor Auth) helps to improve security by 100% ensuring the user is who they say they are. Method of MFA are usually email/phone/app codes, authentication apps and biometrics. MFA uses multiple of these at a time to stay secure as possible. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:25:58',120,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how multi-factor authentication improves system security. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The use of MFA (Multi-Factor Auth) helps to improve security by 100% ensuring the user is who they say they are. Method of MFA are usually email/phone/app codes, authentication apps and biometrics. MFA uses multiple of these at a time to stay secure as possible. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified several methods used in MFA, showing good foundational knowledge.</li><li>You mentioned using \"multiple of these at a time\" which is the core concept of MFA.</li><li>To achieve full marks, try to explain *why* combining these methods improves security, rather than just stating that it does.</li><li>Consider elaborating on what makes it more difficult for unauthorized users to gain access.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on *how* combining different authentication factors makes it harder for unauthorized individuals to access a system, even if one factor is compromised.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Multi-factor authentication improves system security by requiring users to provide two or more different types of verification methods to prove their identity. For example, a user might need to enter a password (something they know) and then a code from their phone (something they have), or scan their fingerprint (something they are). This layered approach significantly reduces the risk of unauthorized access, as compromising one factor is not enough to gain entry.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:26:00',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780305546603_m8boaelz5',1,'2026-06-01 09:25:58','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:26:00',NULL),(2089,58,107,1,7,'<p>Open-source software libraries are great because they are usually free and accessible to most people allowing many different people to interact and share their ideas. It also allows people to edit the source code allowing them to update and add new features to the software and share their ideas meaning that people can add the updates that they themselves want by themselves. However, this is not without risks as people with bad intentions can add malware to the updated software which then can infect unsuspecting people\'s device which then can harm the reputation of the owner of the open-source software and cause damage to many people</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:26:15',463,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of open-source software libraries. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Open-source software libraries are great because they are usually free and accessible to most people allowing many different people to interact and share their ideas. It also allows people to edit the source code allowing them to update and add new features to the software and share their ideas meaning that people can add the updates that they themselves want by themselves. However, this is not without risks as people with bad intentions can add malware to the updated software which then can infect unsuspecting people\'s device which then can harm the reputation of the owner of the open-source software and cause damage to many people</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You clearly identified that open-source software is often free and allows for community interaction and sharing, which are key advantages.</li><li>You correctly identified the ability to edit source code and add features as a benefit, showing good understanding of its flexibility.</li><li>You brought up a very important disadvantage regarding the risk of malicious code, demonstrating your awareness of security implications.</li><li>To improve, consider discussing the variable quality and potential lack of official support as further disadvantages.</li><li>For advantages, you could also mention the transparency of the code as a benefit.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate more on the specific disadvantages such as variable quality and the absence of dedicated official support, which can be crucial in professional settings.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Open-source software libraries offer several advantages, including free access, making them highly accessible. They benefit from strong community support, leading to rapid development and bug fixes. The transparency of the source code allows for scrutiny, enhancing security and trust. However, disadvantages include variable quality, as contributions are not always professionally audited, and a potential lack of official, dedicated support, which can be problematic in critical applications. There\'s also a risk of malicious code being introduced or a lack of consistent updates if community interest wanes.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:26:18',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780305401407_hdtzm1hti',1,'2026-06-01 09:26:15','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:26:18',NULL),(2090,66,191,1,7,'<p>data protection legislation affects software development through restricitng and legistlating what data, what types of data can be collected, procesed , stored and handled. it does provided a chalanges sometimes and should be considered during software development cycles, it affects the types of data and how securely each type should be handled. Specificaly it is important and legislated that personal sensitive data is handled carefuly and securely.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:28:00',344,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how data protection legislation affects software development. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>data protection legislation affects software development through restricitng and legistlating what data, what types of data can be collected, procesed , stored and handled. it does provided a chalanges sometimes and should be considered during software development cycles, it affects the types of data and how securely each type should be handled. Specificaly it is important and legislated that personal sensitive data is handled carefuly and securely.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully identified that legislation restricts what data can be collected, processed, stored, and handled, which addresses the lawful processing aspect.</li><li>You also mentioned the need for data to be handled carefully and securely, which touches upon secure storage.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, explicitly naming key legislation like GDPR would strengthen your answer.</li><li>Consider mentioning the importance of user consent as a specific requirement within data protection.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly name a relevant piece of data protection legislation, such as GDPR, to show deeper understanding.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Data protection legislation, such as GDPR, significantly affects software development by requiring that personal data is processed lawfully and fairly. Developers must design systems that ensure explicit user consent is obtained for data collection and processing. It also mandates secure storage and handling of all personal and sensitive data to prevent breaches and misuse.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:28:02',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301430024_trdc84ig5',1,'2026-06-01 09:28:00','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:28:02',NULL),(2091,62,20,1,7,'<p>The test plan should consist of: running the program to check if it crashes, checking the code for typos/syntax errors and a boundary test by inputting the minimum value you can input and the maximum value you can input to catch errors.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:28:45',712,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Design and justify a testing plan for a Python program that reads a file of student scores and outputs grades. (8 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The test plan should consist of: running the program to check if it crashes, checking the code for typos/syntax errors and a boundary test by inputting the minimum value you can input and the maximum value you can input to catch errors.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a good start by identifying the need for boundary testing. To strengthen your answer, consider what specific values you would use for these tests, like 0 or 100 for scores.</li><li>To fully meet the criteria, expand on the types of tests beyond just checking for crashes. Think about unit tests for individual functions and integration tests for how different parts of the program work together.</li><li>Think about expected results for your tests. For example, if a student scores 85, what grade should the program output?</li><li>You could also consider discussing invalid test data, such as non-numeric scores, and how your program should handle them.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on the specific test data you would use for each test, including expected outputs, and describe different test types like unit testing for functions and integration testing for file handling.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A comprehensive testing plan would include unit tests, boundary tests, and integration tests. Unit tests would verify individual functions, such as the grade calculation logic, using valid scores (e.g., 75 expecting a B, 42 expecting a D) and invalid scores (e.g., \"abc\", -10) to ensure error handling. Boundary tests would specifically target grade thresholds (e.g., 49, 50, 59, 60) to confirm accurate grade assignment at critical points. Integration tests would then confirm the entire workflow, from reading a valid student score file (e.g., \'scores.txt\' with various scores) and an invalid file (e.g., \'empty.txt\' or a file with corrupted data) to correctly outputting all grades. Automation could be used for regression testing, ensuring new code changes don\'t break existing functionality.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:28:48',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301649912_nz8qtk6n0',1,'2026-06-01 09:28:45','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:28:48',NULL),(2092,83,15,1,7,'<p>Data type functions allow data types (such as strings) to be converted into formats that are supported by an algorithm. They also ensure data types are consistent. This prevents errors, crashes, and strange behavior. Developers must ensure that data types are able to be converted successfully however. For example, \"wefoij\" cannot be converted to an integer as it contains non-numerical characters. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 09:56:20',2385,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss how data type conversion functions support robust code in Python. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p><p>Data type functions allow data types (such as strings) to be converted into formats that are supported by an algorithm. They also ensure data types are consistent. This prevents errors, crashes, and strange behavior. Developers must ensure that data types are able to be converted successfully however. For example, \"wefoij\" cannot be converted to an integer as it contains non-numerical characters. </p>\n</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that data type conversions help prevent errors and strange behaviour, which is a great start.</li><li>You gave a good example of an invalid conversion (\"wefoij\" to an integer), showing you understand the limitations.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, explicitly mention specific Python conversion functions like `int()`, `float()`, or `str()` to demonstrate practical knowledge.</li><li>Consider providing a concrete example of how converting user input (e.g., from `input()`) is essential for correct arithmetic operations.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Include specific Python data type conversion functions (e.g., `int()`, `float()`) and give an example of their use, particularly with user input.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Data type conversion functions like `int()`, `float()`, and `str()` are crucial for robust Python code by preventing `TypeError` exceptions. They ensure data is in the correct format for operations, such as converting user input from `input()` (which is always a string) into an integer or float before performing calculations. This ensures arithmetic behaves correctly and avoids crashes. While powerful, developers must ensure data is convertible, as attempting to convert non-numeric strings to integers will raise a `ValueError`. Conversion often complements input validation to build truly robust systems.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 09:56:23',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780301288301_jqll842pj',2,'2026-06-01 09:56:20','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 09:56:23',NULL),(2093,83,177,1,7,'<p>An array is an ordered list of items in a specified order. These items are accessed by index. Dictionaries (also known as hashmaps) are unordered and items are accessed via a key instead.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 12:27:15',52,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Identify one difference between an array and a dictionary. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>An array is an ordered list of items in a specified order. These items are accessed by index. Dictionaries (also known as hashmaps) are unordered and items are accessed via a key instead.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that arrays are accessed by an index and dictionaries by a key, which is excellent!</li><li>You clearly stated that arrays are ordered.</li><li>You also correctly noted that dictionaries are unordered.</li><li>Your response is very comprehensive and addresses the core differences well.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>While your answer is strong, you could concisely define what an \"index\" or \"key\" represents in each context to add even more clarity.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An array stores data in a sequential, ordered list, with each item accessed via a numerical index. A dictionary stores data as unordered key-value pairs, where each value is retrieved using its unique key.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-06-01 12:27:17',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780316768098_jni3w00xl',1,'2026-06-01 12:27:15','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 12:27:17',NULL),(2094,83,100,1,7,'<p>Validation is conducted to ensure data does not crash a program, cause errors, or unexplainable behavior. Verification ensures that data is up to date and correct.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 12:28:31',60,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss how validation and verification work together to improve data quality. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Validation is conducted to ensure data does not crash a program, cause errors, or unexplainable behavior. Verification ensures that data is up to date and correct.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a good start by defining validation in terms of preventing program issues. To strengthen this, consider explicitly mentioning that validation checks if data meets predefined criteria.</li><li>Your definition of verification correctly highlights ensuring data is correct. For a stronger answer, you could add an example of a verification method, like double-entry.</li><li>To fully address the question, try to discuss how both validation and verification are necessary and complement each other to ensure reliable data input and prevent errors further down the line.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, make sure to explain how validation and verification actively work together to improve data quality, rather than just defining them separately.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Validation checks if data meets predefined rules and formats (e.g., a number is entered where expected) to prevent system errors. Verification confirms the accuracy of the data entered, often by comparing it against a source or through double-entry. Together, they form a robust system: validation prevents incorrect data types or formats from entering, while verification ensures the data, once validated, is truly accurate. This combined approach significantly improves data quality by ensuring only accurate and appropriately formatted data is processed, preventing downstream issues.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 12:28:34',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780316768098_jni3w00xl',1,'2026-06-01 12:28:31','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 12:28:34',NULL),(2095,83,9,1,7,'<p>Computational thinking is the process of thinking about a complex problem logically - often using techniques such as abstraction, decomposition, and problem solving. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 12:36:24',49,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define ˜computational thinking (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Computational thinking is the process of thinking about a complex problem logically - often using techniques such as abstraction, decomposition, and problem solving. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that computational thinking is a logical approach to problem-solving, which is a great start.</li><li>You mentioned abstraction and decomposition, which are key techniques; try to include \"pattern recognition\" and \"algorithmic design\" next time for a more complete answer.</li><li>To achieve full marks, consider explaining how these techniques help break problems into manageable parts that can then be expressed as algorithms or coded.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Expand on how the identified techniques (abstraction, decomposition) help in expressing problems as algorithms for coding.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Computational thinking is a logical approach to problem-solving that breaks down complex problems into smaller, manageable parts using techniques like decomposition, pattern recognition, abstraction, and algorithmic design, so they can be expressed as algorithms and later coded.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 12:36:26',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780316768098_jni3w00xl',1,'2026-06-01 12:36:24','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 12:36:26',NULL),(2096,83,187,1,7,'<p>Conditional statements allow different sets of instructions to be carried out if a certain condition or set of conditions are met. These allow rigid programs to adapt based on different situations. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 12:38:51',68,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Describe how conditional statements are used to control program flow. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Conditional statements allow different sets of instructions to be carried out if a certain condition or set of conditions are met. These allow rigid programs to adapt based on different situations. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve made a great start by clearly explaining the purpose of conditional statements in making programs adaptable!</li><li>To strengthen your answer, try to mention the specific keywords used, like `if`, `elif`, and `else`.</li><li>Next time, consider adding a brief example or some pseudocode to illustrate how these statements work in practice.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Include specific examples of conditional statement keywords (e.g., if, elif, else) to show how decisions are made.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Conditional statements control program flow by allowing different blocks of code to execute based on whether specific conditions are met. They use constructs like `if`, `elif` (else if), and `else` to create decision points. For example, an `if` statement checks a condition and executes its block if true, while `else` provides an alternative path if the condition is false. This enables programs to respond dynamically to input or changing states, rather than following a rigid, linear path. </p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 12:38:53',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780316768098_jni3w00xl',1,'2026-06-01 12:38:51','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 12:38:53',NULL),(2097,83,96,1,7,'<p>Comments are written by the developer of a piece of code to explain what it does to other programmers. These comments can also be used to signal things between programmers. For example, there could be a comment showing where a bug is, or a piece of code that should not be modified. This reduces ambiguity, and ensures programmers work together and not against each other. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 12:41:27',132,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain why comments are used in Python programs. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Comments are written by the developer of a piece of code to explain what it does to other programmers. These comments can also be used to signal things between programmers. For example, there could be a comment showing where a bug is, or a piece of code that should not be modified. This reduces ambiguity, and ensures programmers work together and not against each other. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that comments are used to explain code to other programmers, which is great for readability.</li><li>You also highlighted how comments can reduce ambiguity and aid collaboration, linking to maintenance and debugging.</li><li>To achieve full marks, consider explicitly mentioning how comments help to understand the purpose of the code.</li><li>You could also strengthen your answer by stating that comments do not alter the program\'s behaviour.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state that comments describe the purpose of the code and don\'t affect how the program runs.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Comments are used in Python programs to describe the purpose of code and improve readability for developers. They help others understand, maintain, debug, or extend a program in the future without altering the program\'s execution.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 12:41:29',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780316768098_jni3w00xl',1,'2026-06-01 12:41:27','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 12:41:29',NULL),(2098,83,177,1,7,'<p>Items in an array are ordered, while items in a dictionary are unordered. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 12:42:12',27,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Identify one difference between an array and a dictionary. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Items in an array are ordered, while items in a dictionary are unordered. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that arrays are ordered. Great start!</li><li>You also correctly stated that dictionaries are unordered. This shows a good understanding of a key difference.</li><li>To achieve full marks, consider elaborating on *how* arrays are ordered and *how* dictionaries store their items.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, describe the specific method of ordering for arrays (e.g., by index) and how dictionaries store their data (e.g., key-value pairs).</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Arrays store items in a specific order accessed by an integer index, whereas dictionaries store items as unordered key-value pairs.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 12:42:13',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780316768098_jni3w00xl',2,'2026-06-01 12:42:12','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 12:42:13',NULL),(2099,83,108,1,7,'<p>Unit testing ensures that a specific module works correctly on its own. This prevents bugs in the actual module that may be difficult to fix once the module is compiled and shipped. Integration testing ensures that the scripts that tie the modules together are working correctly.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 12:57:31',892,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the role of testing methods such as unit and integration testing. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Unit testing ensures that a specific module works correctly on its own. This prevents bugs in the actual module that may be difficult to fix once the module is compiled and shipped. Integration testing ensures that the scripts that tie the modules together are working correctly.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly distinguished between unit and integration testing, which is a great start. Keep up the good work differentiating these key concepts!</li><li>You touched upon the benefit of unit testing in preventing bugs, which is an excellent point. To further strengthen your answer, consider expanding on how this translates to overall project benefits.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, remember to explicitly discuss the \'role\' of these methods, which includes their impact on project efficiency and cost. Think about the broader implications of finding issues early.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to expand on the benefits of each testing method, such as how they lead to earlier error detection and reduced maintenance costs.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Unit testing plays a crucial role in verifying that individual components or modules of a software system function correctly in isolation. This allows for the early detection and rectification of bugs within specific units, making them easier and cheaper to fix before they propagate. Integration testing, on the other hand, is essential for ensuring that these individual modules interact and work together as intended when combined. Its role is to uncover interface defects and interaction issues, reducing the risk of system-wide failures and significantly lowering overall maintenance costs in the long run by catching complex errors that unit testing alone would miss.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 12:57:33',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780316768098_jni3w00xl',1,'2026-06-01 12:57:31','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 12:57:33',NULL),(2100,83,195,1,7,'<p>Debugging ensures that bugs are found and fixed before the code is shipped to users. This reduces the chance of a user encountering a bug - increasing user experience. </p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 13:03:20',133,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate how debugging contributes to the creation of robust code. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Debugging ensures that bugs are found and fixed before the code is shipped to users. This reduces the chance of a user encountering a bug - increasing user experience. </p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that debugging finds and fixes errors, which is a great start towards explaining reliability. Can you expand on how this process directly makes code more dependable?</li><li>Consider discussing the specific techniques or tools used in debugging, such as testing or trace tables, to show how errors are systematically identified.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, you could also discuss the iterative nature of debugging and how it continuously refines the code.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>To deepen your evaluation, describe specific debugging techniques like using trace tables or integrated development environment (IDE) tools and explain how these methods lead to more thorough error correction.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Debugging is crucial for robust code as it systematically identifies and corrects errors, ensuring the software performs reliably and as intended. Through techniques like testing, using trace tables, and step-through debugging, developers can pinpoint logical errors, runtime issues, and unexpected behaviour. This iterative process of finding and fixing bugs not only improves the immediate functionality but also enhances the overall stability and maintainability of the codebase, significantly reducing the likelihood of failures or vulnerabilities when deployed to users.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 13:03:23',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780316768098_jni3w00xl',2,'2026-06-01 13:03:20','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 13:03:23',NULL),(2101,83,13,1,7,'<p><code>record = list[0]</code></p><p><code><br>for item in list:<br>    if record &lt; item:<br>        record = item</code></p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 13:13:34',145,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Using Python, write and explain an algorithm that finds the largest number in a list. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p><code>record = list[0]</code></p><p><code><br>for item in list:<br>    if record &lt; item:<br>        record = item</code></p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve successfully started by assuming the first element is the largest. Well done!</li><li>Your loop iterates through the list correctly, which is a great use of Python\'s iteration.</li><li>You\'ve accurately compared the current \'record\' with each \'item\' in the list.</li><li>Your code updates the \'record\' when a larger number is found, which is exactly what\'s needed.</li><li>To improve for next time, remember to include an explanation of your algorithm, referencing key steps like iteration and comparison.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Add comments or a short paragraph to explain how your code works, detailing the iteration and comparison steps.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>```python<br>def find_largest_number(numbers):<br>    if not numbers:  # Handle empty list case<br>        return None<br>    <br>    max_num = numbers[0]  # Initialize max_num with the first element<br>    for n in numbers:     # Iterate through each number in the list<br>        if n > max_num:   # Compare current number \'n\' with the stored maximum \'max_num\'<br>            max_num = n   # If \'n\' is larger, update max_num<br>    return max_num<br>```<br><br>This algorithm works by first assuming the initial largest number is the first element in the list (`max_num = numbers[0]`). It then uses a `for` loop to iterate through each subsequent number (`n`) in the list. Inside the loop, a comparison (`if n > max_num`) checks if the current number is greater than the currently stored `max_num`. If it is, `max_num` is updated to this new larger number. This process continues until all numbers have been checked, at which point `max_num` will hold the largest value found. An empty list check is included for robustness. Alternatively, Python\'s built-in `max()` function could achieve this more efficiently.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 13:13:38',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780316768098_jni3w00xl',1,'2026-06-01 13:13:34','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 13:13:38',NULL),(2102,86,79,1,7,'<p>Flowcharts are a way to better graphically express an algorithm. It\'s easier to interpret at a glance and better for those untrained. It can be less clear and accurate to the actual flow of logic than pseudocode which is much closer to actual code. However it can be much harder to interpret and you can\'t gleam the logic of the program at a glance, better for those trained, not for those untrained.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 13:23:15',634,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Compare the use of flowcharts and pseudocode when expressing algorithms. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Flowcharts are a way to better graphically express an algorithm. It\'s easier to interpret at a glance and better for those untrained. It can be less clear and accurate to the actual flow of logic than pseudocode which is much closer to actual code. However it can be much harder to interpret and you can\'t gleam the logic of the program at a glance, better for those trained, not for those untrained.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully identified that flowcharts are visual and easier for beginners, which is a great start.</li><li>You also correctly pointed out that pseudocode is closer to actual programming code.</li><li>To improve, consider expanding on the specific benefits of pseudocode for experienced programmers, such as its ability to show complex logic more accurately.</li><li>Think about how each method handles different aspects like data structures or iteration to demonstrate a deeper understanding.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly state how pseudocode offers better clarity and structure for complex algorithms compared to flowcharts.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Flowcharts are visual representations, making them excellent for beginners and for quickly understanding the overall flow of an algorithm. They are less detailed but good for high-level overviews. Pseudocode, on the other hand, is text-based and much closer to actual programming language, making it more suitable for developers to translate directly into code. It provides greater detail and precision for complex logic and data manipulation.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 13:23:17',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780316608269_0a07lveo8',1,'2026-06-01 13:23:15','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 13:23:17',NULL),(2103,58,75,1,7,'<p>Ignoring unnecessary things and only focusing on the important pieces</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 14:15:02',53,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>What is meant by abstraction in computational thinking?. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Ignoring unnecessary things and only focusing on the important pieces</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that abstraction involves ignoring unnecessary details and focusing on important information.</li><li>To achieve full marks, you could expand slightly on why we do this – to simplify complex problems.</li><li>Consider adding that it helps manage complexity.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on the purpose of abstraction, explaining that it helps to simplify complex problems by hiding detail.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Abstraction means removing unnecessary details to focus only on relevant information in order to simplify complex problems.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</di