h4><p>pattern recognition assists in solving problems as it provides similar processes to find answers, it finds these answers by solving previous questions.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that pattern recognition involves using previous questions to find answers. Well done!</li><li>To strengthen your answer, try to explicitly link this to finding \"similarities\" between problems.</li><li>Think about how recognising these similarities allows you to \"reuse prior solutions\" rather than just finding processes.</li><li>Consider adding a brief example to illustrate your point, like recognising common validation steps in programming.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Explicitly state that pattern recognition identifies similarities between problems, which then allows you to reuse solutions from those similar problems.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Pattern recognition assists problem-solving by identifying similarities between new problems and previously solved ones, enabling the reuse of established solutions. For example, recognising repeated input validation logic means a developer can apply the same solution again.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 14:42:20',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780323124339_vyny1zx1v',2,'2026-06-01 14:42:18','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 14:42:20',NULL),(2106,58,15,1,7,'<p>data type conversion functions support robust code by allowing data to be converted to a different type at any time and this is helpful for data validation and to prevent runtime errors by taking in an input and checking whether it is a type of data that is needed before converting it into that data type</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 14:45:38',226,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Discuss how data type conversion functions support robust code in Python. (5 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>data type conversion functions support robust code by allowing data to be converted to a different type at any time and this is helpful for data validation and to prevent runtime errors by taking in an input and checking whether it is a type of data that is needed before converting it into that data type</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that type conversion helps prevent runtime errors and is useful for validation, which is a great start.</li><li>To strengthen your answer, try to mention specific Python conversion functions like `int()`, `float()`, or `str()`.</li><li>Consider adding a small, practical example, such as converting user input from `input()` before performing calculations.</li><li>You could also briefly discuss how validation complements conversion to ensure robustness.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Include specific examples of data type conversion functions (e.g., `int()`, `str()`) and illustrate their use, perhaps with user input.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Data type conversion functions like `int()`, `float()`, `str()`, and `bool()` are crucial for robust Python code by preventing type errors that can cause runtime crashes. For instance, user input from `input()` is always a string; converting it to an `int()` or `float()` allows for correct mathematical operations. This ensures calculations behave as expected, for example, `int(\"5\") + 3` works, whereas `\"5\" + 3` would raise a TypeError. While conversion is vital, combining it with input validation further enhances robustness by checking if the conversion is even possible or if the data is within acceptable ranges before attempting the conversion, thereby preventing potential `ValueError` exceptions.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 14:45:41',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780323104245_m9r8p2lh5',1,'2026-06-01 14:45:38','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 14:45:41',NULL),(2107,64,77,1,7,'<p>the top down approach in solving problems by minimising complex problems into more simpler and easier to understand problems. This makes it easier for a team to work together as a top down approach helps staff understand complex problems.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 14:49:38',269,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain how the top-down approach assists in solving software problems. (2 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>the top down approach in solving problems by minimising complex problems into more simpler and easier to understand problems. This makes it easier for a team to work together as a top down approach helps staff understand complex problems.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that the top-down approach simplifies complex problems, which is a great start.</li><li>To gain full marks, remember to explain how this simplification happens, for example, by breaking down the overall system.</li><li>Think about the specific actions taken in a top-down approach, like designing the main functions first.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, specifically mention that the process involves breaking the overall system into smaller, manageable sub-systems.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>The top-down approach breaks a complex software problem into smaller, more manageable sub-systems. This allows developers to focus on the overall structure and main functions first, refining details in each sub-system later.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 14:49:40',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780323124339_vyny1zx1v',1,'2026-06-01 14:49:38','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 14:49:40',NULL),(2108,64,74,1,7,'<p>an algorithm is a step by step set of instructions to solve a problem</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 19:52:53',19,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Define algorithm. (1 Mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>an algorithm is a step by step set of instructions to solve a problem</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that an algorithm is a step-by-step set of instructions. Well done!</li><li>You also rightly included that algorithms are used to solve a problem. Great work on capturing these core elements!</li><li>To achieve a stronger response, consider adding that algorithms are also used to perform computations.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, try to include that algorithms can also be used to perform a computation, not just solve a problem.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>An algorithm is a precise, step-by-step sequence of instructions used to solve a problem or perform a computation.</p>RAG RATING:\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"G\">🟢 Green — meets or exceeds the mark scheme criteria</div>',1,'2026-06-01 19:52:54',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780343565877_tmn6xjr9r',2,'2026-06-01 19:52:53','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 19:52:54',NULL),(2109,64,199,1,7,'<p>Software testing methods help increase robust code as it finds bugs and errors before the software is released to the public. Unit testing divides the code into smaller parts, and then is tested within the smaller scope, this makes the overall code easier to test as it\'s faster to find errors or bugs in a small amount of code rather than a large amount of code. Integration testing is used after unit testing and it checks that different modules can work together seamlessly, rather than independently, which helps find errors in data transfer within modules. System testing is used at the end to make sure the whole system is all working with no errors or bugs, making the code ready for user testing. User testing is the process of end users testing the code to make sure it is working. This provides a different view of the system, which the developers might not see. Overall, each part of testing is equally as important as they all benefit the system to make sure that there arn\'t any bugs or errors.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 20:05:30',390,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Analyse how software testing methods ensure solution reliability. (8 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>Software testing methods help increase robust code as it finds bugs and errors before the software is released to the public. Unit testing divides the code into smaller parts, and then is tested within the smaller scope, this makes the overall code easier to test as it\'s faster to find errors or bugs in a small amount of code rather than a large amount of code. Integration testing is used after unit testing and it checks that different modules can work together seamlessly, rather than independently, which helps find errors in data transfer within modules. System testing is used at the end to make sure the whole system is all working with no errors or bugs, making the code ready for user testing. User testing is the process of end users testing the code to make sure it is working. This provides a different view of the system, which the developers might not see. Overall, each part of testing is equally as important as they all benefit the system to make sure that there arn\'t any bugs or errors.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully discussed unit, integration, and system testing methods, which is a great start!</li><li>You clearly explained the purpose of each testing type and how they contribute to finding errors.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, remember to also discuss the benefits and drawbacks of each testing method.</li><li>Consider including how automation or documentation plays a role in ensuring reliability for a more comprehensive answer.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>For each testing method you discussed, briefly explain one benefit and one drawback to show a deeper understanding.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Software testing methods systematically check code to ensure solution reliability by identifying and rectifying defects. Unit testing isolates individual components, verifying their functionality in isolation. A benefit is early bug detection, making fixes cheaper, but a drawback is missing integration issues. Integration testing verifies how modules interact, ensuring data flows correctly between them. This is good for finding interface errors but can be complex with many modules. System testing assesses the complete, integrated software against requirements, ensuring it meets functional and non-functional specifications. This provides a holistic view but is time-consuming. User acceptance testing (UAT) involves end-users to validate the system against business needs, offering real-world feedback. The importance of test automation, especially for unit and integration tests, lies in its ability to run tests quickly and repeatedly, catching regressions efficiently. Comprehensive documentation of test plans, cases, and results is crucial for tracking progress, maintaining quality, and proving the software meets reliability standards.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 20:05:35',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780343565877_tmn6xjr9r',1,'2026-06-01 20:05:30','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 20:05:35',NULL),(2110,64,99,1,7,'<p>count controlled loops and condition controlled loops are divided by the way that the condition is met. For count controlled, the process stops either until the condition is met or the count runs out, for example a for loop. Whereas condition based loops processes end only until the condition is met, for example a while loop.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 20:09:17',118,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Compare count-controlled and condition-controlled loops. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>count controlled loops and condition controlled loops are divided by the way that the condition is met. For count controlled, the process stops either until the condition is met or the count runs out, for example a for loop. Whereas condition based loops processes end only until the condition is met, for example a while loop.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that count-controlled loops and condition-controlled loops differ in how their conditions are met, which is a great start!</li><li>You provided good examples of each type of loop (for and while), demonstrating your understanding of their practical application.</li><li>To achieve higher marks, clearly state that count-controlled loops run a *fixed* number of times, which is a key distinguishing feature.</li><li>Consider adding a point about how condition-controlled loops continue *until* a specific condition becomes false (or true), rather than just \"until the condition is met\".</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state that count-controlled loops execute for a predetermined, fixed number of iterations.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Count-controlled loops (e.g., `for` loops) execute a fixed number of times, determined at the start of the loop, typically using a counter. Condition-controlled loops (e.g., `while` loops) repeat an action until a specified condition becomes false. While count-controlled loops are safer as they are guaranteed to terminate, condition-controlled loops offer more flexibility for scenarios where the exact number of iterations is unknown but a clear stopping condition exists.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 20:09:20',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780343565877_tmn6xjr9r',1,'2026-06-01 20:09:17','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 20:09:20',NULL),(2111,62,14,1,7,'<p>A linear search is a search that checks a data set by checking the values one by one until the value that is being searched for is found, this is more effcient for shorter lists as it is more thorough and takes longer than a binary search. A binary search splits the list into multiple sub lists and repeats that process until the value is found.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 20:17:43',858,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Explain the difference between a linear and binary search algorithm and when each should be used. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>A linear search is a search that checks a data set by checking the values one by one until the value that is being searched for is found, this is more effcient for shorter lists as it is more thorough and takes longer than a binary search. A binary search splits the list into multiple sub lists and repeats that process until the value is found.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly explained that a linear search checks each element one by one. To improve, clearly state that a binary search works by repeatedly halving the list.</li><li>You mentioned that binary search splits the list, which is a great start. Remember to also explain that binary search specifically requires the list to be sorted to work effectively.</li><li>You touched on efficiency for shorter lists with linear search; try to expand on the efficiency of binary search (e.g., how it\'s much faster for larger lists) and when each is best used in different scenarios.</li><li>Consider adding that binary search typically makes fewer comparisons and is much quicker for large datasets once the data is sorted.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, explicitly state that a binary search requires the data to be sorted and explain that it works by repeatedly dividing the list in half at each step.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>A linear search checks each item in a list sequentially until the target is found. It\'s suitable for small or unsorted lists because it doesn\'t require any prior organisation. A binary search repeatedly divides a *sorted* list in half, eliminating half the remaining elements at each step until the target is located. Binary search is significantly faster (more efficient) for large, sorted datasets, but it cannot be used on unsorted data.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 20:17:46',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780347753795_jjp5w72cq',1,'2026-06-01 20:17:43','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 20:17:46',NULL),(2112,64,108,1,7,'<p>The roles of unit testing and integration testing are very important for software test cycles as they reduce the amount of errors and bugs before publishing software to the public. Unit testing is when a large amount of code is seperated into individual modules that can be tested on and ran for errors etc. This is easier and more efficient than just testing the whole program at once, as you dont have to go through all of the code to find errors, also it\'s easier to find errors within smaller chunks of code. Integration testing is the flow of testing the whole code in sync with a relational dataset, making sure that flow of data is correct and accurate for users. Overall, both methods of testing are crucial for an end-user ready program, as they would have been checked for errors from actual code, as well as data accuracy.</p>',NULL,'2026-06-01 21:56:38',266,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Evaluate the role of testing methods such as unit and integration testing. (6 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>The roles of unit testing and integration testing are very important for software test cycles as they reduce the amount of errors and bugs before publishing software to the public. Unit testing is when a large amount of code is seperated into individual modules that can be tested on and ran for errors etc. This is easier and more efficient than just testing the whole program at once, as you dont have to go through all of the code to find errors, also it\'s easier to find errors within smaller chunks of code. Integration testing is the flow of testing the whole code in sync with a relational dataset, making sure that flow of data is correct and accurate for users. Overall, both methods of testing are crucial for an end-user ready program, as they would have been checked for errors from actual code, as well as data accuracy.</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully differentiate between unit and integration testing, explaining what each method focuses on. To strengthen your answer, ensure your definition of integration testing clearly focuses on how components work together, rather than just the whole code with a dataset.</li><li>You effectively note that these methods reduce errors and bugs. To achieve higher marks, explicitly link early error detection to its impact on maintenance costs or overall project efficiency.</li><li>Your response correctly identifies the importance of both testing methods for an end-user ready program. Try to elaborate on the benefits of these methods in terms of cost or time savings in a real-world software development context.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Clearly state how integration testing specifically verifies that individual components function correctly when combined, rather than just testing the whole code with a dataset.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>Unit testing focuses on verifying individual components or modules of software in isolation. This allows for early detection and rectification of errors within specific units, making bugs easier to locate and fix. Integration testing then evaluates how these individual modules interact and function together as a group. Its role is to uncover interface defects and ensure that data flows correctly between connected components. Both methods are crucial as they lead to earlier detection of defects, which significantly reduces the cost and effort of maintenance later in the software development lifecycle, ultimately contributing to a more robust and reliable final product.</p>\n<div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-01 21:56:41',NULL,'A','assessed','session_1780346995735_gw662duzi',1,'2026-06-01 21:56:38','2026-06-03 17:25:10',NULL,'A','2026-06-01 21:56:41',NULL),(2113,62,78,1,7,'<p>…</p>',NULL,'2026-06-02 08:07:10',18,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Write a short Python function that checks if a number is even or odd and explain how it works. (4 Marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>…</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You successfully wrote a Python function to check if a number is even or odd, which is great!</li><li>To improve your explanation, remember to describe how the modulus operator works in detail.</li><li>Consider adding a clear explanation of how the `if/else` statement helps in selecting the correct output.</li><li>Think about explaining what the function `returns` and why that\'s important.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Next time, elaborate on how the `%` (modulus) operator specifically determines even or odd numbers by finding the remainder of a division.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>```python\ndef check_even_odd(number):\n    if number % 2 == 0:\n        return \"Even\"\n    else:\n        return \"Odd\"\n```<br>This function works by using the modulus operator (`%`) which gives the remainder of a division. If a number divided by 2 has a remainder of 0 (`number % 2 == 0`), it means the number is even. Otherwise, if there is any remainder (e.g., 1), the number is odd. The `if/else` statement then selects and `returns` the appropriate string (\"Even\" or \"Odd\") based on this condition.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"A\">🟡 Amber — partially meets the criteria but key points are missing</div>',1,'2026-06-02 08:07:13',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1780387595687_q9b8780n0',1,'2026-06-02 08:07:10','2026-06-03 17:13:07','<p>You should have had a go...</p><p>The key is the mod function </p><p><code>if (x % 2==0):</code></p><p><code>	print(\"X is even\")</code></p><p></p>','R','2026-06-02 10:00:01',1),(2114,1,1277,8,35,'<p>(2xy^5)^4</p>',NULL,'2026-06-02 10:01:23',68,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Simplify (2x³y²)⁴ (2 marks)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>(2xy^5)^4</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You\'ve correctly identified that the entire expression needs to be raised to the power of 4, which is a great start!</li><li>Remember to apply the power of 4 to the coefficient (2) as well as the variables.</li><li>When raising a power to another power, you multiply the exponents, rather than adding them.</li><li>Take another look at how the powers of x and y should be treated when the whole term is raised to the power of 4.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Ensure you apply the outer power to every term inside the bracket, including the numerical coefficient, and multiply the existing powers by the outer power.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>16x¹²y⁸</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings in the response</div>',1,'2026-06-02 10:01:26',NULL,'R','assessed','session_1780394189602_2f1flfp13',1,'2026-06-02 10:01:23','2026-06-03 17:13:07','','R','2026-06-02 10:07:38',1),(2115,1,1353,8,35,'<p>1 is a prime and it is odd</p>',NULL,'2026-06-02 10:03:28',37,'<h4>The Question</h4><p>Give a counter-example to disprove: \'all prime numbers are odd.\' (1 mark)</p><h4>Your Response</h4><p>1 is a prime and it is odd</p><h4>Feedback</h4><ul><li>You correctly identified that you needed to provide a counter-example to the statement.</li><li>However, the number 1 is not considered a prime number; prime numbers have exactly two distinct positive divisors (1 and themselves).</li><li>The number 1 only has one positive divisor, which is 1.</li><li>To effectively disprove the statement, your counter-example needs to be an even number that is also prime.</li></ul><h4>One Thing to Improve</h4><p>Review the definition of a prime number carefully to ensure your counter-example fits all criteria.</p><h4>Model Answer</h4><p>2 is a prime number and it is even.</p><div class=\"ai-rag-suggestion\" data-rating=\"R\">🔴 Red — significant gaps or misunderstandings 